(48, 'Shinya Kougami', '狡噛慎也', '主角', 'Tomokazu Seki', 'Shinya Kougami is an enforcement officer who is tasked with managing crime. Shinya has a high criminal mentality, but because of his skills as a detective, he was released under the condition that he becomes an Enforcer for the Public Safety Bureau, Unit 1. Despite his natural grudge towards [Makishima](https://anilist.co/character/69725/Makishima-Shougo), they are actually somewhat alike, as shown in Shinya''s ability to foresee Makishima''s actions.', '/uploads/images/c_68315.jpg'),
(48, 'Akane Tsunemori', '常守朱', '主角', 'Kana Hanazawa', 'The main female protagonist and the newly assigned Inspector of Unit 1. Considered a model citizen due to her ever calm demeanor and for passing the exams with the highest score for employment on several public sectors and private corporations. She decided to join the police due to being the only place where no one obtained a score as high as hers, thus she believes to be able to do something there that no one else can. She has a unique quirk in which it''s hard to cloud her Pyscho-Pass Hues, making her a perfect fit for the job as Inspector.', '/uploads/images/c_68583.jpg'),
(48, 'Shuusei Kagari', '縢秀星', '配角', 'Akira Ishida', 'Shuusei is the jokester of the group and likes to make fun of people on a regular basis. He enjoys portable video games and spends most of his free time playing them. However, he is more serious when he''s on the job. He hates people who take the freedom they have for granted, because of the fact that he''s been excluded from society since he was five years old. ~!Later on in the series, he is killed by the Chief because he saw the true form of Sibyl System, and has been reported missing ever since.!~', '/uploads/images/c_69055.jpg'),
(48, 'Nobuchika Ginoza', '宜野座伸元', '配角', 'Kenji Nojima', 'A veteran Inspector working with Akane. He coordinates all the Enforcers in Unit 1. An old friend of Shinya''s, his hatred for those with high Crime Coefficients and his zeal to oust them from society came from the inability to stop his former partner from becoming a latent criminal. Although he still has a certain degree of trust with Shinya, he holds a dislike for Shinya''s Enforcer partner, Masaoka, for unknown reasons. Ginoza constantly tells Akane to draw a line between herself and the Enforcers she works with. ~!He is the son of Masaoka Tomomi. After the Makishima incident, his Psycho-Pass reaches 140 and he becomes an Enforcer just like his father.!~', '/uploads/images/c_69057.jpg'),
(48, 'Yayoi Kunizuka', '六合塚弥生', '配角', 'Shizuka Itou', 'The only female Enforcer of Unit One. She stays calm and collected in the face of even the most brutal crimes. She and Shion are lovers.', '/uploads/images/c_69059.jpg'),
(48, 'Tomomi Masaoka', '征陸智己', '配角', 'Kinryuu Arimoto', 'He is an enforcer under Ginoza Nobuchika and Tsunemori Akane. ~!It is later revealed that he is the latent criminal father of Ginoza. Given a Dominator and being told by Sibyl who to shoot, he lost faith in his role as a detective, and his Psycho-pass grew increasingly cloudier until he was eventually detained as a latent criminal, before becoming an Enforcer. That made him hated by his son. Later on in the series, when he''s trying to throw away the bomb that was thrown to Ginoza by Makishima, he died because the bomb exploded in his hands.!~', '/uploads/images/c_69061.jpg'),
(48, 'Shion Karanomori', '唐之杜志恩', '配角', 'Miyuki Sawashiro', '__Height:__ 168 cm (5''6") An analyst in the Public Safety Bureau''s General Analysis Division and a latent criminal as well. She provides backup to the Enforcers and Inspectors in their investigation by analyzing the data and evidence sent by them. She is in a relationship with [Yayoi Kunizuka](https://anilist.co/character/69059/Kunizuka-Yayoi) who is one of the enforcers of Unit 1. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_69063.jpg'),
(48, 'Shougo Makishima', '槙島聖護', '主角', 'Takahiro Sakurai', 'A humanist on the dark side who is hopelessly in love with cruelty, savagery, and all the worst aspects of human nature. A born evangelist, he possesses both uncommon charisma and a true gift for narrative. Makishima has quite a unique personality. He likes books a lot, as shown in his tendency to quote from famous literature. ~!Makishima was the mastermind behind the many cases the Public Safety Bureau are investigating, including the one that led [Shinya Kogami](https://anilist.co/character/68315/Kougami-Shinya) to become demoted to Enforcer. Despite his murderous intent, his hue has always been pure white due to a unique genetics called criminally asymptomatic..!~ ~!According to Kogami, Makishima''s pure Psycho-Pass is the result of having suffered hardships in his early life and that being "unrecognized" by Sibyl left Makishima feeling invisible, which may have triggered his single-minded goal of taking down the Sibyl System. Makishima, on the other hand, believes that isolation made him stronger.!~', '/uploads/images/c_69725.jpg'),
(48, 'Yuki Funahara', '船原ゆき', '配角', 'Kotori Koiwai', 'Tsunemori Akane''s friend. ~!She later dies at the hands of Makishima.!~', '/uploads/images/c_73341.jpg'),
(48, 'Kaori Minase', '水無瀬佳織', '配角', 'Kozue Harashima', 'Akane''s friend. She works as a system engineer.', '/uploads/images/c_73343.jpg'),
(48, 'Gu-Seong Choi', 'チェ・グソン', '配角', 'Yasunori Masutani', 'Works for Makishima Shougo, and is also his right hand man. He is an expert hacker, as he is able to breach through the security system of Sibyl''s core and even witness its true form. He is Korean.', '/uploads/images/c_73345.jpg'),
(48, 'Masatake Midou', '御堂将剛', '配角', 'Daichuu Mizushima', '~!To take over their avatars, he killed Sugawara Shouko, Tokitou Yuuichi, and Hayama Kimihiko.!~', '/uploads/images/c_73347.jpg'),
(48, 'Shouko Sugawara', '菅原昭子', '配角', 'Ayana Taketatsu', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_73349.jpg'),
(48, 'Nobuo Ookura', '大倉信夫', '配角', 'Shouto Kashii', 'The first latent criminal to be shown.', '/uploads/images/c_73351.jpg'),
(48, 'Chika Shimazu', '島津千香', '配角', 'Sachiko Kojima', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_73353.jpg'),
(48, 'Yuuji Kanehara', '金原祐治', '配角', 'Satoshi Tsuruoka', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_73355.jpg'),
(48, 'Kuraudo Gouda', '郷田蔵人', '配角', 'Yoshiyuki Kaneko', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_73357.jpg'),
(48, 'Kimihiko Hayama', '葉山公彦', '配角', 'Takehito Koyasu', 'He is single and unemployed.', '/uploads/images/c_73727.jpg'),
(48, 'Yuuichi Tokitou', '時任雄一', '配角', 'Mutsumi Tamura', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_73729.jpg'),
(48, 'Rikako Ouryou', '王陵璃華子', '配角', 'Maaya Sakamoto', 'She was introduced in episode 6 as a pretty, intelligent, and highly admired student of Oso Girl''s Academy who is the head of the school''s art club. Her talent for painting is impeccable. ~!However, behind her sweet facade is a psychopath whose obsession is killing her fellow schoolmates and using their bodies to construct grotesque works of art and have them displayed in the middle of the city underneath a Holographic Illumination. It is unclear as to what is her relationship with Makishima is, but it is hinted that he is helping her carry out her psychopathic obsession. !~ Her father is confined in a hospital in a vegetative state. (Source: Otaku-streamers forum)', '/uploads/images/c_74005.jpg'),
(48, 'Yoshika Ookubo', '大久保葦歌', '配角', 'Ai Kayano', 'A student from Oso Girl''s Academy ~!who has become one of Makishima and Oryo Rikako''s victim.!~', '/uploads/images/c_74007.jpg'),
(48, 'Kagami Kawarazaki', '川原崎加賀美', '配角', 'Aiko Kusumi', 'One of Ouryou Rikako''s victims.', '/uploads/images/c_74009.jpg'),
(48, 'Mika Shimotsuki', '霜月美佳', '配角', 'Ayane Sakura', 'She is a student of Oso Girl''s Academy who seems to be aware of what''s going on around campus. She is [Kagami](https://anilist.co/character/74009/)''s friend and classmate. ~!She becomes an inspector, working with Akane Tsunemori as the new junior inspector, with a first day on the job mirroring Tsunemori''s own first day.!~', '/uploads/images/c_74011.jpg'),
(48, 'Toyohisa Senguuji', '泉宮寺豊久', '配角', 'Katsumi Chou', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_74405.jpg'),
(48, 'Satsuki Kuzuhara', '葛原皐月', '配角', '', 'One of Ouryou Rikako''s victims.', '/uploads/images/c_74425.jpg'),
(48, 'Rouichi Ouryou', '王陵牢一', '配角', '', 'Ouryou Rikako''s father. He was previously an artist.', '/uploads/images/c_74427.jpg'),
(48, 'Mitsuru Sasayama', '佐々山光留', '配角', 'Shintarou Asanuma', 'Kougami Shinya''s past partner and friend. He was murdered during an operation. Since then, Shinya has been investigating the case.', '/uploads/images/c_74541.jpg'),
(48, 'Kouichi Ashikaga', '足利紘一', '配角', 'Kenta Miyake', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_74726.jpg'),
(48, 'Kouzaburou Touma', '藤間幸三郎', '配角', '', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_74952.jpg'),
(48, 'Jouji Saiga', '雑賀譲二', '配角', 'Kazuhiro Yamaji', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_75206.png'),
(48, 'Rina Takizaki', '滝崎リナ', '配角', 'Akeno Watanabe', 'An unauthorized artist who Yayoi met when playing on a stage. ~!In Yayois background episode it is shown that the two shared a deep relationship and when Yayoi was locked up as a latent criminal, Rina started an antisocial movement that vandalized street scanners. When Yayoi confronted Rina when she was joining the inspectors investigating the vandalism, Rina walks away into the tunnels with the rest of the gang. It is unclear if she is caught.!~', '/uploads/images/c_77051.png'),
(48, 'Joushuu Kasei', '禾生壌宗', '配角', 'Yoshiko Sakakibara', 'The chief of the Public Safety Bureau. She often speaks with Ginoza on classified matters and holds the utmost trust in him. She wishes for Shogo Makishima to be arrested rather than killed. ~!In Episode 13, she shares with Ginoza classified files about the culprit of the Specimen Case, Touma Kouzoburou. She explains that he was able to get away with it due to him having a condition known as being "criminally asymptotic", meaning that he could get scanned and have no problems found with him. It is believed that Shogo Makishima possesses the same condition due to his immunity to the Dominator. In Episode 16, after Shuusei and Gu-Song discover the true form of the Sybil System she appears to kill Gu-Song with the "Lethal Elimiinator". However, she is revealed to be a cyborg and then turns and shoots Shuusei before fading out, leaving thier fates unknown. She is actually a robotic body that the members of the Sibyl System use to run the MWPSB. The body is nothing but a shell, used by the members to do their whims. It is only operational when one of their brains occupies her body.!~', '/uploads/images/c_77753.png'),
(48, 'Hiroko Fujii', '藤井博子', '配角', 'Hiro Nakajima', 'Fuji is a fashionable woman with long, light brown hair and brown eyes. She wears a long red coat with a light colored scarf. She gets involved in the Helmet Riots.', '/uploads/images/c_77755.jpg'),
(48, 'Junmei Itou', '伊藤純銘', '配角', 'Yuuichi Ishigami', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_77757.png'),
(48, 'Risa Aoyanagi', '青柳璃彩', '配角', 'Masumi Asano', '~!Possibly a container or vessel for the Sibyl System, as hinted on various episodes and scenes.!~', '/uploads/images/c_80345.jpg'),
(48, 'Nobuaki Kudama', '管卷宣昭', '配角', 'Tesshou Genda', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_80347.jpg'),
(48, 'Teppei Sugou', '須郷徹平', '配角', 'Hiroki Touchi', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_147046.png'),
(48, 'Komissa-chan', 'コミッサちゃん', '配角', 'Natsumi Takamori', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_359600.png'),
(49, 'Mashiro Shiina', '椎名ましろ', '主角', 'Ai Kayano', '**Height:** 162 cm Mashiro is the female protagonist of the story. She is the resident of room 202. She is a world-famous artist who transferred into Suiko as a second-year to learn how to draw manga. Although her artwork is widely admired by the world, in spite of her young age, she knows nothing other than drawing and has an extreme lack of common sense and living ability. Due to this, [Sorata](https://anilist.co/character/64169/Kanda-Sorata) is forced to handle Mashiro''s living chores, to the point that he even has to pick out underwear for her, or she will go out without them. ~!In the third novel, Mashiro starts to grow feelings for Sorata, and she even claims that she cannot live without him. In the eighth novel Sorata confesses his feelings for her and in the next novel, they are officially a couple.!~ Given her only academic strong point is art, she does very poorly in other subjects. Utilizing her photographic memory allows her to succeed in these subjects. ~!It is heavily implied in the last volume of the novel that Mashiro and Sorata had a child.!~', '/uploads/images/c_61371.jpg'),
(49, 'Misaki Kamiigusa', '上井草美咲', '主角', 'Natsumi Takamori', '**Height:** 156 cm Misaki is the resident of room 201. Misaki is a third-year-student of Suiko who later attends Suimei University of the Arts. She is very outgoing and optimistic. [Sorata](https://anilist.co/character/64169/Kanda-Sorata) often refers to her as an "alien". She has very good grades and is very good at drawing, but the school decided to send her to Sakurasou Dormitory because she pays too much attention on drawing anime and manga. She is very good at making animation and can handle most work in making one without help from others. She has already sold an animation to a famous publishing company and made enough of a fortune for the rest of her life. ~!She has feelings for [Jin](https://anilist.co/character/64171/Mitaka-Jin), and acts very open to express her feelings, but Jin turns a blind eye to this and dates many other girls, which makes her very depressed.!~ ~!She and Jin finally become a couple during the fifth novel. In sixth novel, she registers their marriage without asking Jin, making them officially husband and wife; her new name is Misaki Mitaka. She moves next to the Sakurasou Dormitory after her graduation into a house which she designed and built herself and has a recording studio in the basement.!~', '/uploads/images/c_64165.png'),
(49, 'Nanami Aoyama', '青山七海', '主角', 'Mari Nakatsu', '__Height:__ 158 cm Nanami is [Sorata](https://anilist.co/character/64169)''s classmate. Although she is harsh to Sorata, she actually has a crush on him, and everyone aside from Sorata has noticed this. She escaped from her home to become a voice actress and has to live on her own.', '/uploads/images/c_64167.png'),
(49, 'Sorata Kanda', '神田空太', '主角', 'Yoshitsugu Matsuoka', '**Height:** 168 cm Sorata is the male protagonist of the story. He is a second-year student of Suiko, who lives in room 101 of Sakurasou Dormitory. He was kicked out of the standard school dorm after he chose not to throw away a stray cat he picked up. As many of the Sakurasou Dormitory residents have outstanding grades and art skills, he often feels plain and normal among them. He is chosen by Chihiro to take care of Mashiro''s daily life, although he resists at first, but he ends up getting used to it.', '/uploads/images/c_64169.png'),
(49, 'Jin Mitaka', '三鷹 仁', '主角', 'Takahiro Sakurai', '__Height:__ 178 cm Jin is the resident of room 103. Jin is a third-year student of Suiko. He is Misaki''s childhood friend and a playboy. He has dated several girls, including Misaki''s elder sister, but in the end he breaks up with all of them. ~!Jin has feelings for Misaki, but he feels he is not good enough to match her, so he ended up becoming a playboy. He finally becomes a couple with Misaki during the fifth novel. He wants to become a playwright, and later attends a university in Osaka to achieve his goal. To pacify Misaki, he gives her a marriage registration form with his signature as a warranty, but Misaki ends up turning it in after his departure on the same day, which makes them officially married.!~', '/uploads/images/c_64171.png'),
(49, 'Ryuunosuke Akasaka', '赤坂龍之介', '主角', 'Yui Horie', '__Height:__ 165 cm Ryuunosuke is the resident of room 102. Ryuunosuke is a second-year student of Suiko. He is a hikikomori who rarely leaves his room, and usually communicates with others with cellphone message or e-mails. To reduce the need to communicate with others, he has written the "Maid" program. He is an expert of computer programming, and contributes lots of useful advice and information to Sorata for the latter''s computer game. According to Ryuunosuke, his ultimate goal is to make Maid become a real human. He likes tomatoes ~!He has gynophobia, and will even pass out when girls touch him, which becomes worse after Rita falls in love with him and kisses him on the cheek.!~', '/uploads/images/c_64173.jpg'),
(49, 'Chihiro Sengoku', '千石 千尋', '配角', 'Megumi Toyoguchi', '__Height:__ 164 cm (5''3") Chihiro is the dorm teacher of Sakurasou Dormitory and an art teacher of Suiko. Despite being a teacher, Chihiro is lazy and only cares about drinking alcohol and trying to date men. Despite being a teacher, she often gives Sorata improper advice. She is Mashiro''s cousin and is the one who arranges the transfer, but she forces Sorata to take care of Mashiro due to her laziness. She was a conscientious student of Suiko, and wanted to become a professional artist, but she changed and became an art teacher for unknown reasons instead.', '/uploads/images/c_64175.jpg'),
(49, 'Ayano Iida', '飯田 綾乃', '配角', 'Masumi Asano', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_72753.jpg'),
(49, 'Daichi Miyahara', '宮原大地', '配角', 'Taishi Murata', '[Sorata](https://anilist.co/character/64169/Kanda-Sorata) and [Nanami](https://anilist.co/character/64167/Aoyama-Nanami)''s classmate. ~!He has feelings for Nanami.!~', '/uploads/images/c_72755.jpg'),
(49, 'Mayu Takasaki', '高崎 繭', '配角', 'Yurika Kubo', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_72757.jpg'),
(49, 'Noriko', '紀子', '配角', 'Harumi Sakurai', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_72759.jpg'),
(49, 'Yuuko Kanda', '神田優子', '配角', 'Yui Ogura', 'Sorata''s little sister, who is currently attending 9th grade. She has a brother complex and even lied to her mom, so she could just meet with Sorata. Has also a complex about her flat chest. ~!She gets accepted into Suiko High and lives in the Sakura Dormitory.!~', '/uploads/images/c_72761.jpg'),
(49, 'Rita Ainsworth', 'リタ・エインワーズ', '配角', 'Ayako Kawasumi', 'Rita was Mashiro''s roommate and handler when Mashiro was in England. Despite her being the same age as Sorata and Mashiro, she has a better figure. She was jealous of Mashiro''s art talent, and so advised Mashiro to draw manga, but later she regrets this and comes to Japan to bring Mashiro back to England. After realizing Mashiro''s determination, she gives up and returns to England with Mashiro''s father and starts to study art again. She argues with Ryuunosuke usually. ~!She falls in love with Ryuunosuke and kisses him on the cheek when leaving, which makes him pass out. While Ryuunosuke is cold to her and keeps letting Maid handle her email, this only provokes her determination and makes her constantly argue with Maid over the Internet. In the fifth novel, she visits Japan again to give Ryuunosuke Valentine''s Day chocolate, and catches a chance to kiss him on the lips this time, which makes him pass out again.!~', '/uploads/images/c_73507.png'),
(49, 'Koharu Shiroyama', '白山小春', '配角', 'Mikako Takahashi', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_73947.jpg'),
(49, 'Momoko', '桃子', '配角', 'Nao Touyama', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_73949.jpg'),
(49, 'Akiko Kanda', '神田 明子', '配角', 'Satomi Arai', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_74291.jpg'),
(49, 'Kanda no Chichi', '空太の父', '配角', 'Tooru Ookawa', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_74293.jpg'),
(49, 'Shiori Nanba', '難波 しおり', '配角', 'Sachiko Kojima', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_74295.jpg'),
(49, 'Kazuki Fujisawa', '藤沢 和希', '配角', 'Shintarou Asanuma', 'A game designer. ~!Used to be a resident of Sakurasou.!~ ~!In love with Chihiro.!~', '/uploads/images/c_74695.jpg'),
(49, 'Yayoi Honjou', '本庄 やよい', '配角', 'Yumi Uchiyama', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_75146.jpg'),
(49, 'Shiho Fukaya', '深谷 志穂', '配角', 'Saori Oonishi', 'Classmate of Mashiro.', '/uploads/images/c_75148.jpg'),
(49, 'Saori Himemiya', '姫宮 沙織', '配角', 'Ayumi Fujimura', 'Saori "Hau-Hau" Himemiya is the person Kamiigusa Misaki goes to for her audio. She''s also the person who dates Tatebayashi Souichirou the ex-president of the Student Council.', '/uploads/images/c_75350.jpg'),
(49, 'Souichirou Tatebayashi', '舘林総一郎', '配角', 'Satoshi Hino', 'Boyfriend of Himemiya Saori and president of the student council. Also hates Jin.', '/uploads/images/c_75352.jpg'),
(49, 'Fuuka Kamiigusa', '上井草風香', '配角', 'Saori Hayami', 'Misaki''s big sister. She looks like Misaki and she is Mitaka Jin ex-girlfriend.', '/uploads/images/c_75680.jpg'),
(49, 'Otoha Nakano', '中野乙羽', '配角', 'Yuka Ootsubo', 'She is visual game original character. Briefly appears in the anime.', '/uploads/images/c_76038.jpg'),
(49, 'Iori Himemiya', '姫宮 伊織', '配角', 'Nobunaga Shimazaki', 'He is the younger brother of Saori Himemiya ~!and a new resident of Sakurasou after Misaki Kamiigusa and Jin Mitaka graduate and leave Sakurasou.!~', '/uploads/images/c_81267.jpg'),
(49, 'Kanna Hase', '長谷 栞奈', '配角', 'Haruka Yamazaki', 'Kanna is a first-year student and the highest scorer on entrance exam. ~! She decides to move into Sakurasou after Jin and Misaki graduate.!~', '/uploads/images/c_81325.jpg'),
(49, 'Maid-chan', 'メイドちゃん', '配角', 'Yui Horie', 'Maid is Ryuunosuke''s artificial intelligence (AI) program he wrote personally. Originally, Ryuunosuke designed Maid to filter and automatically reply to his cellphone messages and emails to save him time. However, Ryuunosuke keeps expanding Maid''s AI ability. Maid is now capable of blocking and replying to a message or email by her own preference, using new words she has recently learned from other messages, emails, or the Internet in the reply, giving Sorata solid advice for his computer game program, anticipating people''s emotions with cameras, writing computer or cellphone viruses and sending them out by herself, or even hacking into Suiko''s computer to steal information. The only way to distinguish Maid''s message from those from a human is that she replies too quickly. Ryuunosuke lets Maid enter a social networking service, with most people who meet her not realizing she is an AI program. According to Ryuunosuke, his ultimate goal is to give Maid an artificial body and become a real human.', '/uploads/images/c_84923.jpg'),
(50, 'Shizuku Mizutani', '水谷雫', '主角', 'Haruka Tomatsu', '__Height:__ 158 cm (5''2") A high school student who is only interested about studying and getting the top grades in the class. She appears indifferent towards everything outside of studying.', '/uploads/images/c_37685.jpg'),
(50, 'Haru Yoshida', '吉田春', '主角', 'Tatsuhisa Suzuki', '__Height:__ 178 cm (5''10") Haru is the male protagonist of the story. He is a high school student who sits next to Shizuku in class. He is a delinquent boy who is absent for a long time after getting in a fight early in the story. Despite being a trouble maker, he is a passionate boy who helps others and can achieve high grades with little effort. He does not like going to school because most people see him as a threat and are afraid of him, saddening him as he is unable to make real friends. After meeting Shizuku, he takes her as his first real friend and starts to attend school, falling in love with her in the process. He also keeps a rooster and brings it to school everyday, despite his teacher''s disapproval. He has somewhat of a perverted mind, openly saying to Shizuku that he would "do" her and has "dirty thoughts" about her. It is unclear whether or not he actually thinks before he speaks. ~!At first, Haru was shown to be a delinquent, but as the story unfolds, it was revealed that he was rather a shy and innocent boy. However, he has bipolar tendencies, most likely the result of not interacting with many people in the past.!~', '/uploads/images/c_37687.jpg'),
(50, 'Asako Natsume', '夏目あさ子', '配角', 'Atsumi Tanezaki', '__Height:__ 157 cm She was a classmate of [Shizuku](https://anilist.co/character/37685/Mizutani-Shizuku) who one day asks for help in a re-test that she must not fail. She''s revealed to be active on the web, where she has a blog, on which she even posted to need two strands of Mitti''s hair to complete a ritual that''d assure them to become best friends. She''s good at sports. She has poor grades, and does not have any friends outside of the internet. She was bullied and ostracized by her friends and classmates in the past, due to her popularity with the boys. She falls in love with [Mitsuyoshi Misawa](https://anilist.co/character/64079/Misawa-Mitsuyoshi) and is often comforted by [Souhei Sasahara](https://anilist.co/character/52617/Sasahara-Souhei) when her love attempts fail. She is voiced by Yuiko Tatsumi in drama CD.', '/uploads/images/c_37813.jpg'),
(50, 'Souhei Sasahara', '佐々原宗平', '配角', 'Ryouta Oosaka', '**Height:** 164 cm (5''5) He is a cheerful, friendly, straightforward guy who says what''s on his mind without hesitation. He has knows Haru since middle school and he gets along with everyone. Due to his kindness, he is seen by his friends as a popular boy who is always surrounded by people. ~!In the manga, it is confirmed that he likes Natsume.!~', '/uploads/images/c_52617.jpg'),
(50, 'Yuuzan Yoshida', '吉田優山', '配角', 'Yuuichi Nakamura', '__Height:__ 176 cm Haru''s older brother. He loves sweet things and is often seen eating them. He especially loves donuts. He and his brother don''t really get along with each other. Although Yuuzan tries to get closer to his younger brother and understand him, Haru doesn''t accept him. However Yuuzan claims Haru has a brother complex, though this is denied by Haru himself. He came to take Haru back home upon their father''s request for Haru to attend a nearer school, where he has more leverage, although Yuuzan does want Haru to continue going to school with Shizuku.', '/uploads/images/c_53087.jpg'),
(50, 'Kenji Yamaguchi', '山口賢二', '配角', 'Takuma Terashima', '__Height:__ 177 cm (5''10) He "takes" money from Haru, even though he is rich. He always is with 3 more guys and he knows Haru since he was a child. He is often lost and is very wary of Yuuzan. ~!Later, he starts to like Shizuku, confessing to her.!~', '/uploads/images/c_54823.jpg'),
(50, 'Chizuru Ooshima', '大島千づる', '配角', 'Kana Hanazawa', '__Height:__ 165 cm (5''5) She is a member of the committee class, chosen because she wears glasses. She was helped by Yoshida Haru, and after been cheered her up by Haru, she fell in love with him. She is very shy, a little pessimistic, and anxious, and even though she likes Haru, she always gives him advice when he can''t understand Shizuku.', '/uploads/images/c_54827.jpg'),
(50, 'Yuu Miyama', '宮間ユウ', '配角', 'Sayuri Yahagi', '__Height:__ 146 cm (4''9) A close friend of Oshima since middle school. She is currently in a long distance relationship with a prior classmate of hers from middle school.', '/uploads/images/c_57363.jpg'),
(50, 'Takaya Mizutani', '水谷隆也', '配角', 'Ayumu Murase', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_57365.jpg'),
(50, 'Mitsuyoshi Misawa', '三沢満善', '配角', 'Tomoyuki Higuchi', '__Height:__ 185 cm (6'') Mitsuyoshi is a tall, tan skinned young man with dark brown combed back hair. His attire often consists of casual clothes, his ever-present sunglasses, piercings, a silver necklace, two rings on each hand, a cigarette, and the occasional wrist band. Also, according to the manga, Mitsuyoshi''s eyes strongly resemble [Haru](https://anilist.co/character/37687/Yoshida-Haru) and [Yuuzan](https://anilist.co/character/53087/Yoshida-Yuuzan)''s father''s eyes, which is why he wears sunglasses constantly; so the two siblings do not hate him.', '/uploads/images/c_64079.jpg'),
(50, 'Masahiro Ayanokouji', '綾小路昌弘', '配角', 'Atsushi Abe', '__Height:__ 164 cm (5''5)', '/uploads/images/c_68367.jpg'),
(50, 'Ryuuji Tomioka', '富岡竜二', '配角', 'Yuuki Ono', '__Height:__ 178 cm (5''10)', '/uploads/images/c_68369.jpg'),
(50, 'Saeko Ninomiya', '二宮冴子', '配角', 'Nozomi Sasaki', 'A teacher in Haru''s school.', '/uploads/images/c_72743.jpg'),
(50, 'Takashi Mizutani', '水谷隆司', '配角', 'Takehito Koyasu', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_72745.jpg'),
(50, 'Kyouko Misawa', '三沢京子', '配角', 'Ai Orikasa', '__Height:__ 170 cm', '/uploads/images/c_73915.jpg'),
(50, 'Shimoyanagi', '下柳', '配角', 'Yuuichi Iguchi', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_73917.jpg'),
(50, 'Seta', '瀬田', '配角', 'Junichi Yanagita', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_73919.jpg'),
(50, 'Murakami', '村上', '配角', 'Ryouta Asari', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_73921.jpg'),
(50, 'Terashima', '寺島', '配角', 'Yuusuke Shirai', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_73923.jpg'),
(50, 'Yumeko', 'ゆめ子', '配角', 'Natsue Sasamoto', 'A nurse.', '/uploads/images/c_76004.jpg'),
(50, 'Nagoya', '名古屋', '配角', 'Yuuki Ono', 'Nagoya is a stray rooster that Haru named.', '/uploads/images/c_181123.png'),
(51, 'Joutarou Kuujou', '空条承太郎', '配角', '', '__Height:__ 195 cm (6''5") __Occupation:__ Student, Marine Explorer, Oceanographer __Nationality:__ Japanese Joutarou is Holly Kujo''s son and [Joseph Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/6356)''s grandson. In Part 3, he has a recognizable attire of a blue trenchcoat-length school uniform jacket with yellow chains on the collar. He also wears a trademark hat which, while torn in the back, often seems to blend with his hair. When Joutarou first appears, he turned himself in to the police because he believes his Stand is an evil spirit possessing him. After he is released from jail, and learns what his Stand is, Joutarou gets used to Star Platinum -- a fierce, muscular, vaguely Aztec-looking spirit with "the precision of a machine" and the ability to destroy virtually anything with a sledgehammer barrage of fists. He has a very tough exterior, and is even rather rough and delinquent, but he also is very dedicated, intense, and loyal. He is very intelligent, but usually lets his (or Star Platinum''s) fists do the talking with the enemy, even though he often has to rely on his wits to deal with stand users'' attacks. He is also known for a quick and short temper. His catchphrase is "Yare yare daze." It generally relates of being bored or exasperation. In Part 3, he is the main target of [Dio](https://anilist.co/character/4004), who realizes that Joutarou is his greatest threat. One of the strongest stands in the JoJo universe; Star Platinum possesses super human senses, strength, sta', '/uploads/images/c_4003.png'),
(51, 'Dio Brando', 'ディオ・ブランドー', '主角', 'Takehito Koyasu', '__Height:__ 195 cm (6''5") __Race:__ Human (formerly), Vampire (onwards) __Nationality:__ British Dio is an immortal vampire and the arch rival of the Joestar clan. __Series 1: Phantom Blood__ ~!Dio is the son of [Dario Brando](https://anilist.co/character/74099/Brando-Dario), an alcoholic and abusive father. Back when Dio was just a boy, he was brought into the household of [George Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/21956/Joestar-I-George) after the mysterious death of his father, so as to repay the debt he owed Dio''s father for saving his life. But soon Dio''s personality caused trouble for George''s young son, [Jonathan Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/8087/Joestar-Jonathan). Even more of a sociopath than his father, Dio was resolute to shatter Jonathan''s spirit and take his place as the favored son, even going so far as to arrange for Jonathan''s dog [Danny](https://anilist.co/character/222601/Danny) to be burned to death. Initially, Dio is able earn the trust of the patriarch of the Joestar family through deceit (and at Jonathan''s expense). However, his plans of taking over the Joestar household were discovered by Jonathan when he discovered that not only had Dio poisoned his biological father to death, he was doing the same to his adoptive father, all to take the Joestar estate for his own. Determined not to be stopped, and understanding the potential to enjoy power over all things instead of just the Joestar estate, Dio wears and activates the Stone Mask, becoming ', '/uploads/images/c_4004.png'),
(51, 'Joseph Joestar', 'ジョセフ・ジョースター', '主角', 'Tomokazu Sugita', '__Height__: 195 cm (6''5") Joseph Joestar begins as a young Englishman in New York, with his grandmother [Erina](https://anilist.co/character/21937). However, an attack by [Straits](https://anilist.co/character/21961) and the disappearance of [Robert Edward O Speedwagon](https://anilist.co/character/21938) soon involve him in the greater chain of events.', '/uploads/images/c_6356.png'),
(51, 'Jonathan Joestar', 'ジョナサン・ジョースター', '主角', 'Kazuyuki Okitsu', '__Height:__ 195 cm __Nationality:__ British __Occupation:__ Archaeologist Born the unique son of the wealthy businessman [George Joestar I](https://anilist.co/character/21956), Jonathan is an honest, kind, and positive man whose life is fraught with tragedy after meeting his adopted older brother - and series antagonist - [Dio Brando](https://anilist.co/character/4004). In his battle against Dio, Jonathan becomes a Ripple user under the tutelage of the master [Will Anthonio Zeppeli](https://anilist.co/character/18062). **Part 5:**~!Jonathan is the biological father of [Giorno Giovanna](https://anilist.co/character/10529), the protagonist of Vento Aureo, as well as a handful of other illegitimate offspring.!~', '/uploads/images/c_8087.png'),
(51, 'Will A. Zeppeli', 'ウィル・A・ツェペリ', '配角', 'Yoku Shioya', 'Will A. Zeppeli was on a ship with a crew studying Aztec ruins when he was younger when his father put on the mask and killed everyone in the crew but his son. After this horrific event, Zeppeli travels the world in order to destroy the mask, and sees a man cure someone using the Ripple. Zeppeli is then directed to his master Tonpetty, who teaches him to use the Ripple. However, Tonpetty foresees Zeppeli''s death during his training, warning him that should he complete his training he will surely die. Zeppeli doesn''t share this fact until the fight with Tarkus, where he afterwards gives his power to Jonathan, whom he trained after the Joestar''s house burns down. His grandson is Caesar Anthonio Zeppeli.', '/uploads/images/c_18062.jpg'),
(51, 'Erina Pendleton', 'エリナ・ペンドルトン', '配角', 'Ayako Kawasumi', 'Erina is a young girl from [Jonathan Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/8087/)''s hometown. ~!She becomes his love interest then wife. She is the mother to [George Joestar II](https://anilist.co/character/130262/), and the grandmother and guardian to [Joseph Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/6356/).!~ (Source: JoJo Wikia)', '/uploads/images/c_21937.jpg'),
(51, 'Robert E. O. Speedwagon', 'ロバート・E・O・スピードワゴン', '配角', 'Youji Ueda', 'Robert E. O. Speedwagon is a major ally featured in the 1st part of JoJo''s Bizarre Adventure, Phantom Blood, and then the 2nd part, Battle Tendency. Formerly a Londoner thug residing in Ogre Street, Speedwagon befriends [Jonathan Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/8087/Joestar-Jonathan) and, despite remaining a powerless human, becomes a loyal ally to the Joestar Family during his whole life and beyond thanks to the company he''s founded: the Speedwagon Foundation. His company supports the Joestars in Stardust Crusaders, Diamond is Unbreakable, and Stone Ocean.', '/uploads/images/c_21938.jpg'),
(51, 'George Joestar I', 'ジョージ・ジョースターI世', '配角', 'Masashi Sugawara', 'George is [Jonathan Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/8087/Joestar-Jonathan)''s father and, after a tragic misunderstanding, adopts [Dio Brando](https://anilist.co/character/4004/Brando-Dio) in his family, kick-starting the events of the first six parts of the series.', '/uploads/images/c_21956.jpg'),
(51, 'Smokey Brown', 'スモーキー・ブラウン', '配角', 'Yuu Hayashi', 'A young boy living in New York. Joseph saves him from brutal, racist policemen, and he sticks around long enough to watch the battle against Straits. He also shows up at the end of Part 2 with Rudolf von Stroheim''s cavalry. Smokey is initially shown with a pigtail in Volume 5, which mysteriously disappears in the rest of the series. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_21957.jpg'),
(51, 'Rudol von Stroheim', 'ルドル・フォン・シュトロハイム', '配角', 'Atsushi Imaruoka', 'Stroheim is the commander of the Wehrmacht forces who discovered Santana in Mexico. ~!He is appropriately militaristic and menacing, but is also responsible for not only saving the life of Robert E. O. Speedwagon, but also for trying to help Joseph Joestar defeat Santana by blowing himself (and the enemy) up. He returns later as a cyborg to assist in the fight against Cars were he is sliced to pieces by Cars. He later returns again with a squad of soldiers to aid Joseph when an army of vampires tries to attack him. Later, when Joseph takes a plane to try and send Cars into a volcano, he saves him by jumping out the cockpit, breaking his legs as a direct result. He dies in 1943 in the front during the Battle of Stalingrad as a German soldier. He is the one who made Joseph''s prosthetic cyborg hand.!~ (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_21958.jpg'),
(51, 'Caesar Zeppeli', 'シーザー・アントニオ・ツェペリ', '主角', 'Takuya Satou', '__Height:__ 186 cm The grandson of [Will A. Zeppeli](https://anilist.co/character/18062/Zeppeli-Will-A). He is a blond, suave ladies'' man, as well as a skilled Ripple user. He was taught by [Lisa Lisa](https://anilist.co/character/21960/Lisa-Lisa), and currently lives in Italy. He is rather cool and collected, especially compared to [Joseph](https://anilist.co/character/6356/Joestar-Joseph), with whom he is grudgingly paired to fight the Pillar Men. But over time Joseph starts to grow on him so much he is able to understand his strange thought pattern. ~!When Caesar was young his father suddenly left with no explanation. Because of this Caesar grew up hating his father thinking he was out living a new life. One day when Caesar spots him walking he tails him with the intention of killing him. Caesar spots a jewel not knowing that it was the activation of [Wham](https://anilist.co/character/21965/Wamuu)''s trap and his father pushes him out of the way, sacrificing himself for Caesar. This leads to Caesar going ahead of the rest of the group to fight Wham, where he meets the ultimate fate, but not before doing his fair share of damage and ripping off Wham''s lip piercing, sending it in a Ripple bubble for Joseph before his body is crushed by a rock.!~', '/uploads/images/c_21959.jpg'),
(51, 'Lisa Lisa', 'リサリサ', '配角', 'Atsuko Tanaka', '__Birthday:__ ~!Dec, 1888!~ __Age:__ ~!50!~ __Height:__ 175 cm A mysterious Ripple user whom Joseph Joestar meets in Venice, Lisa Lisa reveals herself to be his friend Caesar Zeppeli''s mentor. She trains Joseph in the ways of the Ripple and joins in the fight against the Pillar Men, as a powerful Ripple user in her own right. ~!It is eventually revealed that she is Joseph''s long-lost mother, despite her youthful appearance. Her real name is Elisabeth Joestar and she is the infant Jonathan Joestar saved at the end of Phantom Blood and gave to his widow Erina to raise. She was subsequently adopted by the Ripple user Straits, and learned the art of the Ripple from him. As a young adult, Elisabeth eventually married George Joestar II, and they had one child. After George had been killed by a vampire, Elisabeth murdered her husband''s killer and burned him to ash, but he happened to be a high ranking military official. In order to avoid retaliation, the Speedwagon Foundation helped her to erase all evidence of her existence. She is gravely wounded in her one-on-one struggle with Kars, but manages to survive. She later tells Joseph her relation to him personally, at his own funeral. She eventually remarries.!~', '/uploads/images/c_21960.jpg'),
(51, 'Straits', 'ストレイツォ', '配角', 'Nobuo Tobita', 'Straits is another of Tonpetty''s followers. He aided Jonathan in the fight against Dio and his minions. He, along with Dire, were named after the band Dire Straits. ~!When Santana was discovered in the 1930s during Part 2, he betrayed Speedwagon and donned one of the newly discovered Stone Masks. He explained that he had always envied Dio''s strength and beauty and, as a result, desired to stop his aging process. He died after battling and losing to Joseph Joestar in New York City, overloading his own vampire body with Ripple energy. He is also the adoptive father of Lisa Lisa. !~ (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_21961.png'),
(51, 'Suzie Q', 'スージーＱ', '配角', 'Sachiko Kojima', '__Height:__ 168 cm The female assistant to Lisa Lisa. Suzie Q is a slightly ditzy girl who worries for her friends. Evidently this carefree personality has not diminished even in the events of Stardust Crusaders, when she is shown enthusiastically recording her sightings in Japan on a camcorder when on a trip to see her daughter. ~!She is introduced as the female assistant to Lisa Lisa. When she first appears, she is taken over by the remains of Esidisi and attacks her friends. Thanks to a combination attack by Caesar and Joseph, she is saved with only minor injury. She marries Joseph in 1939.!~', '/uploads/images/c_21962.png'),
(51, 'Santana', 'サンタナ', '配角', 'Kenji Nomura', 'He is discovered in a Mexican pyramid in 1938. He is then awakened and studied by a Nazi vampire study team in an underground base. The team, led by Major Stroheim, conducts live human experiments with the stone mask to try to strengthen the Nazi Army. The team awakens Santana in an advanced isolation room fortified with steel plates, and conduct behavioral experiments on him. They soon find that Santana feeds on vampires and is able to absorb food from the surface of his body. The team then is shocked by Santana''s escape from the isolation room. Santana breaks many of his own bones in order to squeeze himself into the 4-by-20 cm ventilation outlet of the room, and does all this at a speed faster than human eyes can perceive. The team shoots Santana with machine guns, only to find that Santana has learned their language and the mechanisms of their weapons from only minutes of contact. He then easily disposes of the Nazis who disturbed his sleep, and even manages to stay alive after being attacked, exposed to sunlight, and blown up. He is named after the long-lived rock group Santana. He is the only member of the Pillar Men to survive, and is theoretically still alive throughout all of the arcs. However, due to his vastly-improved Ripple power, it is possible that Joseph killed him after returning to America. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_21963.png'),
(51, 'ACDC', 'エシディシ', '配角', 'Keiji Fujiwara', 'ACDC is one of the Pillar Men that were discovered by Nazis in Rome. Like Wham and Cars, ACDC is very confident in his powers and abilities and see humans as inferior. However, he has a more violent temper than the others to the point that he has to cry and sob to calm himself down. He is named after Australian Hard rock band AC/DC. ~!ACDC uses "the skill of fire". He raises his body temperature in order to heat his blood to 500°C. He then extends his blood vessels out of his body and makes them into long, prehensile needles with which he injects his hot blood into enemies, dissolving them from within. Even if the blood isn''t injected directly, it can still eat through flesh and metal alike if sprayed on a target from the outside. AC/DC has been shown to have an extremely erratic temper, sobbing at the sight of his own severed arm, only to calm himself near-instantly and replace it with the arm of Loggins. He himself stated that he has a more explosive temper than either of his brethren, and claims to openly express any rage or sorrow he feels so he doesn''t lose his self-control. ACDC had traveled to ancient China and knew Sun Tzu''s theory that "all warfare is based on deception". In his battle with Joseph Joestar, he tries to intimidate him by disabling Joseph''s deceptive tactics. ACDC cuts the hidden rope through which Joseph plans to send Ripple energy to hurt him. Nevertheless, he falls for Joseph''s more sophisticated deception, for Joseph has predicted his action and emp', '/uploads/images/c_21964.png'),
(51, 'Wamuu', 'ワムウ', '配角', 'Akio Ootsuka', 'Wamuu is introduced as a servant to both Esidisi and Kars. He is a very strong and honorable warrior who possess the power of the wind, and also reflexively attacks anyone who steps on his shadow. If he goes blind, he can grow a horn on his forehead and sense sound waves with it. He can also draw air into his body and blast it through the tip of the horn, creating a highly-destructive "wind scalpel". He is also extremely honorable, stopping himself from defeating a defenseless Joseph Joestar when he said that with a month to train he could beat Wham. ~!Later on, he engaged in battle with Caesar Anthonio Zeppeli and killed him, but not before he managed to rip off Wham''s lip piercing containing the poison within Joseph. In another display of honor, Wham allowed the antidote to stay where Joseph could get it out of respect for Caesar''s valiant effort. Later challenging Wham to battle to avenge Caesar, they engaged in a deadly Roman chariot race, with Wham initially getting the upper hand. After Joseph managed to counter Wham''s wind scalpel, he was left as nothing more than a head with the Ripple energy slowly killing him. After Joseph gave Wham some of his own blood to ease his pain, he used the last of is strength to destroy a group of vampires that attempted to kill Joseph. Wham then vanished in a gust of wind, with Joseph giving an unconscious salute to him.!~ He is named after the 80s duo featuring George Michael, Wham!. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_21965.png'),
(51, 'Kars', 'カーズ', '配角', 'Kazuhiko Inoue', 'Cars is the leader of the Pillar Men. He is intelligent, ruthless, and single-minded in his dedication to obtaining the Red Stone of Aja. Strangely, despite his apathy towards humans and willingness to kill them, he has been shown to be more compassionate for other living beings. In Switzerland, he sliced a car that was about to hit a puppy in half, and later on maneuvered himself during a long fall to miss a patch of flowers near the bottom of the cliff. Cars'' power is that of light; he is able to produce bladed appendages from his arms and use these to reflect blinding light toward his enemies. He also has the same powers over his body that all the Pillar Men share. ~!When he gains the power of the stone mask, he becomes invulnerable to sunlight, and also gains some abilities on a genetic level; he can produce living creatures and control them, and can mutate his body into various forms. He outlasts his comrades and eventually does gain almost unlimited power as the ultimate "evolved" man through the Red Stone of Aja and a stone mask. In a final confrontation, he succeeds in severing Joseph''s hand but is eventually blown into space by a volcanic eruption as well as an ultimate Ripple attack from Joseph. Being immortal, he does not die; however he is unable to return to Earth after being thrown out of orbit. Trapped in the void of space for eternity, he eventually stops thinking and desires death.!~ He is named after the 80''s new wave group The Cars. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_21966.png'),
(51, 'Narrator', 'ナレーター', '配角', 'Tooru Ookawa', 'This character page is set to represent and list all narrators, which haven''t been given a visual representation of themselves in their respective work. Please add other narrator characters, which were given a visual representation of themselves, separately from this narrator page.', '/uploads/images/c_36309.jpg'),
(51, 'Dire', 'ダイアー', '配角', 'Taketora', 'Dire is a minor ally featured in Phantom Blood. Dire is a Ripple disciple under the Ripple Master Tonpetty and is a very close friend of Will Anthonio Zeppeli.', '/uploads/images/c_74057.png'),
(51, 'Tompetty', 'トンペティ', '配角', 'Tamio Ooki', 'Tonpetty is a minor ally featured in Part I: Phantom Blood. He is a Ripple master who trained Will Anthonio Zeppeli as well as Straizo and Dire.', '/uploads/images/c_74097.png'),
(51, 'Dario Brando', 'ダリオ・ブランドー', '配角', 'Tadashi Miyazawa', 'Dario is the father of [Dio Brando](https://anilist.co/character/4004/Brando-Dio). An alcoholic and abusive man, he is primarily responsible for contributing to Dio''s descent into evil. After a tragic misunderstanding, [George Joestar I](https://anilist.co/character/21956/Joestar-I-George) decides to give him a favor and adopts his son Dio into the Joestar Family.', '/uploads/images/c_74099.png'),
(51, 'Wang Chung', 'ワンチェン', '配角', 'Hiroshi Naka', 'Wang Chan is a minor antagonist featured in Part I: Phantom Blood personally as a human, Wang Chan has shown a greedy personality, selling a poison to Dio Brando without any regard for its use and heading back to the Joestar mansion to salvage for treasures and antiques. Upon becoming a vampire, however, he becomes entirely devoted to Dio''s wishes. Synopsis Originally only known as the "Oriental Man", he owned a curiosity shop on Ogre Street. Wang Chang sold Dio the poison which Dio used in his murder of Dario Brando and his attempted murder of George Joestar, although Wang was not concerned with what the poison was to be used for. He told Dio, without much, if any, intent to provoke him, of a man in his own land who had a similar birthmark to Dio''s who had had a harsh life, but in the end lived to be over 183. Sometime after, he was was captured by Jonathan Joestar and taken to the the Joestar Manor. When he is used in an attempt to force Dio to go with the police, he again mentions his fortune telling, saying that Dio is far too lucky to fully have to give up this early. Dio uses George''s blood to become a vampire, taking Wang Chan as his subordinate when the latter goes to search the Joestar manor for valuables. Dio trusts him enough to be responsible for his head and implanting it onto Jonathan''s body. This did not go according to plan, however as Jonathan use the last of his strength to crush Wang Chan''s head and sent a ripple to take control of his body, and made him si', '/uploads/images/c_74101.png'),
(51, 'Jack', '切り裂きジャック', '配角', 'Naomi Kusumi', 'Jack is a serial killer who meets Dio Brando and is transformed into a Zombie sent to fight the Joestar Group. He was inspired by the historical figure of the same name. (Source: JoJo Wikia)', '/uploads/images/c_74105.png'),
(51, 'Tarkus', 'タルカス', '配角', 'Tetsu Inada', 'Tarkus the "Dark Knight" was a knight from 16th Century Great Britain who was executed after losing a war. Resurrected as a Zombie by Dio Brando, he is wholeheartedly loyal to his new master and fights the Joestar Group. (Source: JoJo Wikia)', '/uploads/images/c_74109.png'),
(51, 'Bruford', 'ブラフォード', '配角', 'Kenjirou Tsuda', 'Bruford is an antagonist featured in Part I: Phantom Blood. He is a vampire made from the centuries-old corpse of a brave and powerful warrior of ancient Britain. Along with Tarkus, Bruford was one of "The Dark Knights". He also had unusual battle prowess and powers associated with his dark hair. ~!Bruford and Tarkus were successful in the Challenge of the 77 in 1563, two of only five challengers to succeed in history. Prior to their corruption, Bruford and Tarkus were members of the Tudor Dynasty and retainers of Mary Stuart. Eventually they were beheaded for supporting Mary against her political rival, Elizabeth. However, Elizabeth''s deception to force them to surrender led to a strong sense of betrayal that made them susceptible to manipulation by Dio.!~ ~!The pair were eventually resurrected as vampires by Dio Brando to oppose Jonathan Joestar, Will A. Zeppeli, and Robert Speedwagon. Bruford''s manipulation of his hair poses much challenge to Jonathan, eventually leading to them fighting underwater, until Jonathan swims downward to find air bubbles beneath the rocks, enabling him to draw breath and hit Bruford with a ripple overdrive. Moments before he disintegrates from the ripple, Bruford gives Jonathan his sword, Luck and Pluck. However, his corpse is kicked aside by a wrathful Tarkus, who attempts to finish off Jonathan and party on his own.!~', '/uploads/images/c_74113.png'),
(51, 'Holly Kuujou', '空条ホリィ       ', '配角', '', 'Holly Kuujou née Joestar is the daughter of [Joseph Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/6356/) and mother of [Joutarou Kuujou](https://anilist.co/character/4003/).', '/uploads/images/c_129824.png'),
(51, 'Mary Joestar', 'メアリー・ジョースタ', '配角', '', 'Mary Joestar is the late mother of Jonathan Joestar and wife of George Joestar. Never shown in person in the series, the only thing known about her story is that she accompanied her husband during a trip to London and died protecting her baby when her carriage had an accident and fell into a ravine. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130250.png'),
(51, 'Tattoo', '刺青', '配角', 'Hiroaki Tajiri', 'Tattoo is a rugged looking grown man with a medium sized beard and unkempt hair. His wardrobe consists mainly of a fringed leather jacket, pants, and belt. His most noticeable feature, and the obvious source of his name, is a large tattoo stretching from cheek to cheek and from forehead to nose dorsum - the tattoo appears to be either a butterfly or a design similar to a Rorschach test image. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130251.png'),
(51, 'Doobie', 'ドゥービー', '配角', 'Yuuichi Ishigami', 'Doobie is a minor antagonist featured in Phantom Blood. He is a musclebound masked zombie that Dio Brando sics on Poco''s Sister after she refuses to serve him. Doobie grabs the girl and rips her dress in an attempt to assault her, but his plan is quickly ruined by an anvil thrown by Jonathan Joestar. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130252.png'),
(51, 'Poco', 'ポコ', '配角', 'Yumiko Kobayashi', 'Poco was a cowardly boy who got bullied by other kids, but was protected by his sister. When confronted by her about when he was going to fight back and live on his own, Poco answered that he would do this "tomorrow", which causes her to slap him. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130253.png'),
(51, 'Donovan', 'ドノヴァン', '配角', 'Kenichirou Matsuda', 'Donovan is a mature athletic man whose dark hair is slicked back. His skin is colored differently around his eyes, starting from a wide area on his hairline and converging to the side of the root of his nose. Donovan wears a sleeveless officer outfit. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130259.png'),
(51, 'Mario Zeppeli', 'マリオ ・ ツェペリ', '配角', 'Jin Yamanoi', 'Mario Zeppeli is characterized as hard-working, trustworthy, and a wholesome family man. Although he loved his family, Mario had to abandon them in order to investigate the Pillar Men. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130260.png'),
(51, 'Loggins', 'ロギンズ', '配角', 'Yutaka Nakano', 'Loggins is a tall, muscular man with chiseled features and somewhat glazed eyes. He wears a tunic, an over-sized fez, and armbands. Loggins displays a very demanding demeanor when instructing Joseph and Caesar, often forcing them to do tough trials during their Ripple training. Despite this, he seems to have, along with Messina, a sense of humor as the two would often tease their disciples. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130261.png'),
(51, 'George II Joestar', 'ジョージ・ジョースター 2世', '配角', '', 'George resembles his father Jonathan and his son Joseph. He is only seen wearing a military dress uniform. Assumed to be a capable fighter pilot, George was one of the first to fly an aircraft during World War I. It''s hinted that he may have had a talent for the Ripple much like his father and son, though he was never given any training to properly use it. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130262.png'),
(51, 'Messina', 'メッシーナ', '配角', 'Hidetoshi Nakamura', 'Messina is a tall muscular man with short hair tied into a ponytail and a Fu Manchu mustache. He wears a long hat, a sleeveless tunic, and armbands. Though much of Messina''s personality isn''t focused upon, he displays the characteristics of a stern, yet effective instructor to Joseph and Caesar. Despite this, Messina seems to have a sense of humor as he, along with Loggins, would often tease his disciples during their training. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130263.png'),
(51, 'Poco no Ane', 'ポコの姉', '配角', 'Aya Endou', 'She''s the older sister of Poco and was held captive in the castle by Dio', '/uploads/images/c_154086.png'),
(51, 'Styx', 'スティクス', '配角', 'Masayuki Katou', 'An alcoholic priest who discovers Dio''s coffin in the boat Jonathan and Erina board.', '/uploads/images/c_222600.png'),
(51, 'Danny', 'ダニー', '配角', '', 'Minor character appearing in Phantom Blood. He is [Jonathan Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/8087/Joestar-Jonathan)''s dog and childhood best friend. [George Joestar I](https://anilist.co/character/21956/Joestar-I-George) bought Danny when he was a puppy when Jonathan was five years old. Danny was very afraid of unfamiliar places and strange people causing him to bite Jonathan when the young boy first approached him. For a while, Jonathan also antagonized Danny by throwing stones at him. One day, while swimming in a river, Jonathan started drowning and was saved by Danny, which made them the best of friends. ~!Danny''s death at the hands of [Dio Brando](https://anilist.co/character/4004/Brando-Dio) serves as one of the primary catalysts in the lifelong rivalry between Jonathan and Dio.!~', '/uploads/images/c_222601.png'),
(51, 'Mark', 'マルク', '配角', 'Ryouta Oosaka', 'Mark is a German soldier and a friend of Caesar Zeppeli who participated in the effort for stopping the Pillar Men''s awakening.', '/uploads/images/c_232362.png'),
(51, 'Kisha', '記者', '配角', 'Seiko Yoshida', 'She arrives at the cafe where Joseph and Straizo are fighting and begins to take photos, saying it would reach the front page of the newspaper. Straizo catches her off guard and uses her as a hostage to approach Joseph, vowing to kill her if the Joestar runs off. Though Joseph attempts to bluff his way out by calling her a "floozie" he won''t risk his life to save, Straizo forces Joseph to fight him when he rips the reporter''s tooth out. After being saved, the reporter punches Joseph for insulting her and then kicks him in the knee. The adrenaline from the ordeal then wears off and she screams from the delayed pain of losing her tooth. This content comes from JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia (https://jojowiki.com), and must be attributed to its authors, as specified in the license. JoJo''s Bizarre Wiki (the FANDOM wiki) is prohibited from using it, for repeatedly copying without giving attribution.', '/uploads/images/c_232365.png'),
(51, 'Chuugoku Kenpouka', '中国拳法家', '配角', 'Itaru Yamamoto', 'He originally tries to rob Jonathan Joestar in Ogre Street alongside Robert E. O. Speedwagon and Tattoo', '/uploads/images/c_233084.png'),
(51, 'Elizabeth I', 'エリザベスⅠ世', '配角', 'Yuka Keichou', 'Elizabeth I is a queen of England and a monarch from the Tudor dynasty. In 1565, she battles her first cousin once removed, Mary Stuart, over the throne. Her betrayal of Bruford and Tarkus, two retainers of Mary, led to the two knights cursing humanity; Dio Brando uses this resentment to his advantage over three hundred years later when he revives them as zombies. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Adventure Wiki)', '/uploads/images/c_243876.png'),
(51, 'Shitsuji', '執事', '配角', 'Shinobu Matsumoto', 'A butler of the Joestar Family.', '/uploads/images/c_243880.png'),
(51, 'Wired Beck', '鋼線のベック', '配角', 'Satoshi Tsuruoka', 'He is a Vampire created by Kars tasked with guarding the hotel Kars is hiding in and briefly battles Lisa Lisa.', '/uploads/images/c_243882.png'),
(51, 'Adams', 'アダムス', '配角', 'Hidenori Takahashi', 'Adams is a former human and villager from Windknight''s Lot who becomes a Zombie created by Dio Brando.', '/uploads/images/c_243884.png'),
(51, 'Shikai', '司会', '配角', 'Eiji Takeuchi', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389583.jpg'),
(51, 'Shounen B', '少年B', '配角', 'Ryouta Asari', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389584.jpg'),
(51, 'Yaji B', 'ヤジB', '配角', 'Takahiro Miwa', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389585.jpg'),
(51, 'Otoko', '男', '配角', 'Taira Kikumoto', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389586.jpg'),
(51, 'Kankyaku', '観客', '配角', 'Shinobu Matsumoto', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389587.jpg'),
(51, 'Onna', '女', '配角', 'Keiko Watanabe', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389588.jpg'),
(51, 'Yaji A', 'ヤジA', '配角', 'Yuusuke Kuwahata', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389589.jpg'),
(51, 'Shounen A', '少年A', '配角', 'Yoshitsugu Matsuoka', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389590.jpg'),
(52, 'Narrator', 'ナレーター', '配角', 'Houchuu Ootsuka', 'This character page is set to represent and list all narrators, which haven''t been given a visual representation of themselves in their respective work. Please add other narrator characters, which were given a visual representation of themselves, separately from this narrator page.', '/uploads/images/c_36309.jpg'),
(52, 'Yuuta Togashi', '富樫勇太', '主角', 'Jun Fukuyama', 'A high school boy who used to be a delusional teen, believing himself to be the Dark Flame Master and becoming alienated from everyone as a result. Finding this to be embarrassing, he attempts to erase this past from existence, even choosing to go to a separate high school from all of his junior high school classmates. However, after encountering [Rikka](https://anilist.co/character/65865), his past delusions come back to haunt him.', '/uploads/images/c_65863.jpg'),
(52, 'Rikka Takanashi', '小鳥遊六花', '主角', 'Maaya Uchida', '__Height:__ 150 cm (4''11") Rikka Takanashi is an active Chuunibyou, who still has the syndrome. Her delusional syndrome involves her right eye which she calls her "Wicked Eye," which, according to her, wields darkness tamed by the power of a pure heart. In reality, her so-called "Wicked Eye" is nothing more than a colored contact lens which she conceals underneath an eyepatch. Despite being quite attached to [Yuuta](https://anilist.co/character/65863/Togashi-Yuuta), she is cautious of strangers and adopts a battle pose whenever she meets someone for the first time. She is also rather clumsy, often tripping over and forgetting things. She also doesn''t have many friends, as shown that in her mobile phone only has her sister''s email. ~!Rikka''s father died in the past, which she stubbornly denies. In the process, she one-sidedly met Yuuta, who was an active chuunibyou at that time, and was amazed by how cool Yuuta was as the Dark Flame Master. Her belief that her father is in the "horizon" is the cause of her chuunibyou.!~ ~!Rikka eventually falls in love with Yuuta and makes a contract with him.!~', '/uploads/images/c_65865.jpg'),
(52, 'Makoto Isshiki', '一色誠', '主角', 'Souichirou Hoshi', 'Yuuta''s classmate and friend. He created a "cutie poll" which ranked all the girls in class in terms of cuteness. However, because of this, his head was shaved into a crew cut. Later on he joins Rikka''s club and develops a crush on Kumin.', '/uploads/images/c_65869.jpg'),
(52, 'Shinka Nibutani', '丹生谷森夏', '主角', 'Chinatsu Akasaki', 'A beautiful girl in [Yuuta](https://anilist.co/character/65863/Togashi-Yuuta)''s class. Shinka is Yuuta''s classmate and class representative, who is also a cheerleader. One of the most popular girls in the class due to her looks, she is generally thought of a kind and gentle girl. ~!She too suffered a case of eighth-grader syndrome, going by the name of Forest Summer. Like Yuuta, she chose a school that none of her former classmates were going to so she could escape from her embarrassing past. When she is with Yuuta, [Rikka](https://anilist.co/character/65865/Takanashi-Rikka), and the others in the clubroom, her usual happy, sweet demeanor fades and she is blunt, edgy, and tends to fight with [Dekomori](https://anilist.co/character/67215/Dekomori-Sanae) quite a lot. This is because Dekomori admires Forest Summer (and does not believe Shinka is actually Forest Summer, constantly referring to Shinka as "fake Forest Summer") and has numerous copies of books, consisting of documents that Forest Summer had written, titled Mabinogion. Shinka seeks to destroy every last trace of her past, and Dekomori is a barrier against this, causing frequent fights between them.!~', '/uploads/images/c_65871.jpg'),
(52, 'Yumeha Togashi', '富樫夢葉', '配角', 'Mami Shitara', 'Yumeha is Yuuta''s youngest sister.', '/uploads/images/c_65873.jpg'),
(52, 'Kumin Tsuyuri', '五月七日くみん', '主角', 'Azumi Asakura', 'Kumin is [Yuuta](https://anilist.co/character/65863)''s chill and carefree senpai who loves adventures, cats, and pillows. Spends most of the time in the club room napping. She adores any chuunibyous and once said that it would''ve been fun to have some delusions herself.', '/uploads/images/c_67213.jpg'),
(52, 'Sanae Dekomori', '凸守早苗', '主角', 'Sumire Uesaka', 'Sanae is an underclassman to the rest of the club members. She, like [Rikka](https://anilist.co/character/65865/Takanashi-Rikka), is a Chuunibyou. She claims that she is Rikka''s servant and wants to take her master''s place. Her "power" is Mjolnir, a pair of hair nunchucks. Despite being a Chuunibyou, she is top in her class. Little was known about her relatives but it''s implied that she is from a rich family. ~!She eventually becomes the student council president with [Nibutani](https://anilist.co/character/65871/Nibutani-Shinka) as her vice president. Her "nunchucks" are filled with candy, since her previous attempt with cookies didn''t go well.!~ (Source: Anime News Network)', '/uploads/images/c_67215.jpg'),
(52, 'Kuzuha Togashi', '富樫樟葉', '配角', 'Kaori Fukuhara', 'Kuzuha is [Yuuta Togashi](https://anilist.co/character/65863/Togashi-Yuuta)''s younger sister who is in the first year of junior high school. She knows Yuuta very well, especially how he acted during his Chuunibyou days in middle school as Dark Flame Master, though she always considered him embarrassing. Kuzuha got used to her older brother''s delusions since she was young. Every once in a while she would ponder if her brother''s acts were actually cool before immediately dismissing the thought as Yuuta would spectacularly embarrass himself yet again.', '/uploads/images/c_69431.jpg'),
(52, 'Togashi no Haha', '勇太の母', '配角', 'Yuri Amano', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_69433.jpg'),
(52, 'Touka Takanashi', '小鳥遊十花', '配角', 'Eri Sendai', 'Older sister to [Rikka Takanashi](https://anilist.co/character/65865). According to Rikka, she is the alleged powerful and overseeing Priestess of the Deep Horizon. She uses a ladle as a weapon against Rikka''s crazy antics. She works as a cook. ~!Later in the story she moves to Italy for work and eventually marries there.!~', '/uploads/images/c_71911.jpg'),
(52, 'Nanase Tsukumo', '九十九七瀬', '配角', 'Kikuko Inoue', 'Yuuta and Rikka''s homeroom teacher, who is often kind, if sometimes a little sadistic in teasing her students, particularly Rikka. She is called Nana-chan by Yuuta and Rikka.', '/uploads/images/c_73129.jpg'),
(52, 'Takanashi no Sofu', 'タカナシの祖父', '配角', 'Hiroshi Naka', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_73965.jpg'),
(52, 'Takanashi no Sobo', 'タカナシの祖母', '配角', 'Sumako Nomura', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_73967.jpg'),
(52, 'Takanashi no Haha', '六花の母', '配角', 'Junko Iwao', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_75198.png'),
(52, 'Chimera', 'きめら', '配角', '', 'Throughout the series she is seen wearing pink angel wings with a snake attached to them. Touka Takanashi is allergic to cats and refuses to let Chimera to be near her.', '/uploads/images/c_307712.png'),
(53, 'Hachiman Hikigaya', '比企谷八幡', '主角', 'Takuya Eguchi', '__Height:__ 175 cm (5''9") Hachiman is an isolated, friendless boy who is pragmatic to a fault. His most prominent feature is his set of "dead fish-eyes." He firmly believes that "youth" is simply an illusion created by hypocrites, for hypocrites, born from the ashes of past failures. In this state of apparent corruption, he is coerced into joining the Service Club by his futures advisor in the hopes that exposing him to the world will change his personality, and ultimately make him a "better person." He is called "Hikki" affectionately by [Yui](https://anilist.co/character/67069).', '/uploads/images/c_67065.png'),
(53, 'Yukino Yukinoshita', '雪ノ下雪乃', '主角', 'Saori Hayami', 'Yukino is the leader of the Service Club, of which she is the sole member until [Hachiman](https://anilist.co/character/67065) joins her. She is smart, beautiful, and is nicknamed the "Ice-cold Beauty" for her icy demeanor. She has a twisted sense of "noblesse oblige", and believes that it is the duty of the exceptional (in other words, herself) to help the "lost lambs" of the world. Her personality often leads her to be disgusted at the naivete of others, particularly [Yui](https://anilist.co/character/67069)''s, and she does not hesitate to show it. Despite this, Yui still affectionally calls her "Yukinon." She is a student of Class 2J (The academic standards of Class J are 2 to 3 points higher than the regular classes on the bell curve.) ~!It was later revealed that her father is a member of the National Diet (a legislator in Japan''s parliament). Yukino was in the car that hit [Hachiman](https://anilist.co/character/67065).!~ ~!She later confesses to [Hachiman](https://anilist.co/character/67065) and becomes his girlfriend.!~', '/uploads/images/c_67067.png'),
(53, 'Yui Yuigahama', '由比ヶ浜結衣', '主角', 'Nao Touyama', 'Yui is a cheerful, outgoing girl who becomes the Service Club''s first "customer", asking them to help her bake cookies for "a certain someone". Her problems lie not with her personality, but with her inability to deal with issues by herself. She believes that talent is inborn, and often aspired to be like others until [Yukino](https://anilist.co/character/67067) changed her way of thinking. Following her experience with the Service Club, Yui begins to attend Service Club sessions after school as well, despite Yukino''s objections early on. ~!She is the owner of the dog that led to [Hachiman](https://anilist.co/character/67065)''s accident.!~ ~!She has feelings for [Hachiman](https://anilist.co/character/67065) which she admits to the members of the Service Club in the final episode of the series.!~', '/uploads/images/c_67069.png'),
(53, 'Saika Totsuka', '戸塚彩加', '配角', 'Mikako Komatsu', 'Saika is a member of the tennis club who has a feminine appearance, but prefers others to not mistake his gender. He is called "The Prince" by his female classmates. On their first meeting, Saika asks help from [Hachiman](https://anilist.co/character/67065) to join the tennis club, which was brushed off by [Yukino](https://anilist.co/character/67067). Saika then asked the service club to help him improve his tennis skills. He eventually became one of the few people in class 2F who would talk to Hachiman, and often hangs out with Hachiman.', '/uploads/images/c_67071.jpg'),
(53, 'Yoshiteru Zaimokuza', '材木座義輝', '配角', 'Nobuyuki Hiyama', 'Zaimokuza is a student from class 2C who suffers from adolescent delusions. He displays a high interest in historical shoguns, magic, and writing (despite the fact he is a terrible writer), and video game creation. He often talks like a movie narrator or with grandiose overtones. He sometimes refers to himself and those around him in the 3rd person and involves them in his fantasy/roleplaying scenarios. He sees Hachiman as a friend after being paired up with him during physical education lessons. While he is annoying, he has a group of otaku friends he''s on good terms with. He aims to be a light novel writer.', '/uploads/images/c_67073.png'),
(53, 'Komachi Hikigaya', '比企谷小町', '配角', 'Aoi Yuuki', '[Hachiman](https://anilist.co/character/67065)''s younger sister who is very different than her brother. She''s cheerful and lively and is part of her school''s student council.', '/uploads/images/c_67075.png'),
(53, 'Shizuka Hiratsuka', '平塚静', '配角', 'Ryouka Yuzuki', 'Shizuka is [Hachiman](https://anilist.co/character/67065)''s teacher, a language teacher who serves as his futures advisor/counselor. She is aware of Hachiman''s supposed "problems", and takes steps to ensure he is freed from them, her first move being to force him into joining the Service Club. However, she appears to have some quirks of her own: she is a young smoker, she is very sensitive about her age, and she is often prone to quoting or copying scenes from popular shounen manga. She also never remembers to knock before entering the Service Club''s classroom, much to [Yukino](https://anilist.co/character/67067)''s chagrin.', '/uploads/images/c_67077.png'),
(53, 'Saki Kawasaki', '川崎沙希', '配角', 'Ami Koshimizu', '[Hachiman Hikigaya](https://anilist.co/character/67065/Hikigaya-Hachiman)''s classmate who seems like a delinquent, but wants to make friends. She cares deeply for her brother as she hid her name and age to work in night-shift part-time jobs in order to pay school fees and reduce her family''s load. After her brother asked help from the service club, the service club eventually followed her to her workplace and found out her motives behind working night-shifts, she stopped working after the service club suggested her to aim for a scholarship instead.', '/uploads/images/c_74587.jpg'),
(53, 'Taishi Kawasaki', '川崎大志', '配角', 'Ayumu Murase', 'Saki''s younger brother who requested the group''s help as to find out about his sister''s nightly activities. Which he later found out that her sister is working as a bar tender under a false name and age to support his cram school tuition. (Source: ANN)', '/uploads/images/c_74589.jpg'),
(53, 'Haruno Yukinoshita', '雪ノ下陽乃', '配角', 'Mai Nakahara', '[Yukino](https://anilist.co/character/67067)''s elder sister who is even more outstanding than Yukino. However, unlike Yukino, she shows a good attitude towards other people, even if she has to lie about her true feelings most of the time. As the eldest sister she has to maintain a cheerful facade when representing the family for either their father''s political events or mother''s business meetings.', '/uploads/images/c_79589.png'),
(53, 'Hayato Hayama', '葉山隼人', '配角', 'Takashi Kondou', 'He is a very popular guy in [Hikki](https://anilist.co/character/67065) and [Yui](https://anilist.co/character/67069)''s class, who is good in almost everything. (Source: Otaku-streamers)', '/uploads/images/c_79591.png'),
(53, 'Yumiko Miura', '三浦優美子', '配角', 'Marina Inoue', 'She is [Hikki](https://anilist.co/character/67065) and [Yui](https://anilist.co/character/67069)''s classmate who is very popular in Class 2-F, as well as the main female figure in [Hayato Hayama](https://anilist.co/character/79591/Hayato-Hayama)''s clique. Yumiko''s personality is pompous. Due to her popularity, she is held in highest hierarchy. Hence, she has no trouble making friends and also has little to no understanding towards people who have social troubles. Yumiko doesn''t show interest, or mind anyone other than higher hierarchy of the class, which is noted by Hachiman Hikigaya by her attitude towards him. She holds herself in a very high esteem, and is not afraid to use her authority. Yumiko has be shown to be very good at tennis as it was stated that she won the Junior High Championship. She also demonstrated her skills in the tennis match showdown and she also participated in the athletic festival sports event of cavalry battle for the white team.', '/uploads/images/c_79593.png'),
(53, 'Hina Ebina', '海老名姫菜', '配角', 'Nozomi Sasaki', 'Hina is a classmate of [Yui](https://anilist.co/character/67069) and [Hachiman](https://anilist.co/character/67065), who is a quiet girl and hangs around [Yumiko](https://anilist.co/character/79593/). She is a fujoshi, which is why other boys from her class are always avoiding her.', '/uploads/images/c_79595.png'),
(53, 'Kakeru Tobe', '戸部翔', '配角', 'Chado Horii', 'Kakeru is one of [Hayato](https://anilist.co/character/79591)''s friends. He is in the football club. He has feelings for [Hina](https://anilist.co/character/79595) and is the only guy in class who often supports Hina''s scripts.', '/uploads/images/c_82543.png'),
(53, 'Yamato', '大和', '配角', 'Yoshihisa Kawahara', 'Yamato is one of Hayato''s friends. He is in the rugby club.', '/uploads/images/c_82545.png'),
(53, 'Oooka', '大岡', '配角', 'Minoru Shiraishi', 'Oooka is one of Hayato''s friends. He is in the baseball club.', '/uploads/images/c_82547.png'),
(53, 'Atsugi', '厚木', '配角', 'Yoshihisa Kawahara', 'Atsugi is a physical education teacher in Sōbu High School. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_83657.png'),
(53, 'Rumi Tsurumi', '鶴見留美', '配角', 'Sumire Morohoshi', 'Rumi is a lonely primary school student who is openly despised by her peers. Hayato at first tried to resolve the situation through talking to her in front of her classmates, which instead attracted more hateful attention to her. After much discussion, Hachiman and company decided that the only way out is to destroy the trust between her peers, through having Hayato and Kakeru acting as bullies threatening Rumi''s group-mates during treasure hunt and exposing their selfish nature to each other, thus preventing further organized acts of teasing on Rumi. However, in exchange, she would hardly have any friends after this. (Source:Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_84613.png'),
(53, 'Yuka', '由香', '配角', 'Ibuki Kido', 'First appearance: episode 7', '/uploads/images/c_85213.png'),
(53, 'Hitomi', '仁美', '配角', 'Erii Yamazaki', 'First appearance: episode 7', '/uploads/images/c_85215.png'),
(53, 'Mori', '森', '配角', 'Haruka Shiraishi', 'First appearance: episode 7', '/uploads/images/c_85217.png'),
(53, 'Yokko', 'ヨッコ', '配角', 'Megu Sakuragawa', 'First appearance: episode 7', '/uploads/images/c_85219.png'),
(53, 'Minami Sagami', '相模南', '配角', 'Minako Kotobuki', 'Minami is the leader of the second most influential clique in class 2F, and holds a grudge towards [Yui](https://anilist.co/character/67069/Yuigahama-Yui), who she was friendly with in their first high school year, for being in the superior clique. She volunteered to be event organizer for the cultural festival in order to promote her worth without the actual ability to do such job, and thus requested help from the service club. ~!As such, [Yukino](https://anilist.co/character/67067/Yukinoshita-Yukino) took up the role of assistant event organizer and claimed the spotlight in making the cultural festival a successful one, which in turn made Minami depressed about her own uselessness and refused to host the closing ceremony. However, as [Hachiman](https://anilist.co/character/67065/Hikigaya-Hachiman)''s fierce scolding has successfully turned himself into the scapegoat and shifted the blame away from Minami, she attended the closing ceremony and ended the cultural festival on a high note.!~', '/uploads/images/c_85283.png'),
(53, 'Meguri Shiromeguri', '城廻めぐり', '配角', 'Azumi Asakura', 'Meguri is a third year student and the president of Sobu High School''s student council. Although she is not a reliable leader herself, her personality has brought her immense support from the councilors and thus she is able to unite the student council. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_86015.jpg'),
(54, 'Satan Jacob', 'サタン・ジャコブ', '主角', 'Ryouta Oosaka', 'Satan Jacob is the main protagonist of the series. He was once the Demon King who declared war on Ente Isla in an attempt to annex the four continents. However, due to the actions of the Hero [Emilia Justina](https://anilist.co/character/70735) and her companions, he was forced to retreat to Earth, causing him to lose almost all of his powers. Satan was well-known throughout Ente Isla as the great overlord of his people, his name synonymous with the terror and cruelty his army brought to those unfortunate enough to fall victim. He allowed his minions the right to perform any heinous acts they deemed fit, showing immense cruelty through the slaughter of many innocent humans in his conquest. By contrast, on Earth Sadao Maou is shown to be a diligent and proactive employee, instead applying his strong drive and determination to better himself in his new life. Forced to spend time living as a human and interacting with those he previously considered to be lesser beings, he has since developed a kindhearted and cheerful disposition making him popular among both his colleagues and neighbors. He now strives to climb the corporate ladder at MgRonald''s. ~!Though he is not the legendary Satan spoken of in the Ente Islan Bible, Satan Jacob was given the name at birth, as it has since become an extremely common name among demons. While he once belonged to a lowly goblin-class tribe, Satan''s family and comrades were slaughtered in a conflict between demons, the enemy having left him behin', '/uploads/images/c_70733.png'),
(54, 'Emilia Justina', 'エミリア・ユスティーナ', '主角', 'Youko Hikasa', 'Emilia is the main female protagonist and the Hero who defeated the [Demon King Satan](https://anilist.co/character/70733). After forcing the Demon King to retreat from Ente Isla, she followed him to modern day Japan to ensure his destruction. However, just like the Demon Lord, she lost most of her powers upon her arrival and was forced to assume a Japanese name. She was also forced to find employment, and so became a call center agent. She is a half human and half angel. Overall, Emi is a strong-willed and determined hero, displaying many admirable qualities befitting of one in her position; among which are a pure heart, boundless courage, unwavering loyalty to those closest to her, and a deep-seated desire to protect the innocent. Moreover, she lacks self-confidence and gets angry/frustrated easily. While initially hesitant to become the great hero of Ente Isla, the death of her father at the hands of [Lucifer](https://anilist.co/character/83103)''s Army ignited a fire in the heart of the young hero, giving her a motivation to train harder and strike down those who destroyed her village. Due to her personal losses, she sees all demons as her enemy, most of all their leader, Satan Jacob. ~!Emilia Justina was born to her parents, an ordinary farmer named Nord Justina and the archangel Lailah. Knowing she had committed a taboo by birthing a child to a human, her mother fled, leaving Emilia to be raised by her father on his farm located somewhere on the Western Continent. During', '/uploads/images/c_70735.png'),
(54, 'Alciel', 'アルシエル', '主角', 'Yuuki Ono', 'Alciel is one of Satan''s Demon Generals and was also transported to modern day Japan with him. Extremely loyal to Maou, he takes care of the domestic duties at home and goes to the library to research ways for Maou and himself to regain their powers. Back in Ente Isla, Alciel was known widely as the right hand of King Satan and a master strategist, making him both a trusted adviser and top military commander to the ruler of the Demon Realm. However, he shared his leader''s belief that humans lives are meaningless and expendable, considering demonkind to be superior beings and showing a strong sense of pride bordering on extreme arrogance. While living in Japan, Ashiya has come to accept his rather mundane life, though he still openly laments how low they have fallen since arriving on Earth, and still tends to consider humans as beneath him. Due to their lack of sufficient funds and personal comforts, Ashiya has become incredibly tightfisted and strict about the household budget. One part of him that has not changed, though, is his extreme dedication and loyalty to the Demon King. (Source: Hataraku Maou-sama Wikia, edited)', '/uploads/images/c_70737.png'),
(54, 'Chiho Sasaki', '佐々木千穂', '主角', 'Nao Touyama', 'Chiho is Maou''s friend and a fellow employee at MgRonald''s. She has a crush on Maou. She can hear and understand the language of Ente Isla, after receiving feedback from a hypnosis spell that Maou cast on her father, Inspector Sasaki. She has a strong will and a polite, friendly, pleasant all around personality. She is head over heels for Maou, and sometimes gets jealous when she sees Emi and Maou together. She is a part-time employee at MgRonald''s along with Maou. Maou had met her father when he first landed on Earth, as her father is a policeman and caught him and Ashiya loitering around. Chiho attends school at Sasahata North High School. (Source: Hataraku Maou-sama Wikia)', '/uploads/images/c_70739.png'),
(54, 'Mayumi Kisaki', '木崎真弓', '配角', 'Yumi Uchiyama', 'She is Maou''s immediate superior at MgRonalds where he works.', '/uploads/images/c_82295.jpg'),
(54, 'Lucifer', 'ルシフェル', '主角', 'Hiro Shimono', 'Lucifer is a fallen angel and one of the Demon King''s generals. After his defeat at the hands of Hero Emilia, he was secretly rescued by Olba Meyer, who promised to return Lucifer to heaven if they became allies in defeating the Demon Lord. After being defeated by the Demon Lord, Urushihara moved in with Sadao Maou and Ashiya. Lucifer is shown to be cunning and sneaky as well as a childish, preferring to surf the internet and play video games rather than help Ashiya with the housework. Due to his attitude, everyone tends to treat him lightly and pay no mind to many of his protests at being excluded from things. Lucifer is also self-proclaimed socially awkward, lazy to an extent, and has a short temper. However, it seems he has hidden feelings beneath his seemingly irresponsible and carefree attitude, and shows his serious side from time to time. To his irritation, Lucifer is usually referred to as a hikikomori even when among company. ~!Known as the "original sin" and the son of Ignora, Lucifer was born after the destruction of the angels'' home-world, making him part of the second generation of his kind. Once an honored and revered archangel, he was tasked with the responsibility of leading the archangels. Lucifer eventually abandoned his job, feeling it was too boring in heaven for him to remain. Losing his former status and gaining black wings signifying his corruption, his powers became demonic, reclassifying him a fallen angel. Lucifer traveled to the Demon Realm where he', '/uploads/images/c_83103.png'),
(54, 'Crestia Bell', 'クレスティア・ベル', '主角', 'Kanae Itou', 'She is the chief interrogator and executioner for the Church Investigation Commission, who came into the human realm from Ente Isla to check on reports about Emi''s alliance with Maou. Unknown to Maou who she is, she becomes his next door neighbor and eventually became close, being a good cook she would drop by in Maou''s apartment to prepare meals for everyone. She knows little about the human realm especially in Tokyo that she is having difficulty going around the city and understanding people''s sense of fashion. ~! It seems since the start that Maou and Lucifer knew who she was. !~ (Source: Animefreak)', '/uploads/images/c_83105.jpg'),
(54, 'Miki Shiba', '志波美輝', '配角', 'Kimiko Saitou', '**Miki** is the landlord at the place the Devil King stays, "Villa Rosa Sasazuka". She requested that her apartment be rented out to "shady characters" such as Maou and Alciel. She seems to have some knowledge of Ente Isla. ~!She is a guardian of the Earth and is thought to be incredibly powerful to the point where Sariel and Gabriel did not strike Villa Rosa Sasazuka out of fear of provoking her. She is older than any known archangels in history.!~ (Source: Hataraku Maou-sama Wikia)', '/uploads/images/c_83461.png'),
(54, 'Rika Suzuki', '鈴木梨香', '配角', 'Asuka Nishi', 'Emi''s coworker.', '/uploads/images/c_83463.png'),
(54, 'Emeralda Etuva', 'エメラダ・エトゥーヴァ', '配角', 'Azumi Asakura', 'Emi''s friend from Ente Isla.', '/uploads/images/c_83465.png'),
(54, 'Albert Ende', 'アルバート・エンデ', '配角', 'Hiroki Yasumoto', 'One of the comrades of Yusa, Emi on attacking the Dark Lord''s castle.', '/uploads/images/c_83467.png'),
(54, 'Olba Meyer', 'オルバ・メイヤー', '配角', 'Katsuhisa Houki', '~!He is an ambitious high member of the church who came into the human world with Hanzou to seek and eliminate both Maou and Emi, so that he can be the sole ruler of Ente Isla.!~ (Source: ANN)', '/uploads/images/c_83469.png'),
(54, 'Nord Justina', 'ノルド・ユスティーナ', '配角', 'Atsushi Ono', '[Emilia''s](https://anilist.co/character/70735) father. ~!He was thought to be dead, but it was revealed that he has been hiding in Japan under the name Sato Hiroshi!~', '/uploads/images/c_83471.png'),
(54, 'Senichi Sasaki', '佐々木千一', '配角', 'Haruo Yamagishi', 'Chiho''s father.', '/uploads/images/c_83603.png'),
(54, 'Riho Sasaki', '佐々木里穂', '配角', 'Takako Honda', 'Chiho''s mother.', '/uploads/images/c_83605.png'),
(54, 'Kaori Shouji', '東海林佳織', '配角', 'Haruka Yamazaki', 'Chiho''s classmate, who seemly has an affinity for boy''s love.', '/uploads/images/c_83887.png'),
(54, 'Robertio Iguno Valentia', 'ロベルティオ・イグノ・ヴァレンティア', '配角', 'Yutaka Nakano', 'One of the Chief Inquisitors of The Church on Ente Isla.', '/uploads/images/c_83889.png'),
(54, 'Servantes Reberiz', 'セルヴァンテス・レベリーズ', '配角', 'Yukihiro Misono', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_83891.png'),
(54, 'Mitsuki Sarue', '猿江三月', '配角', 'Yuuichi Iguchi', 'He was introduced in ep. 8 as the manager of Sentucky Fired Chicken or SFC, MgRonald''s rival fast food chain in Hatagaya district. He apparently has a thing for beautiful girls. ~!His true identity is the archangel Sariel, who came to Japan to retrieve Emi''s sword, "Better Half".!~', '/uploads/images/c_84873.png'),
(54, 'Watanabe', '渡辺', '配角', 'Yasuhiro Mamiya', 'Sadao''s acquaintance. Sadao met him while volunteering on the Neighborhood Cleanup.', '/uploads/images/c_85359.png'),
(54, 'Kawachi', 'カワッチ', '配角', 'Eiji Takeuchi', '**First appearance:** Episode 9.', '/uploads/images/c_85361.png'),
(54, 'Yuki Mizushima', '水島由姫', '配角', 'Mamiko Noto', '**First appearance:** Episode 10 as the Manager of MgRonalds at the Fushima Park branch.', '/uploads/images/c_86071.png'),
(54, 'Kuryuu', '九流', '配角', 'Kenta Miyake', '**First appearance:** Episode 13.', '/uploads/images/c_87387.png'),
(54, 'Tamura', '田村', '配角', 'Hironori Saitou', '**First appearance:** Episode 13.', '/uploads/images/c_87389.png'),
(55, 'Narrator', 'ナレーター', '配角', 'Marina Inoue', 'This character page is set to represent and list all narrators, which haven''t been given a visual representation of themselves in their respective work. Please add other narrator characters, which were given a visual representation of themselves, separately from this narrator page.', '/uploads/images/c_36309.jpg'),
(55, 'Mikasa Ackerman', 'ミカサ・アッカーマン', '主角', 'Yui Ishikawa', '__Height:__ 170 cm (5''7") - 176 cm (5''9½") __Position:__ 104th Training Corps, Survey Corps __Relatives:__ [Birth Mother](https://anilist.co/character/84341/Mikasa-no-Haha) (Deceased), [Birth Father](https://anilist.co/character/84339/Mikasa-no-Chichi) (Deceased), [Grisha Yaeger](https://anilist.co/character/62477/Grisha-Yeager) (Foster Father), [Carla Yaeger](https://anilist.co/character/62475/Carla-Yeager) (Foster Mother, Deceased), [Eren Yeager](https://anilist.co/character/40882/Eren-Yeager) (Foster Brother) Mikasa is Eren Yaeger''s foster sister and mutual childhood friend of [Armin Arlert](https://anilist.co/character/46494), living with the two of them in Shiganshina District within the southern region of Wall Maria. When she was young, her parents were killed by human traffickers, and she was kidnapped. Eren discovered this and helped her escape her captors. Later, Eren gave her his scarf, which she constantly wears and shares an emotional attachment to. She was adopted by the Yaeger family soon after. Because of these past events, Mikasa shares an unbreakable bond with Eren and lives to protect him, constantly worrying for Eren''s well-being. After the Titans broke through Wall Maria and killed her and Eren''s mother, she chose to follow Eren into the military to try and keep him safe from danger. Even as a child, Mikasa possessed impressive fighting skill and strength, and that skill was only honed further during her training. Mikasa is considered a genius among all th', '/uploads/images/c_40881.png'),
(55, 'Eren Yeager', 'エレン・イェーガー', '主角', 'Yuuki Kaji', '__Height:__ 170 cm (5''7") - 183 cm (6''0") __Affiliation:__ 104th Trainees Squad, Survey Corps. Eren was born to [Carla](https://anilist.co/character/62475/Yeager-Carla) and [Grisha Yeager](https://anilist.co/character/62477/Yeager-Grisha) in Shiganshina District within the southern region of Wall Maria. He grew up in the town with his parents and foster sister [Mikasa](https://anilist.co/character/40881/Ackerman-Mikasa), who moved in with the Yeagers as a child. Eren spent most of his time with Mikasa and their mutual best friend [Armin Arlert](https://anilist.co/character/46494/Arlert-Armin), whom the pair often defended from neighborhood bullies. Eren is a passionate, determined, hardheaded, and impulsive young man. When they were children, Armin showed him a book depicting the wonders of the outside world. Eren grew to share Armin''s curiosity of the world beyond the Walls and resolved to see it for himself. This dream inspired his admiration of the Survey Corps and his desire to join their ranks as soon as he became eligible for enrollment. When the Titans suddenly broke through Wall Maria into Shiganshina, Eren was forced to watch on as his mother became trapped under the rubble of their house and eaten by a titan. Forever changed from this event, Eren vows to kill every last titan.', '/uploads/images/c_40882.jpg'),
(55, 'Levi', 'リヴァイ', '配角', 'Hiroshi Kamiya', '__Height:__ 160 cm (5''3") Squad Captain of the Special Operations Squad (known as Squad Levi) within the Survey Corps. He is known as humanity''s strongest soldier. Levi is abrasive, blunt, and has a strong respect for structure and discipline. He is a clean-freak, demanding spotless cleanliness of himself, his equipment, and his environment. Rumors say he was involved in underground crime in his life before coming a soldier. Despite his emotionless and unfriendly demeanor, Levi cares deeply for his squad and greatly values human life.', '/uploads/images/c_45627.png'),
(55, 'Sasha Blouse', 'サシャ・ブラウス', '配角', 'Yuu Kobayashi', '__Initial Height:__ 168cm __Affiliations__: 104th Cadet Corps, Survey Corps; Soldier __Relatives__: [Artur Blouse](https://anilist.co/character/131281/Artur-Blouse) (Father), [Lisa Blouse](https://anilist.co/character/134952/Lisa-Blouse) (Mother) Originally from Dauper, a remote and scarcely populated village of hunters located in a mountain forest in the southern area of Wall Rose, Sasha joined the military as a cadet of the 104th Training Corps, where she ranked 9th upon graduation. After graduating, she''d choose to enlist in the Scouting Regiment. Sasha is a friendly and fun-loving girl. She speaks with a local accent from her home village, but initially hid it out of embarrassment by using overly formal and polite speech. She is a constant food hoarder and is known to have an incredible appetite; eating provided her with considerable gratification and relief, especially during times of great stress, and food was often the only thing on her mind when at ease. Raised as an animal hunter, Sasha specializes in archery, horseback riding, and tracking, although her eccentricity and unconventional methods tend to make her a poor fit for group operations. ~!She later saves a child named [Kaya](https://anilist.co/character/132738/Kaya) from a titan attack, who her family ends up adopting.!~', '/uploads/images/c_45887.jpg'),
(55, 'Reiner Braun', 'ライナー・ブラウン', '配角', 'Yoshimasa Hosoya', '__Height__: 185 cm (6''1") Member of the Survey Corps and former cadet of the 104th Training Corps. Reiner is a passionate and strong-willed young man with a strong sense of duty. He ranked 2nd in his training class upon graduation, finishing behind only [Mikasa](https://anilist.co/character/40881). His comrades have great trust in him, and he is stated to be the "big brother" of the 104th cadets.', '/uploads/images/c_46484.png'),
(55, 'Connie Springer', 'コニー・スプリンガー', '配角', 'Hiro Shimono', '__Height__: 158 cm (5''2") __Relatives:__ [Mother](https://anilist.co/character/137287/Conny-no-Haha), Martin Springer (Brother), Sunny Springer (Sister) Connie Springer is a graduate of the 104th Training Corps, having ranked 8th in class. He is known to be one of the quickest soldiers while using ODM gear and is skilled at making very sharp turns. He hails from the rural Ragako Village within Wall Rose, his greatest ambition being to make his family and village proud of him. Upon graduation, he chose to join the Survey Corps. Upbeat and naive, Connie is rather unfocused outside of combat, and enjoys goofing around and messing with his friends, but can also be a bit dense at times, as he can have some difficulty comprehending new developments as they appear. Connie always tries to remain optimistic, consistently caring for the well-being of his friends, family and village, and being willing to help in any way he can. However, this soft spot and the struggles he goes through as a member of the Survey Corps takes a toll on him, as he often responds to grief and loss with anger, irritation and hatred, causing him to at times make rash, impulsive decisions. He will do anything to protect his family, whether it be his biological family or his closest friends.', '/uploads/images/c_46486.png'),
(55, 'Bertolt Hoover', 'ベルトルト・フーバー', '配角', 'Tomohisa Hashizume', '__Height__: 192 cm (6''3") __Affiliation__: Survey Corps Member of the Survey Corps and former cadet of the 104th Training Corps. Bertoldt ranked 3rd in his training class upon graduation, finishing behind only [Mikasa](https://anilist.co/character/40881) and his hometown friend [Reiner](https://anilist.co/character/46484). He is a quiet young man who identifies himself as someone with a weak will that follows popular opinion. Despite ranking 3rd in his class, his training commandant noted him to be a person with great potential, but an utter lack of initiative. Bertoldt originally he enlisted in the military with aspirations of joining the Military Police and living in the safety of the inner wall, but after the Battle of Trost he instead decided to join the Survey Corps.', '/uploads/images/c_46488.jpg'),
(55, 'Annie Leonhart', 'アニ・レオンハート', '配角', 'Yuu Shimamura', '__Height__: 153 cm (5") A member of the 104th Southern Division in the Cadet Corps. After graduating from the 104th, ranked 4th place in the top 10, she ends up joining the Military Police. She is roommates with [Hitch Dreyse](https://anilist.co/character/86017). A stoic girl, Annie is considered to be an isolated, solitary type, being rarely seen smiling or socializing and often having an emotionless expression. She is apathetic and somnolent, with little desire to put in any effort into meaningless disciplines or activities. Nonetheless, what drives Annie more than anything is her desire for a normal life.', '/uploads/images/c_46490.jpg'),
(55, 'Hannes', 'ハンネス', '配角', 'Keiji Fujiwara', 'A soldier who saves Eren and Mikasa during the prologue. He owes a debt to the Yeager family.', '/uploads/images/c_46492.jpg'),
(55, 'Armin Arlert', 'アルミン・アルレルト', '主角', 'Marina Inoue', '__Height:__ 163 cm (5''4") __Position:__ 104th Trainees Squad, Survey Corps __Relatives:__ [Grandfather](https://anilist.co/character/84313/Armin-no-Ojiisan) Armin is a young boy who was born and raised in the Shiganshina District within the walls, being childhood friends with both [Eren Yeager](https://anilist.co/character/40882/Eren-Yeager) and [Mikasa Ackerman](https://anilist.co/character/40881). After Wall Maria was breached, he chose to join Mikasa and Eren in joining the military, both to try to make a good and meaningful impact on the world, and to fulfill his dream of seeing the outside world. Even when he was young, the naturally curious Armin has always had a deep fascination with the world beyond the Walls. As a child, he found and studied an illegal book about the outside world that was owned by his grandfather. He often shared the book and information contained in it with Eren Yeager, his best friend, and his dreams of seeing the world outside the walls. Armin was branded a heretic by other children for his unusual interest in the outside world and was thus frequently picked on. Too timid to defend himself, Armin would often rely on his friends Eren and Mikasa Ackerman to protect him from local bullies. This, coupled with his frail physique, was a deep shame for Armin, leading him to have poor self-esteem and to believe that he is a burden to others. Because of this, Armin has always been very eager to prove his worth, especially towards his close friends. Armin ', '/uploads/images/c_46494.png'),
(55, 'Erwin Smith', 'エルヴィン・スミス', '配角', 'Daisuke Ono', '**Height:** 188 cm **Position:** 13th Commander, Survey Corps Discerning, intelligent, and widely respected, Erwin is the unshakable and calculated 13th commander of the Survey Corps. While he cares deeply for his men, he does not hesitate to sacrifice them for the good and prosperity of mankind, and his men have proven more than willing to stake their lives at his order. Erwin developed the Long-Distance Enemy Scouting Formation.', '/uploads/images/c_46496.png'),
(55, 'Jean Kirstein', 'ジャン・キルシュタイン', '配角', 'Kishou Taniyama', '__Height__: 175 cm (5''8") __Relatives__: [Mother](https://anilist.co/character/131444/Jean-no-Haha) Jean Kirschtein is a graduate of the 104th Cadet Corps, among whom he ranked 6th for his skills with ODM gear and ability to look at things through a more tactical lense. Jean hails from Wall Rose''s Trost District, and joined the military with hopes of living a peaceful life within the walls as part of the Military Police. However, he would later find himself joining the Survey Corps after being convinced both by his close friend [Marco Bott''s](https://anilist.co/character/62479/Marco-Bott) words, and after witnessing the death of several of his comrades. Jean has a blunt personality. He holds no restraint when it comes to speaking his mind, even when he knows it would not be wise to do so or when it could spark conflict. Jean is also pragmatic: he has a strong aversion to exposing himself to dangerous situations. During his time as a cadet, Jean was extremely hot-headed, easily becoming frustrated and quick to resort to violence when pushed. Jean was also very cynical about defeating the Titans, believing that humanity has no chance against them and openly mocking more idealistic individuals like [Eren Yeager](https://anilist.co/character/40882/Eren-Yeager), and saw resisting the Titans as a hopeless cause. However, despite these things, and although he presents himself as self-centered, Jean places high value on the lives of his comrades, and is willing to risk his life to pr', '/uploads/images/c_46498.png'),
(55, 'Carla Yeager', 'カルラ・イェーガー', '配角', 'Yoshino Takamori', 'Eren''s mother. ~!She''s eaten alive in the second chapter.!~ Note: Carla Yeager is the official English translation by Kodansha.', '/uploads/images/c_62475.png'),
(55, 'Grisha Yeager', 'グリシャ・イェーガー', '配角', 'Hiroshi Tsuchida', 'Father of [Eren Yaeger](https://anilist.co/character/40882/Eren-Yeager) and caretaker of [Mikasa Ackerman](https://anilist.co/character/40881/Mikasa-Ackerman). He is a renowned doctor who was well respected in the District of Shiganshina after he saved the village from a mysterious viral epidemic by developing vaccines. He also provides a medical house call service to the people of Shiganshina and to various towns in addition to having a network of contacts within the Corps of the Shiganshina District. He is married to [Carla Yaeger](https://anilist.co/character/62475). ~!In the basement of the Yeager family house, he hides a secret which he refers to as the "truth". Upon finding Eren after the fall of Wall Maria, he injects him with a series of chemicals and amnesiacs and entrusts him with the key to the "truth", before mysteriously disappearing. This strange serum resulted in Eren gaining the ability to transform into a titan.!~', '/uploads/images/c_62477.jpg'),
(55, 'Marco Bott', 'マルコ・ボット', '配角', 'Ryouta Oosaka', '__Height__: 178 cm (5''9") __Affiliations__: 104th Training Corps Originally from Jinae District. Marco ranked 7th in the 104th Training Corps and is widely respected by other cadets of the 104th. Marco is a very kind, calm, and idealistic person, valuing the good of the group above his own interests, as well as understanding and coping with his own shortcomings and limitations. He is seen as a natural leader, and desires to join the Military Police to serve near the King. *Note: Marco Bott is the official English translation by Kodansha.*', '/uploads/images/c_62479.jpg'),
(55, 'Krista Lenz', 'クリスタ・レンズ', '配角', 'Shiori Mikami', '__Height__: 145 cm (4''8") __Affiliations__: 104th Trainees Squad, Survey Corps Ranked tenth in the trainee class, Krista is a very shy and kind, caring person, often being described as a "goddess" or "angel" by her peers. She is good friends with [Ymir](https://anilist.co/character/71479/Ymir).', '/uploads/images/c_62481.png'),
(55, 'Thomas Wagner', 'トーマス・ワグナー', '配角', 'Shigeyuki Susaki', 'Thomas Wagner was from Trost District. A member of the 104th Trainees Squad, he first met Eren Yeager while questioning him about the Colossal Titan. Later, he operated the training gear for the Three Dimensional Maneuver Gear during Eren''s second attempt at his aptitude test. At Keith Shadis'' orders, Thomas exchanged gear with Eren and it was discovered that Eren''s gear was defective. After graduating, Thomas planned to join the Scouting Legion. ~!After the second attack of the Colossal Titan, he was assigned to the middle guard along with Eren Yeager and Armin Arlert. Initially tasked with working under the training corps, they eventually were incorporated into the front guard due to the number of titans. Catching the group unaware, a titan lunged at the rooftop they were standing on. The group scattered but unfortunately, Thomas wasn''t fast enough. He was caught and swallowed whole, while his teammate, Eren, looked on in terror.!~', '/uploads/images/c_62483.png'),
(55, 'Dot Pixis', 'ドット・ピクシス', '配角', 'Masahiko Tanaka', 'The highest-ranked Administrator of the Southern Region. Head of the Garrison''s Southern Territories, Pixis is a cunning leader with astute insights. However, he is also an alcoholic who is constantly watched over by his aid, [Anka](https://anilist.co/character/84331/Anka-Rheinberger), who constantly scolds him for sleeping and drinking during critical moments.', '/uploads/images/c_62485.png'),
(55, 'Petra Ral', 'ペトラ・ラル', '配角', 'Natsuki Aikawa', '__Height:__ 158 cm (5''2") __Affiliation:__ Survey Corps; Soldier, Special Operations Squad. __Relatives:__ [Father](https://anilist.co/character/131987/Petra-no-Chichi) Petra Ral is a soldier of the Survey Corps hand-picked by [Captain Levi](https://anilist.co/character/45627/Levi) to join the Special Operations Squad. Petra is a very kind and caring woman, going out of her way to look after and guiding [Eren Yaeger](https://anilist.co/character/40882/Eren-Yeager) when he was first admitted to the squad. She seemed to have the most attachment to Eren among Levi Squad, as she was often the only one shown to actually worry about him and his wellbeing, at least at first. Although all of Levi''s squad wished for Eren''s unconditional trust, it was ultimately Petra who convinced him to do so. Despite her kind nature, Petra was a conditioned soldier with a quick reaction time against perceived danger. She displays extreme loyalty to her leaders, superiors and their orders, and cares deeply for her team, although she tends to be at odds with [Oluo Bozad](https://anilist.co/character/71687/Oluo-Bozard) due to his irritating tendency to try and imitate Levi. She greatly looks up to Levi as her superior and is deeply devoted to him, willing to completely dedicate her life to his cause. It is implied that she may harbor romantic feelings for her captain.', '/uploads/images/c_62501.jpg'),
(55, 'Mike Zacharias', 'マイク・ザカリアス', '配角', 'Kenta Miyake', 'Squad Captain of his own squad, Squad Mike, a major division within the Survey Corps. He has been described by others as "humanity''s second strongest soldier", being only behind [Levi](https://anilist.co/character/45627/Levi). Mike is an extremely strong and durable soldier and an acknowledged leader with a brave heart and a tactical mind. He also has a remarkably good sense of smell, which allows him to detect Titans from great distances. During times of ease, Mike is shown to be a quiet and reserved man, rarely speaking unless it concerned a more serious matter. He also has a bizarre habit of "sniffing" people when he meets them.', '/uploads/images/c_71119.jpg'),
(55, 'Hange Zoe', 'ハンジ・ゾエ', '配角', 'Romi Park', '__Height:__ 170 cm (5''7") __Affiliation:__ Survey Corps; Section Commander, Squad Leader. Leader of the Survey Corps'' Fourth Squad, Hange is also in charge of conducting research on Titans, and pursues this knowledge so passionately that they have become obsessed with Titans as a result. After originally holding a deep hatred for the creatures, Hange decided to take on a new outside-the-box approach to their research by letting go of their resentment towards Titans and approaching the test subjects with compassion. Hange is an energetic, freethinking and quirky scientist, with a unique way of conducting both themselves and their work. Hange is a genius outside of just Titan research too, using their brain to create weapons, tactical plans, and inventions for the benefit of humanity. As a leader, Hange is thoughtful of their comrades, and can easily figure out complex problems in order to create plans for their teammates to carry out.', '/uploads/images/c_71121.png'),
(55, 'Nile Dok', 'ナイル・ドーク', '配角', 'Anri Katsu', 'Chief of the Military Police.', '/uploads/images/c_71123.png'),
(55, 'Darius Zackly', 'ダリス・ザックレー', '配角', 'Hideaki Tezuka', 'The head of all three divisions of the army. __ _Note:___ Darius Zackly is the official English translation by Kodansha.', '/uploads/images/c_71125.png'),
(55, 'Nick', 'ニック', '配角', 'Tomohisa Asou', 'Pastor Nick is a member of a religion that worships the Walls as holy. He claims that he lost his family as a result of addiction to Vine. As a religious leader, Pastor Nick used his influence to oppose any modification of the walls, be it permanently sealing the gates or even mounting cannons on the top. Though he claimed it was blasphemy for humans to "maim" the wall, ~!the real reason was to reduce the risk of workers discovering the Titans within during renovations.!~ (Source: Shingeki no Kyojin Wikia) Note: Minister Nick is the official English translation by Kodansha.', '/uploads/images/c_71453.jpg'),
(55, 'Marlo Freudenberg', 'マルロ・フロイデンベルク', '配角', 'Tomokazu Sugita', '__Affiliations:__ Military Police, 104th Cadet Corps. Recruit of the Military Police stationed in Stohess District. While most who join the Military Police Regiment do so because they want a safe position far from the danger of the Titans, Marlo did so because he claims to want "to uphold justice and do what''s right.", much to the amusement of his fellow officer, [Hitch Dreyse](https://anilist.co/character/86017/Hitch-Dreyse), whom he often clashes with due to them being near complete opposites. His goal is to rise to the top of the organization so he can stop the pilfering of taxes and misappropriation of land. Though steadfast in his idealism, he could make moral compromises to achieve his goal, confessing a willingness to act like "scum" in order to move up in rank. Due to his passion towards his ideals, he had often been compared to [Eren Yeager](https://anilist.co/character/40882/Eren-Yeager) by people who know both of them.', '/uploads/images/c_71457.png'),
(55, 'Dieter Ness', 'ディータ・ネス', '配角', 'Kouichi Sakaguchi', 'A member of the Scout Regiment and a team leader in the 57th Exterior Scouting Mission. ~!He encounters the Female Titan, who catches Ness''s line and whips it to the ground, killing him instantly.!~', '/uploads/images/c_71459.jpg'),
(55, 'Luke Siss', 'ルーク・シス', '配角', 'Masamichi Kitada', 'Luke Siss was a skilled member of the Survey Corps and a participant during the 57th Expedition Outside the Walls.', '/uploads/images/c_71461.jpg'),
(55, 'Ymir', 'ユミル', '配角', 'Saki Fujita', '__Height:__ 172 cm (5''7") __Affiliations:__ 104th Trainees Squad, Scouting Legion Member of the Scouting Legion. She seems selfish, cynical, bossy, sly, uncooperative, exploitative, and confrontational, but she can apparently be kind, especially to [Krista](https://anilist.co/character/62481/Krista-Lenz).', '/uploads/images/c_71479.png'),
(55, 'Nanaba', 'ナナバ', '配角', 'Asami Shimoda', '__Height:__ 172 cm __Affiliation:__ Scouting Legion Survey Corps', '/uploads/images/c_71481.png'),
(55, 'Oluo Bozard', 'オルオ・ボザド', '配角', 'Shinji Kawada', '__Height:__ 173 cm (5''8") __Affiliations:__ Survey Corps; Soldier, Special Operations Squad __Relatives:__ [Mother](https://anilist.co/character/131991/Oluo-no-Haha), [Father](https://anilist.co/character/131994/Oluo-no-Chichi), Several Siblings. Oruo Bozad is a soldier of the Survey Corps hand-picked by [Captain Levi](https://anilist.co/character/45627/Levi) for the Special Operations Squad for his especially high Titan kill record. Oruo is a very self-confident, outspoken individual, and enjoys boasting about his own prowess. Despite his obnoxious demeanor, he is admittedly one of the best out of Levi Squad; having the highest kill count out of his peers, bested only by Levi. This only helps fuel his haughty nature. Though Oruo tries to come across as self-important, his cockiness is rarely taken seriously, and he is also shown to be somewhat clumsy, frequently biting his own tongue on accident while riding horses. Oruo also frequently attempts to imitate Levi, such as his rough speech and confident attitude, much to the frustration of one of his fellow teammates, [Petra Ral](https://anilist.co/character/62501).', '/uploads/images/c_71687.png'),
(55, 'Eld Gin', 'エルド・ジン', '配角', 'Susumu Chiba', '__Height:__ 182 cm (6''0") Eld Gin is an elite soldier in the Survey Corps. He was hand-picked by [Captain Levi](https://anilist.co/character/45627/Levi) and placed in the Special Operations Squad, of which he is second-in-command. Eld is a responsible and firm leader with a strong sense of duty. He does not talk much, but when he does, he did so bluntly and in a straightforward manner. He also seems to have been a veteran of sorts as he teased [Petra Ral](https://anilist.co/character/62501) and [Oluo Bozad](https://anilist.co/character/71687/Oluo-Bozard) about how they acted during their first expedition. He also seems to hold some sort of belief of what makes a true soldier, saying that a kill record alone does not make a great soldier.', '/uploads/images/c_71689.png'),
(55, 'Gunther Schultz', 'グンタ・シュルツ', '配角', 'Kouzou Mito', '__Height:__ 183 cm (6''0") __Relatives:__ [Mother](https://anilist.co/character/131990/Gunther-no-Haha), [Grandfather](https://anilist.co/character/131986/Gunther-no-Ojsan). Gunther Schultz is one of the Survey Corps soldiers hand-picked by [Captain Levi](https://anilist.co/character/45627/Levi) to join the Special Operations Squad, both for his strength and his distrust for [Eren Yaeger](https://anilist.co/character/40882/Eren-Yeager). Being a soldier of the Survey Corps who survived multiple encounters with Titans significantly affected Gunther''s personality, making him deeply obedient and loyal to his superiors. Within the Special Operations Squad, Gunther seems to be the most reasonable one. However, he is shown to get irritated when his comrades joke around with one another, showing he also possesses a stern side and does not take kindly if a soldier doesn''t focus on the task at hand.', '/uploads/images/c_71691.png'),
(55, 'Mina Carolina', 'ミーナ・カロライナ', '配角', 'Chika Anzai', 'Mina appears in Ch. 3. When the Colossal Titan appears outside Trost District, the burst of steam from its body knocks a number of trainees off the Wall. She follows when Eren instructs the other trainees to attack the Colossal Titan. After the second attack of the Colossal Titan, she was assigned to the middle guard along with Eren Yeager and Armin Arlert. Initially tasked with working under the training corps, they eventually were incorporated into the front guard due to the number of titans. Catching the group unaware, a titan lunged at the roof top they were standing on. When Eren was talking about how killing titans that got in Trost District will get their rank up high, she joined him indicating that she is also signing up for Scouting Legion. ~! After Eren''s leg got bitten off by one of the titans, She and the other two tries to kill the titan that is responible for biting off Eren''s leg. However, her Three Dimensional Maneuver Gear''s wire was caught by titan''s hand and was knocked over to the wall. When she found out where she was, it was too late for her to escape. She was caught by another titan and her face got bitten off. !~', '/uploads/images/c_83181.png'),
(55, 'Keith Shadis', 'キース・シャーディス', '配角', 'Tsuguo Mogami', 'Keith Shadis was the head instructor of the 104th Trainees Squad. He seemed to be a friend or have some sort of relationship with Dr. Grisha, as he knew Eren is the son of the doctor and praised Eren for his effort.', '/uploads/images/c_84305.png'),
(55, 'Hugo', 'フーゴ', '配角', 'Akio Suyama', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_84307.jpg'),
(55, 'Moses', 'モーゼス', '配角', 'Takuya Masumoto', 'He was a member of the Scouting Legion and was the first person killed by a Titan at the start of the series. When the Recon Corps squad returns to the District of Shiganshina, his mother starts asking for him, and the Squad leader, gives her all that remained of him- his right arm. In the manga his name is Brown (ブラウン), although it is changed to Moses in the anime. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_84309.png'),
(55, 'Moses no Haha', 'モーゼスの母', '配角', 'Kyouko Terase', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_84311.png'),
(55, 'Armin no Ojii-san', 'アルミンのお祖父さん', '配角', 'Masaharu Satou', 'The paternal grandfather of Armin Arlert. Before the fall of Wall Maria, He possessed a book containing illegal information about the world beyond the Walls. He gave this book to his grandson, Armin Arlert, who showed it to his best friend Eren, kindling his desire to see the outside world', '/uploads/images/c_84313.jpg'),
(55, 'Samuel Linke-Jackson ', 'サムエル・リンケ-ジャクソン', '配角', 'Kenji Takahashi', 'Samuel is a member of the 104th Trainees Squad. He appears in Ch. 3. When the Colossal Titan appears outside Trost District, the burst of steam from its body knocks a number of trainees off the Wall. While most are able to switch to their Three Dimensional Maneuver Gear and anchor themselves to the Wall, Samuel is struck in the head by a piece of falling rock and stunned. Sasha saves him from falling to his death by firing one of her grappling hooks into his leg. Eren tells Sasha to take Samuel somewhere safe, then instructs the other trainees to attack the Colossal Titan. ~!He is killed by Connie after being shot three times in the head.!~', '/uploads/images/c_84315.png'),
(55, 'Franz Kefka', 'フランツ・ケフカ', '配角', 'Kenta Ookuma', 'Franz is a member of the 104th Trainees Squad. Franz first appears Ch.3 in walking through Trost District with Eren and Hannah. Eren refers to Hannah and Franz as a couple, which they both embarrassedly deny. ~!At some point following the breach of the Wall by the Colossal Titan, Franz is attacked by a Titan. He is bitten in half and dies. Armin finds Hannah futilely attempting CPR on what remains of Franz''s corpse. He tells her it''s useless, and advises her to retreat to the Wall before it''s too late.!~ (Source: Shingeki no Kyojin Wikia)', '/uploads/images/c_84317.png'),
(55, 'Hannah Diament', 'ハンナ・ディアマント', '配角', 'Megumi Satou', 'Hannah is a member of the 104th Trainees Squad. Hannah first appears in Ch. 3 walking through Trost District with Eren and Franz. Eren refers to Hannah and Franz as a couple, which they both embarrassedly deny.', '/uploads/images/c_84319.png'),
(55, 'Daz', 'ダズ', '配角', 'Shuuhei Takubo', 'Daz is a member of the 104th Trainees Squad. ~!In Ch. 40, Ymir and Historia Reiss recount a story about Dazz from training. Wanting praise and recognition, Dazz undertook harsh physical training in the snowy mountains. However, he wasn''t strong enough to endure it, and nearly died. Ymir told Krista to leave him behind or her own life would be endangered; when Krista refused, Ymir used her Titan shifter powers to bring Dazz back to the camp safely. In Ch. 12, when Dot Pixis announces the plan to reconquer Trost District, Dazz has a breakdown and starts screaming that he doesn''t want to die. Though Marco Bott tries to quiet him, a commanding officer overhears and threatens to execute him. Dazz replies that execution would be better then being eaten by a Titan. However, Dot Pixis then announces that all deserters will be pardoned -- but have to live with the guilt that they abandoned their families to the Titans. Dazz is unable to leave his family to that fate, and returns to participate in the operation to plug the breach. After the mission, he briefly appears in Chapter 21 standing next to Sasha Blouse when Irvin Smith gives a speech urging the 104th Training Squad members to join the Scouting Legion. As he is not present in the group of trainees who join, he presumably opted for the Stationary Guard instead.!~ (Source: Shingeki no Kyojin Wikia)', '/uploads/images/c_84321.png'),
(55, 'Megane no Kyoukan', '眼鏡の教官', '配角', 'Yuuya Murakami', 'Instructor with glasses that first appears in episode 3 and is later seen in episode 5 teaching the 104th Corps what is known about the Titans and their origins.', '/uploads/images/c_84323.png'),
(55, 'Kitz Weilman', 'キッツ・ヴェールマン', '配角', 'Tomoyuki Shimura', 'The Captain of the Garrison''s 1st Division Elite Forces', '/uploads/images/c_84325.jpg'),
(55, 'Bart', 'バルト', '配角', 'Kousuke Takaguchi', 'Original anime character. He is a Noble in the District of Marquis and friend of Pixis, who challenges him to leisurely games of chess. In the anime, as Pixis makes to leave upon learning of the invasion of Trost in the year 850, he tries to prevent him from going to the battlefield and instead have Pixis and his men stay and protect him and his property, viewing the lowly commoners being attacked as trash. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_84327.jpg'),
(55, 'Gustav', 'グスタフ', '配角', 'Gou Shinomiya', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_84329.png'),
(55, 'Anka Rheinberger', 'アンカ・ラインベルガー', '配角', 'Ikumi Hayama', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_84331.png'),
(55, 'Ian Dietrich', 'イアン・ディートリッヒ', '配角', 'Yuuya Murakami', 'Ian is a member of the Stationary Guard in Trost District. Ian first appears in Ch. 5 after Trost District is breached by the Colossal Titan. He compliments Mikasa for killing a Titan that was attacking a group of evacuating civilians. ~!In Ch. 12, a plan is formed for Eren to use his Titan powers to seal the breach with a boulder. Ian is placed in charge of the elite squad assigned to protect Eren on his mission. When Eren loses control of his Titan form in Ch. 13, Mitabi and Rico advise Ian to abort the mission and retreat. However, Ian orders his soldiers to continue to defend Eren down to the last man, as Eren is their only hope against the Titans. In Ch. 14, Eren regains his senses due to Armin''s intervention, and Ian orders his soldiers to protect him until he reaches the breach even at the cost of their own lives. Ian uses himself as bait to lure Titans away from Eren, sacrificing his life in order to ensure the success of the mission.!~ (Source: Shingeki no Kyojin Wikia)', '/uploads/images/c_84333.png'),
(55, 'Nack Tierce', 'ナック・ティアス', '配角', 'Tomoyuki Higuchi', 'One of the graduates from the 104th Training Corps. He was a part of the 34th squad sent to support the rear vanguard during the invasion of Trost. He was killed after the squad was ambushed by a group of Titans. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_84335.png'),
(55, 'Mylius Zeramuski', 'ミリウス・ゼルムスキー', '配角', 'Kazuhiro Fusegawa', 'One of the graduates from the 104th Training Corps. He was a part of the 34th squad sent to support the rear vanguard during the invasion of Trost. ~!He was killed after the squad was ambushed by a group of Titans.!~ (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_84337.png'),
(55, 'Mikasa no Chichi', 'ミカサの父', '配角', 'Daichi Endou', 'He and his family lived in a forest within the Shiganshina District. He seemed to be a lighthearted but hard working man. When asked by Mikasa how babies were made, he jokingly claimed he did not know and suggested she ask Dr. Jaeger when he arrives. ~!It is hinted that Mikasa''s father, or a close relative of his, was driven into poverty due to their business failing. As such, Mikasa''s father and his family lived in the woods within the Shiganshina District to avoid persecution from the government!~', '/uploads/images/c_84339.jpg'),
(55, 'Mikasa no Haha', 'ミカサの母', '配角', 'Yuuka Hirose', 'Mikasa''s mother. First Appearance Anime: Ep. 6 A woman of Oriental heritage appearing to be in her mid thirties. She appeared to be a kind and loving mother, holding value in keeping with tradition. When her and Mikasa''s lives were threatened, she quickly turned into a fierce mother, trying to do whatever was necessary to protect Mikasa.', '/uploads/images/c_84341.png'),
(55, 'Rico Brzenska', 'リコ・ブレツェンスカ', '配角', 'Michiko Kaiden', 'The Squad Leader of the 1st Division Elite Force of the Stationary Guard. ~!She is the sole survivor of the elite squads assigned to protect Eren during the liberation of Trost District. She does not trust Eren and still views him as a traitor.!~', '/uploads/images/c_84707.jpg'),
(55, 'Tom', 'トム', '配角', 'Shigeyuki Susaki', 'One of the graduates from the 104th Training Corps. During the invasion of Trost in the year 850, he was part of the squad including Jean and Mikasa whose Maneuvering Gears start to run out of propulsion fuel. As his fuel finally depletes he becomes surrounded by a group of Titans and is killed. Jean, who was in charge of the squad, capitalized on the opportunity and used him as bait to distract the Titans while the rest of the squad made their way back to the Headquarters to resupply. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_85211.jpg'),
(55, 'Hitch Dreyse', 'ヒッチ・ドリス', '配角', 'Akeno Watanabe', '**Height:** 168 cm __Affiliations:__ 104th Cadet Corps. Recruit of the Military Police stationed in Stohess District. She was roommates with [Annie Leonhart](https://anilist.co/character/46490/Annie-Leonhart). Hitch acts immature in certain ways, she has a sarcastic, easygoing personality and seems to mischievously enjoy teasing and needling her fellow officers, especially [Marlo Freudenberg](https://anilist.co/character/71457/Marlo-Freudenberg). She claims she chose to join the Military Police out of laziness, as it is well known that the senior staff are incredibly corrupt and she wanted to benefit from the system herself; however, she did not take into account that, as a new recruit, her superiors would dump all their work on her. Though she may act a bit air-headed at times, Hitch is not selfish and cares about those around her, especially her fellow comrades.', '/uploads/images/c_86017.jpg'),
(55, 'Mitabi Jarnach', 'ミタビ・ヤルナッハ', '配角', 'Takanori Hoshino', 'Mitabi Jarnach is a member of the Stationary Guard in Trost District. ~!Mitabi first appears in Ch. 13 as the leader of one of the units assigned to protect Eren on his mission to plug the breach in Trost''s Wall created by the Colossal Titan. When Eren loses control of his Titan form, Mitabi advises Ian to abort the mission and retreat to the safety of Wall Rose; however, Ian orders him to continue defending Eren. In Ch. 14, Eren regains his senses and begins carrying a boulder to plug the breach in the Wall. As there are too many Titans to fight them all, Mitabi and his men instead use themselves as bait to lure the Titans away from Eren, sacrificing their lives to ensure the success of the mission.!~ First Appearance Manga: Ch. 13 Anime: Ep. 11 (Source: Shingeki no Kyojin Wikia)', '/uploads/images/c_87385.jpg'),
(55, 'Boris Feulner', 'ボリス・フォイルナー', '配角', 'Yuuichi Karasuma', 'is a member of the Military Police stationed in Stohess District. Boris came to Annie''s defense when she got late to her duty, telling others to give her a rest. He stated that being the only one to experience the actual combat (Defense of Trost district) among her squad, Annie must be still suffering trauma from it. When Marlo tells his colleagues of his ambition to reform the Military Police, Boris tells Marlo good luck, albeit with nonchalance', '/uploads/images/c_127568.png'),
(55, 'Dimo Reeves', 'ディモ・リーブス', '配角', 'Daichi Endou', 'Dimo Reeves is a merchant that leads the company that''s named after him. He''s stationed in Trost District. ~!After the Battle of Trost, his company was assigned a mission to kidnap Eren and Historia by the Military Police Brigade.!~', '/uploads/images/c_127572.jpg'),
(55, 'Moblit Berner', 'モブリット・バーナー', '配角', 'Rintarou Nishi', '__Height:__ 176 cm (5''9") __Affiliation:__ Survey Corps; Executive Officer, Fourth Squad. A veteran member of the Survey Corps and [Hange Zoe](https://anilist.co/character/71121/Hange-Zoe)''s second-in-command within the Survey Corps'' Fourth Squad. He also serves as Hanji''s assistant and messenger. He comes across as an intelligent and responsible person, which may be the reason he was tasked to keep his overzealous and eccentric superior out of trouble. Much of the time, this leaves him in a state of near-panic, having to constantly remind Hange to be more careful or yanking them to safety. That he remains at Hange''s side constantly suggests he is a loyal person, and that he cares deeply for his superior''s safety, regardless of the stress involved with being under their command. He is also able to show signs of a serious nature when it comes to missions, going out of his way to investigate problems and put himself in danger before others.', '/uploads/images/c_127573.jpg'),
(55, 'Abel', 'ゴーグル', '配角', 'Kiyohito Yoshikai', 'Goggles is a soldier in the Scout Regiment fourth squad under the command of Hange Zoë, who is noted for his trademark glasses, or "goggles". He participated in the 57th Exterior Scouting Mission and often accompanies higher ups, such as Hange and Levi, on serious missions. (Source: Shingeki no Kyojin Wikia)', '/uploads/images/c_127681.jpg'),
(55, 'Phil', 'フィル', '配角', 'Yukari Shimotsuki', 'A member of the Garrison.', '/uploads/images/c_130625.png'),
(55, 'Dennis Aiblinger', 'デニス・アイブリンガー', '配角', 'Seirou Ogino', 'Military Police Officer stationed in the Stohess District.', '/uploads/images/c_130657.png'),
(55, 'Waltz', 'ヴァルツ', '配角', 'Ryouta Asari', 'He is a member of the Military Police Regiment who serves as Nile Dawk''s aide', '/uploads/images/c_131208.png'),
(55, 'Annie no Chichi', 'アニの父', '配角', 'Unshou Ishizuka', 'Father and trainer of Annie Leonhart. He relentlessly trained Annie to fight, using mostly kicks and the attacker''s weight against them. ~!Memories of his pleas for forgiveness later create an opening for Annie to crystallize herself before Eren Jaeger has the chance to capture her!~', '/uploads/images/c_131257.png'),
(55, 'Jurgen', 'ユルゲン', '配角', 'Kazuhiro Fusegawa', 'A member of the Scout Regiment and a participant of the 57th Exterior Scouting Mission. ~!Jurgen was a reckless man, who disobeyed his superiors and put his entire brigade in danger just to retrieve a body. This recklessness would prove to be the end of him. When his friend Ivan was killed, he showed more composure than his friend Dieter; but he still chose to disobey his superiors to retrieve his body. In his final moments, he expressed great fear and regret on his face as he was killed without even completing the task he had set out to do!~', '/uploads/images/c_131455.png'),
(55, 'Darius  Baer Walbrunn', 'ダリウス・ベーア＝ヴァルブルン ', '配角', 'Akimitsu Takase', 'A team leader of the Scout Regiment who participated in the 57th expedition beyond the Walls.', '/uploads/images/c_131456.png'),
(55, 'Dieter', 'ディター', '配角', 'Yoshihito Sasaki', 'A member of the Scout Regiment and participated in the 57th Exterior Scouting Mission. ~!Dieter appears very unconditioned and mentally cracking. He shows great distress over the death of his friend Ivan, and disobeys his superiors when they refuse his request to retrieve his body; resulting in the death of his friend Jurgen. When confronted by Captain Levi, Dieter bursts into tears, cracking under the mental stress he had endured. Though he shows passion for his friends, this passion manifests itself in the form of recklessness resulting in comrades deaths!~', '/uploads/images/c_131457.png'),
(55, 'Ivan', 'イヴァン', '配角', '', 'A member of the Scout Regiment and a participant of the 57th Exterior Scouting Mission. ~!Ivan was killed during the Scout Regiment''s 57th Expedition. As the Corps was returning to Calaneth District, two of Ivan''s friends, Dieter and Jurgen, tried, unsuccessfully, to retrieve his body to return to his family!~', '/uploads/images/c_131458.png'),
(55, 'Gunther Sofu', 'グンタ祖父', '配角', 'Shuuhei Takubo', '[Gunther](https://anilist.co/character/71691)''s grandfather.', '/uploads/images/c_131986.jpg'),
(55, 'Petra no Chichi', 'ペトラの父', '配角', 'Masaki Terasoma', 'The father of [Petra Rall](https://anilist.co/character/62501), a skilled female member of Levi''s former Special Operations Squad.', '/uploads/images/c_131987.png'),
