(64, 'Yukinari Mori', '森行成', '配角', 'Tooru Sakurai', 'A college student and a middle blocker in the Karasuno Neighborhood Association Team.', '/uploads/images/c_139525.png'),
(64, 'Asuka Hirama', '平間あすか', '配角', 'Ai Kakuma', 'One of the girls who came to cheer for Aoba Johsai, especially Oikawa, during the Interhigh Preliminary match against Karasuno. Throughout the match, she shows that she isn''t too familiar with the rules and plays of volleyball and relies on [Takinoue](https://anilist.co/character/80511/Yuusuke-Takinoue) and [Shimada](https://anilist.co/character/80513/Makoto-Shimada) to explain things to her. She would later appear during Seijoh''s rematch against Karasuno.', '/uploads/images/c_290163.jpg'),
(64, 'Manaka Ujiie', '氏家愛花', '配角', 'Haruka Terui', 'One of the girls who came to cheer for Aoba Johsai, especially [Oikawa](https://anilist.co/character/71611/Tooru-Oikawa), during the InterHigh Preliminary. Throughout the match, she shows that she isn''t too familiar with the rules and plays of volleyball and relies on [Takinoue](https://anilist.co/character/80511/Yuusuke-Takinoue) and [Shimada](https://anilist.co/character/80513/Makoto-Shimada) to explain things to her. She would later appear during Seijoh''s rematch against Karasuno.', '/uploads/images/c_290164.jpg'),
(64, 'Chizuru Sasaki', '佐々木千鶴', '配角', 'Kanami Satou', '__Uniform Number:__ 11 Third-year student at Karasuno High and wing spiker for the girls'' volleyball team. She is close friends with [Michimiya](https://anilist.co/character/77165/Yui-Michimiya) and Aihara.', '/uploads/images/c_290165.jpg'),
(64, 'Yasushi Kamasaki', '鎌先靖志', '配角', 'Takuya Satou', '__Height:__ 186.8cm (6'' 1.5") __Uniform Number:__ 1 __Position:__ Middle Blocker __Ability Parameters (out of 5):__ Power = 5; Jump = 2; Stamina = 4; Game Sense 2; Technique = 2; Speed = 4 Third-year student at Datekougyou High School. Prior to retiring, he played on the boys'' volleyball team as a middle blocker and the vice-captain. He is loud, strict, and often argues with and threatens his problematic kouhai [Futakuchi](https://anilist.co/character/77415/Kenji-Futakuchi). However, he is incredibly supportive of his team and often attends their official and practices matches with [Moniwa](https://anilist.co/character/77413/Kaname-Moniwa) and [Sasaya](https://anilist.co/character/137486/Takehito-Sasaya) after retiring.', '/uploads/images/c_290202.jpg'),
(64, 'Kyoutou', '教頭', '配角', 'Yasumichi Kushida', 'Vice Principal of Karasuno High School. He is balding and attempts to keep his head covered with a toupee. He is said to have a bad relationship with the volleyball club that has gotten worse since Hinata and Kageyama joined the club. However, once the team starts to win again, he begins supporting the club more.', '/uploads/images/c_290203.jpg'),
(64, 'Mao Aihara', '相原真緒', '配角', 'Rie Suegara', '__Uniform Number:__ 2 Third-year student at Karasuno High School. She played on the girls'' volleyball team as the team''s ace and vice-captain. She is good friends with and very supportive of [Michimiya](https://anilist.co/character/77165/Yui-Michimiya).', '/uploads/images/c_290205.jpg'),
(65, 'Joutarou Kuujou', '空条承太郎', '主角', 'Daisuke Ono', '__Height:__ 195 cm (6''5") __Occupation:__ Student, Marine Explorer, Oceanographer __Nationality:__ Japanese Joutarou is Holly Kujo''s son and [Joseph Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/6356)''s grandson. In Part 3, he has a recognizable attire of a blue trenchcoat-length school uniform jacket with yellow chains on the collar. He also wears a trademark hat which, while torn in the back, often seems to blend with his hair. When Joutarou first appears, he turned himself in to the police because he believes his Stand is an evil spirit possessing him. After he is released from jail, and learns what his Stand is, Joutarou gets used to Star Platinum -- a fierce, muscular, vaguely Aztec-looking spirit with "the precision of a machine" and the ability to destroy virtually anything with a sledgehammer barrage of fists. He has a very tough exterior, and is even rather rough and delinquent, but he also is very dedicated, intense, and loyal. He is very intelligent, but usually lets his (or Star Platinum''s) fists do the talking with the enemy, even though he often has to rely on his wits to deal with stand users'' attacks. He is also known for a quick and short temper. His catchphrase is "Yare yare daze." It generally relates of being bored or exasperation. In Part 3, he is the main target of [Dio](https://anilist.co/character/4004), who realizes that Joutarou is his greatest threat. One of the strongest stands in the JoJo universe; Star Platinum possesses super human senses, strength, sta', '/uploads/images/c_4003.png'),
(65, 'Dio Brando', 'ディオ・ブランドー', '配角', 'Takehito Koyasu', '__Height:__ 195 cm (6''5") __Race:__ Human (formerly), Vampire (onwards) __Nationality:__ British Dio is an immortal vampire and the arch rival of the Joestar clan. __Series 1: Phantom Blood__ ~!Dio is the son of [Dario Brando](https://anilist.co/character/74099/Brando-Dario), an alcoholic and abusive father. Back when Dio was just a boy, he was brought into the household of [George Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/21956/Joestar-I-George) after the mysterious death of his father, so as to repay the debt he owed Dio''s father for saving his life. But soon Dio''s personality caused trouble for George''s young son, [Jonathan Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/8087/Joestar-Jonathan). Even more of a sociopath than his father, Dio was resolute to shatter Jonathan''s spirit and take his place as the favored son, even going so far as to arrange for Jonathan''s dog [Danny](https://anilist.co/character/222601/Danny) to be burned to death. Initially, Dio is able earn the trust of the patriarch of the Joestar family through deceit (and at Jonathan''s expense). However, his plans of taking over the Joestar household were discovered by Jonathan when he discovered that not only had Dio poisoned his biological father to death, he was doing the same to his adoptive father, all to take the Joestar estate for his own. Determined not to be stopped, and understanding the potential to enjoy power over all things instead of just the Joestar estate, Dio wears and activates the Stone Mask, becoming ', '/uploads/images/c_4004.png'),
(65, 'Jean-Pierre Polnareff', 'ジャン＝ピエール・ポルナレフ', '主角', 'Fuminori Komatsu', '__Height:__ 185 cm (6''1") Jean-Pierre Polnareff is a Frenchman who joins the Joestar group on their journey to Egypt after being freed from Dio''s control by the group. He aims to avenge the murder of his sister. His brash nature and overconfidence combined with his general tomfoolery is often the source of trouble throughout the journey, and other members of the group often remark on his tendency to endanger himself and others. ~!Polnareff reappears in 2001 (Part 5), now 36 years old and wheelchair-bound, to assist [Giorno](https://anilist.co/character/10529/Giovanna-Giorno) and the rest of Passione in their fight against the boss.!~ He also serves as the inspiration for many characters in other franchises such as [Guile](https://anilist.co/character/9312/Guile) (Street Fighter), [Paul](https://anilist.co/character/285435/Phoenix-Paul) (Tekken), [Benimaru Nikaido](https://anilist.co/character/61203/Nikaido-Benimaru) (King of Fighters).', '/uploads/images/c_4368.png'),
(65, 'Joseph Joestar', 'ジョセフ・ジョースター', '主角', 'Unshou Ishizuka', '__Height__: 195 cm (6''5") Joseph Joestar begins as a young Englishman in New York, with his grandmother [Erina](https://anilist.co/character/21937). However, an attack by [Straits](https://anilist.co/character/21961) and the disappearance of [Robert Edward O Speedwagon](https://anilist.co/character/21938) soon involve him in the greater chain of events.', '/uploads/images/c_6356.png'),
(65, 'Jonathan Joestar', 'ジョナサン・ジョースター', '配角', '', '__Height:__ 195 cm __Nationality:__ British __Occupation:__ Archaeologist Born the unique son of the wealthy businessman [George Joestar I](https://anilist.co/character/21956), Jonathan is an honest, kind, and positive man whose life is fraught with tragedy after meeting his adopted older brother - and series antagonist - [Dio Brando](https://anilist.co/character/4004). In his battle against Dio, Jonathan becomes a Ripple user under the tutelage of the master [Will Anthonio Zeppeli](https://anilist.co/character/18062). **Part 5:**~!Jonathan is the biological father of [Giorno Giovanna](https://anilist.co/character/10529), the protagonist of Vento Aureo, as well as a handful of other illegitimate offspring.!~', '/uploads/images/c_8087.png'),
(65, 'Noriaki Kakyouin', '花京院典明', '主角', 'Daisuke Hirakawa', '__Height:__ 178 cm (5''10") __Stand:__ Hierophant Green Kakyoin is a high school student and user of the stand Hierophant Green. Unlike most stand users, Kakyoin was born with his stand, though it caused him to feel like an outsider for most of his life due to not knowing any other stand users. Until meeting the rest of the main characters, Hierophant was Kakyoin’s only real friend. Hierophant is not physically strong, but is elastic and can able to unravel into tentacles which can capture opponents. It can also enter an enemy’s body to possess them, though Kakyoin rarely uses this ability. Hierophant’s signature power is emerald splash, which hurls emeralds that slice opponents. Kakyoin remains calm and collected even in dangerous situations, and is good at seeing through opponents’ strategies. During a trip to Egypt with his family, he encountered [Dio](https://anilist.co/character/4004/Brando-Dio), who controlled him using a flesh bud. It was later removed by [Jotaro](https://anilist.co/character/4003/Kuujou-Joutarou) and Kakyoin joined the Joestar group.', '/uploads/images/c_8945.jpg'),
(65, 'Mohammed Avdol', 'モハメド・アヴドゥル', '主角', 'Kenta Miyake', '__Height:__ 188 cm (6''2") __Stand:__ Magician''s Red Avdol is a fortune teller and friend of [Joseph Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/6356/Joestar-Joseph). They met three years before the events of the story. He was born with a stand, Magician’s Red, which controls fire. This stand’s abilities include Crossfire Hurricane, which shoots fire in the shape of an Ankh, and Crossfire Hurricane Special, which splits into multiple Ankh-shaped flames. He can also create flame tracker that detects a person’s energy. Avdol presents himself as a serious person but can sometimes let his emotions get the best of him. He often acts as the voice of reason among the Joestar group and exhibits strong loyalty by frequently placing himself in danger to protect his friends. He is knowledgeable about geography and stands, enjoys India’s chaotic atmosphere, and respects [Polnareff](https://anilist.co/character/4368/Polnareff-JeanPierre)''s chivalrous attitude that he displayed when they first met. Avdol gives [Jotaro](https://anilist.co/character/4003/Kuujou-Joutarou)''s stand its name. ~!Avdol encountered [DIO](https://anilist.co/character/4004/Brando-Dio) in Egypt before the main events of the story, but was able to escape unscathed.!~ ~!At one point he is shot by [Hol Horse](https://anilist.co/character/16557/Horse-Hol) and presumed dead, but he was actually in hiding and rejoins the Joestar group later. He is killed protecting Polnareff and [Iggy](https://anilist.co/character/21089/Iggy) from', '/uploads/images/c_8946.jpg'),
(65, 'Hol Horse', 'ホル・ホｰス', '配角', 'Hidenobu Kiuchi', '**Height**: 188cm *(anime)* Hol Horse is a minor antagonist in JoJo''s Bizarre Adventure: Stardust Crusaders (first seen in Chapter 141 and Episode 10), as well as one of the main characters of Crazy Diamond''s Demonic Heartbreak. He is a tall, blonde-haired cowboy-themed mercenary, serving under Dio and his army of other Stand Users. He considers himself "The #2", preferring to work as support with a partner due to his cowardice and caution. He also respects women, no matter how pretty, or how ugly, as seen with his ex, Nena. His Stand is Emperor, named after the Tarot Card of the same name. It manifests itself as a retro-futuristic pistol, which functions as a normal firearm, although the bullets are able to change their trajectory to Hol Horse''s command. ~!He is seemingly fatally injured by his own Stand''s bullets in Chapter 221 (and episode 37 of the anime), but manages to survive and go into hiding, fearing Dio''s punishment for failing his mission of killing the Joestar group.!~', '/uploads/images/c_16557.png'),
(65, 'Iggy', 'イギー', '配角', '', '__Height:__ 33.3 cm __Nationality:__ American Iggy is a boston terrier who wields a stand known as The Fool, which is able to manipulate sand. Since The Fool is made of sand, damaging it will not hurt Iggy. He creates various objects out of sand including the wings of a glider and a statue of DIO. Iggy is depicted as rude and disobedient, as shown by his tendency to chew on people’s hair while farting on them. He loves coffee-flavored gum. Iggy was previously owned by a rich man, but he ran away and became a stray in New York. Avdol caught him and brought him to Egypt to help the Joestar group defeat DIO. He frequently chews Polnareff’s hair and once put chewed gum inside Jotaro’s hat. ~!At first, Iggy seems indifferent towards the Joestar’s quest to defeat DIO. Then he accidentally finds DIO’s mansion and is attacked and injured by Pet Shop, causing his hatred for DIO to grow. He is killed after saving Polnareff from Vanilla Ice.!~ He was initially drawn as realistic dog, but as the story progressed, his face gradually became more similar to a human’s. He is named after Iggy Pop.', '/uploads/images/c_21089.jpg'),
(65, 'Suzie Q', 'スージーＱ', '配角', '', '__Height:__ 168 cm The female assistant to Lisa Lisa. Suzie Q is a slightly ditzy girl who worries for her friends. Evidently this carefree personality has not diminished even in the events of Stardust Crusaders, when she is shown enthusiastically recording her sightings in Japan on a camcorder when on a trip to see her daughter. ~!She is introduced as the female assistant to Lisa Lisa. When she first appears, she is taken over by the remains of Esidisi and attacks her friends. Thanks to a combination attack by Caesar and Joseph, she is saved with only minor injury. She marries Joseph in 1939.!~', '/uploads/images/c_21962.png'),
(65, 'Narrator', 'ナレーター', '配角', 'Tooru Ookawa', 'This character page is set to represent and list all narrators, which haven''t been given a visual representation of themselves in their respective work. Please add other narrator characters, which were given a visual representation of themselves, separately from this narrator page.', '/uploads/images/c_36309.jpg'),
(65, 'J. Geil', 'J・ガイル', '配角', 'Takuya Kirimoto', 'J. Geil is the man responsible for the murder of Polnareff''s sister, earning him Polnareff''s desire for revenge. J. Geil expend most of his time hiding from plain view, preferring to have a partner in which to rely on. This made him a perfect candidate for Hol Horse who like him believe working in pairs. He would hide in the shadows while Hol Horse broke the glass needed for his stand to work and sometimes they would do combination attack, such as Hal Horse breaking glass and J. Geil attacking while Hol Horse shot a bullet from his Stand, the Emperor, locking the enemy in a mortal circle. Like his mother he had a deformity that give him two right hands. (Source: JJBA Wikia)', '/uploads/images/c_42159.jpg'),
(65, 'Enya Geil', 'エンヤ・ガイル', '配角', 'Reiko Suzuki', 'Enya Geil is one of Dio''s most loyal supporters, and the one who originally gave him the Stand Arrow, which she obtained from Diavolo. She is the mother of J. Geil. Her stand is Justice, which is able to control people through their wounds, whether alive or dead. For legal reasons, her name is changed in the American version of both the game and the manga, to N-Yah Gail and Enyaba Geil respectively. In the OVA: ~!She is able to change her appearance from that of a young woman to an old lady at will. No explanation as to why is ever given.!~', '/uploads/images/c_77359.jpg'),
(65, 'Rubber Soul', 'ラバーソール', '配角', 'Shinji Kawada', 'Rubber Soul is a medium-height curly haired man, with his Stand granting him the ability to grow larger and to change appearance at will. He was hired by Dio with the promise of earning 100 millions as a reward for killing Jotaro. Rubber Soul does, however, have a rather disturbing personality: he is extremely rude and impolite, showing no respect nor mercy for people and animals, as they are beings that he only sees as food for his Yellow Temperance. He does not seem to be particularly intelligent, though he has a really bad temper: he wanted to ambush Jotaro with Kakyoin''s appearance, but his unusual behavior blew his cover. Rubber Soul is also very violent: he attempts to kill a pickpocket by breaking his back, and remorselessly eats a dog under the eyes of its master with his Stand. In order to grow bigger, he did not hesitate to eat bugs either. From: http://jjba.wikia.com/wiki/Rubber_Soul', '/uploads/images/c_78409.png'),
(65, 'Boingo', 'ボインゴ', '配角', '', 'Boingo is a young Stand User whose Stand is Tohth. As part of the Egypt 9 Glory Gods, he attempts to assassinate the Joestar Group in Egypt alongside his older brother Oingo and later Hol Horse. Boingo is a young child of ordinary build, but his characteristics include an unusually large mouth and a large afro held together by a topless cap, leaving a few stray hair locks. His attire consists of a bright shirt and trousers over which he wears shorts and a jacket, plus a coat and simple shoes. Tohth is an Artificial Non-Humanoid Stand that takes the form of a manga. The book, titled, Oingo Boingo Brothers Adventure, will show predictions of the future. When an image appears, the prediction(s) then become fate and are destined to come to fruition. However, nobody, not even Boingo, can control the Image projected onto Tohth.', '/uploads/images/c_79703.jpg'),
(65, 'Nena', 'ネーナ', '配角', 'Satsuki Yukino', 'Nena is a minor antagonist appearing in Stardust Crusaders. She first appears in India alongside Hol Horse and tries to assassinate Joseph Joestar while passing as an ordinary woman. She is a Stand User who uses Empress. Nena first looks like a beautiful young Indian woman in typical Indian attire. However, this is only a disguise and Nena is truly a short, ugly and overweight woman wearing a bikini. Nena also possesses a bud on her tongue. Nena used her Stand Empress to kill a beautiful young woman and wore her skin to hide her true form. (Source: Jojo Wiki)', '/uploads/images/c_129823.png'),
(65, 'Holly Kuujou', '空条ホリィ       ', '配角', 'Reiko Takagi', 'Holly Kuujou née Joestar is the daughter of [Joseph Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/6356/) and mother of [Joutarou Kuujou](https://anilist.co/character/4003/).', '/uploads/images/c_129824.png'),
(65, 'Forever', 'フォーエバー', '配角', 'Kappei Yamaguchi', 'Forever is a malicious orangutan in DIO''s service who confronts the group in the South China Sea aboard a freighter. Said ship happens to be possessed by Forever''s Stand: Strength.', '/uploads/images/c_130569.png'),
(65, 'Sherry Polnareff', 'シェリー・ポルナレフ', '配角', 'Yuka Komatsu', 'Sherry Polnareff is Jean Pierre Polnareff''s little sister who was raped and murdered by J. Geil, prompting Polnareff to seek revenge against her killer.', '/uploads/images/c_130570.png'),
(65, 'Anne', 'アン', '配角', 'Rie Kugimiya', 'Anne is a minor character appearing in Stardust Crusaders. Joining the Joestar Group before departing for Singapore, she somehow follows them from there to Pakistan and appears regularly alongside the main characters.', '/uploads/images/c_130571.png'),
(65, 'Gray Fly', 'グレー・フライ', '配角', 'Katsumi Chou', 'Gray Fly is an assassin sent by DIO who attacks the group aboard a plane traveling from Tokyo to Cairo, eventually crashing it into the ocean near Hong Kong. He is a Stand User and wields Tower of Gray.', '/uploads/images/c_130572.png'),
(65, 'Steely Dan', '鋼入りのスティーリーダン', '配角', 'Daisuke Kishio', 'Steely Dan is a Stand User using the microscopic Lovers. Steely Dan is sent to assassinate Enya the Hag and then confronts the Joestar Group in Pakistan.', '/uploads/images/c_130573.png'),
(65, 'Devo', 'デーボ', '配角', 'Shouto Kashii', 'Devo the Cursed is an infamous Native American shaman and assassin in DIO''s service. Devo ambushes Jean Pierre Polnareff in his hotel room in Singapore. He is a Stand User and uses Ebony Devil.', '/uploads/images/c_130574.png'),
(65, 'Cameo', 'カメオ', '配角', 'Kinryuu Arimoto', 'Cameo (カメオ Kameo) is a minor antagonist featured in Stardust Crusaders. He isolates Polnareff from the Joestar Group on a secluded island in the Red Sea while they are there to retrieve Avdol. Cameo is one of DIO''s henchmen, and the Stand User behind the genie Stand, Judgement.', '/uploads/images/c_130575.png'),
(65, 'Mannish Boy', 'マニッシュ・ボーイ', '配角', 'Ikue Ootani', 'Mannish Boy is an evil genius baby and Stand user in DIO''s service. He tries to murder the Joestar Group inside the nightmare-world of his Death Thirteen.', '/uploads/images/c_130576.png'),
(65, 'Arabia Fats', 'アラビア・ファッツ', '配角', 'Manabu Sakamaki', 'Arabia Fats is another of DIO''s goons, who ambushes the Joestar Group in the middle of the Arabian desert with his Stand: Sun.', '/uploads/images/c_130577.png'),
(65, 'Roses', 'ローゼス', '配角', 'Motomu Kiyokawa', 'Roses is the butler of Joseph Joestar and Suzi Q, also acting as the latter''s personal chauffeur and bodyguard.', '/uploads/images/c_130578.png'),
(65, 'ZZ', 'ズィー・ズィー', '配角', 'Masami Iwasaki', 'ZZ is another of DIO''s assassins who confronts the Joestar Group. He is a Stand User who drives his Wheel of Fortune.', '/uploads/images/c_130579.png'),
(65, 'Nise Captain Tennille', '偽キャプテン・テニール', '配角', 'Tesshou Genda', 'The impostor Captain Tennille is a minor antagonist appearing in Stardust Crusaders. He is an assassin sent by DIO who fights the Joestar Group in the middle of the ocean on their way to Egypt. He is a Stand User and wields Dark Blue Moon.', '/uploads/images/c_130580.png'),
(65, 'Midler', 'ミドラー', '配角', 'Aya Hisakawa', 'Midler is the last of DIO''s assassins the heroes encounter before entering Egypt. She is a Stand User, and her High Priestess attacks the group as they travel by submarine in the Red Sea.', '/uploads/images/c_130581.png'),
(65, 'Imushitsu no Sensei', '医務室の先生', '配角', 'Ayumi Tsunematsu', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_388258.png'),
(65, 'Kankoukyaku A', '観光客A', '配角', 'Ayaka Suwa', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389591.jpg'),
(65, 'Kankoukyaku B', '観光客B', '配角', 'Ai Kakuma', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389592.jpg'),
(65, 'Keikan A', '警官A', '配角', 'Koutarou Nakamura', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389593.jpg'),
(65, 'Keikan B', '警官B', '配角', 'Eiji Miyashita', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389594.jpg'),
(65, 'Senin A', '船員A', '配角', 'Shinobu Matsumoto', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389595.jpg'),
(65, 'Senin B', '船員B', '配角', 'Takahiro Fujiwara', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389596.jpg'),
(65, 'Senin C', '船員C', '配角', 'Yuuma Uchida', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389597.jpg'),
(65, 'Tenshu', '店主', '配角', 'Takahiro Fujiwara', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389598.jpg'),
(65, 'Suri', 'スリ', '配角', 'Kenji Yanagisawa', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389599.jpg'),
(66, 'Kazuto Kirigaya', '桐ヶ谷和人', '主角', 'Yoshitsugu Matsuoka', '__Height:__ 172 cm __Weapon(s) of choice:__ Anneal Blade (1st Level), Queen''s Knightblade (9th Level), Elucidator (50th level) and Dark Repulser (forged by Lisbeth) Kirito is a "solo" player, a player who hasn''t joined a guild and usually works alone. He is also one of the very few people to have had the privilege to play in the beta testing period of Sword Art Online. His game alias, Kirito, is created by taking the syllables of the first and last Kanji of his real last and first names respectively: (Kirigaya Kazuto). In the real world, he lives with his mother and younger sister in a family of 3. When [Kayaba](https://anilist.co/character/36829) announced the start of the death game, he is surprised, but unlike everyone else he quickly gets over it and accepts it to an extent. He invited his friend [Klein](https://anilist.co/character/36830) to go with him but Klein had to find his friends in the game. He was invited to join them but he declined as he couldn''t take the pressure of protecting them even with his beta testing knowledge of the game.', '/uploads/images/c_36765.png'),
(66, 'Asuna Yuuki', '結城明日奈', '主角', 'Haruka Tomatsu', '__Height:__ 160-168 cm __Weapons of choice:__ Wind Fleuret (1st Floor), Lambent Light (Forged by [Lisbeth](https://anilist.co/character/43906/Shinozaki-Rika)) Asuna is a friend of [Kirito](https://anilist.co/character/36765/Kirigaya-Kazuto) and is a sub-leader of the guild Knights of the Blood (KoB), a medium-sized guild of about thirty players, also called the strongest guild in Aincrad. Being one of the few girls that are in SAO, and even more so that she''s extremely pretty, she receives many invitations and proposals. She is a skilled player earning the title "Lightning Flash" for her extraordinary sword skill that is lightning fast. Her game alias is the same as her real world name.', '/uploads/images/c_36828.png'),
(66, 'Ryoutarou Tsuboi', '壷井遼太郎', '配角', 'Hiroaki Hirata', 'A friendly player that meets Kirito at the start of the game and quickly befriends and learns from him. He and Kirito later separate because he has friends who were also new to the game so he couldn''t leave them. He survives for the past two years and managed to protect his friends the whole time, something Kirito regretted not doing. He is a katana user and the leader of the small guild Fuurinkazan who participates in the boss battles. As one of the few people close to Kirito, he always keeps him in check and wants Kirito to survive the game. He chose the Salamader race on ALO ~! In the side story Caliber, he fell in love at first sight with the girl on the cage named Freyja and agreed that he will help her find her tribe''s treasure which is a hammer, though the decision still remains to be a team''s decision. The team said yes on Caliber and it turned out that the girl they saved was Thor. It was revealed that Thor disguised as a beautiful girl to get close to Giant King Þrym and retrieve his hammer. Thor defeated Giant King Þrym and that stopped the medallion from being corrupted and ending the quest. !~', '/uploads/images/c_36830.png'),
(66, 'Suguha Kirigaya', '桐ヶ谷直葉', '配角', 'Ayana Taketatsu', '[Kazuto](https://anilist.co/character/36765)''s sister in the real world. She is 15 years old and in her third year of junior high, as well as a member of the Kendou club. She''s a diligent worker and has been practicing Kendou for 8 years. ~!In the VRMMO game *Alfheim Online*, she is known as Leafa, a Sylph fairy. She stumbled onto Kazuto by accident one night and decided to travel with him to the World Tree. She eventually fell in love with him because he showed that he really loves playing VR games as if living in it and is very honest in everything. In the real world she slowly got closer to her brother (actually a cousin) but because they''re family and because he already got [Asuna](https://anilist.co/character/36828) as a girlfriend she decided to give up on him and fall in love with Kazuto instead. But soon afterwards she realized that they''re the same person. After being convinced by Kazuto to have a fierce duel which ended up in them flying in each others'' arms, she decided to help Kazuto in rescuing Asuna.!~', '/uploads/images/c_36831.png'),
(66, 'Keiko Ayano', '綾野珪子', '配角', 'Rina Hidaka', 'She is a middle level dagger user. She is a very cheerful and sweet girl. She has a very rare familiar, a feathery dragon that she named [Pina](https://anilist.co/character/212810/Pina) after her cat in the real world. She treasured Pina a lot and was the reason she survived in the game. Aside from being a female player, she is also a Beast Tamer and thus perceived as an idol amongst the middle level players. She received endless invitations from parties and guilds who wanted an idol player to join them to get more fame. Because of the attention she got, she became overly proud of herself and left a party one time after a misunderstanding. She got surrounded by monsters and lost Pina in the end. She was then rescued by [Kirito](https://anilist.co/character/36765/Kirigaya-Kazuto) who was passing by and helped her to resurrect the dead familiar.', '/uploads/images/c_37681.jpg'),
(66, 'Yui', 'ユイ', '配角', 'Kanae Itou', 'A young and cheerful girl with long black hair who looks no older than 10 years old. [Kirito](https://anilist.co/character/36765) and [Asuna](https://anilist.co/character/36828) found her in a forest on the 22nd floor of Aincrad. ~!Her true identity is actually a players'' self-regulation program for mental maintenance, Mental Health Counseling Program or MHCP. After being forbidden by the game master [Akihiko Kayaba](https://anilist.co/character/36829) to come close to the players at the beginning of the death game, she was flooded with errors and broke down. In the process she became an AI that possesses actual intelligence. When the Cardinal system governing *Sword Art Online* decided to erase her, Kirito turned her into a tear shaped crystal pendant. He actually converted her to a part of environmental data for the client program and was saved to his NerveGear''s local memory.!~ ~!In *ALfheim Online*, she was able to return to her normal form because ALO was based on a copy of the SAO server. She supports Kirito there as a Navigation Pixie. Kirito and Asuna still treat her as their daughter.!~', '/uploads/images/c_43892.jpg'),
(66, 'Rika Shinozaki', '篠崎里香', '配角', 'Ayahi Takagaki', 'A mace wielder that runs a blacksmith shop in Aincrad on the 48th floor. She made [Asuna](https://anilist.co/character/36828)’s rapier ‘Lament Light’ and one day got a request from [Kirito](https://anilist.co/character/36765) to make him a sword with similar or better quality than his one handed long sword ‘Elucidator’ that he got from a monster drop. She told him that if she had the right materials she could make weapons that would break any sword, so they formed a party and went on a journey to find the material she needed. Because of that journey she came to the conclusion that she felt lonely and yearned for warmth. In ALO she is Leprechaun race blacksmith. ~!She comes to realize that she loves Kirito but after finding out that the one Asuna had feelings for was in fact Kirito she decided to give up on him despite how she feels so Asuna could express her feelings, however during the moments after Kirito''s victory and SAO''s announcement that the game has been cleared she shouts at the top of her lungs that she loves Kirito and that she will meet him again in the real world, which after the ALO incident she actually does, going to school with him and Asuna.!~', '/uploads/images/c_43906.png'),
(66, 'Andrew Gilbert Mills', 'アンドリュー・ギルバート・ミルズ', '配角', 'Hiroki Yasumoto', '__Height:__ 180cm A merchant stationed at city Algate, located at the 50th floor of Aincrad. His shop motto is "Buy cheap and sell cheap". He is a very strong axe-wielding warrior in the frontlines. Kirito sometimes stays in his shop as sort of a disaster shelter, which he gets annoyed with but later ignores as Asuna also visits, which results in some publicity for his shop. ~!In the real world he is married and owns a Bar called Dicey Cafe!~ ~!In the side story Aria in the Starless Night, he is among the few players who participated in the first floor boss fight and supported Kirito when he knew of the latter''s status as a beta tester and later called a Beater. !~ ~!Upon returning to the real world he helps Kirito implement Kayaba''s "seed" which allows VR games to be easier accessed throughout the world, also vastly decreasing the large licensing cost that companies would pay in servers.!~', '/uploads/images/c_54099.jpg'),
(66, 'Shino Asada', '朝田詩乃', '主角', 'Miyuki Sawashiro', 'Shino is a skilled VRMMO player. She goes by the name Sinon in *Gun Gale Online* and *Alfheim Online*. She is nicknamed Hecate, after her gun PGM Ultima Ratio Hecate II, a .50 caliber anti-material rare sniper rifle. She is one of the main characters of volumes five and six and first female player that [Kirito](https://anilist.co/character/36765/Kazuto-Kirigaya) meets in *GGO*. She plays *GGO* to overcome her trauma concerning guns. Calm and cool are the two words that best describe Sinon''s personality. In battle and most of the time in the game, she keeps a cool head that actually makes other female players admire her. However, Sinon has a violent temper once angered something that is best seen with her interactions with Kirito. It is actually said that Kirito is the first one to make her extremely angry. Despite all this, Sinon, while may be hard to approach, is generally a friendly person and doesn''t mind helping others. ~!She becomes a Cait Sith archer in *ALO* where she is capable of hitting targets from 200m away despite her bow being limited to 100m.!~', '/uploads/images/c_55147.png'),
(66, 'Yuuki Konno', '紺野木綿季', '主角', 'Aoi Yuuki', 'She is a new player who appears in ALO in volume 7, she leads the Sleeping Knights and quickly becomes known as one of the strongest in the game winning 67 straight matches. ~!Her guild the Sleeping Knights is a group of terminally ill patients who play using the FullDive Technology MediCuboid, Yuuki''s disease is AIDS which she obtained through a bad blood transfer she received as a child due to dystocia, the disease took form when she was bullied in school after it was known she was a carrier; she was then later taken to the hospital where she lived the next 3 years in the new medical FullDive Technology called MediCuboid; it is due to this that her experience in the VR world exceeds even the survivors of SAO, and for this reason even makes her a match for [Kirito](https://anilist.co/character/36765/Kirigaya-Kazuto) when he is not Dual wielding. She quickly becomes friends with [Asuna](https://anilist.co/character/36828/Yuuki-Asuna) due to the reason that she looks similiar to her elder twin sister who died one year prior to her meeting with Asuna.!~', '/uploads/images/c_64523.jpg'),
(66, 'Vassago Casals', 'ヴァサゴ・カザルス', '配角', 'Tsuyoshi Koyama', 'Leader and founder of the red guild "Laughing Coffin", known for his large knife and catch phrase "It''s show time." His guild was later destroyed by other players in SAO, but his whereabouts are missing. He is presumed to be alive because he wasn''t listed as one of the dead players. (Source: SAO Wiki)', '/uploads/images/c_70683.jpg'),
(66, 'Shouichi Shinkawa', '新川昌一', '配角', 'Souichirou Hoshi', 'One of the top members in the red guild Laughing Coffin. He was a master of the Estoc Thorn Sword that was bathed in the color of red. He holds a grudge against [Kirito](https://anilist.co/character/36765) and the clearers that defeated Laughing Coffin in the anti-PK raid. He was also partners with Johnny Black, and together served as a combination where they poisoned and killed. ~!After his release from *Sword Art Online*, through the recommendation of his brother [Kyouji](https://anilist.co/character/73151), he began to play *Gun Gale Online*. The two looked to another Laughing Coffin member and began to plot a ingenious plan to kill players in both the virtual world and the real world. He enters the Bullet of Bullets tournament under the name Sterben to prove his "true" killing ability to the rest of the world. He would stun people with special shells from his L115A3 Silent Assasin sniper rifle and then get up close to shoot them with his Death Gun, a 7.62 X 25 handgun. While he commited the kill in-game, his brother and the other Laughing Coffin member would inject the players in the real world with a syringe that stopped the heart. They had obtained the address by hiding under a Metamaterial Optical Camouflage while they watched the other players type their real addresses during the BoB registration process. His plans were foiled by Kirito and [Sinon](https://anilist.co/character/55147), and eventually goes to prison after the incident had passed.!~', '/uploads/images/c_70685.png'),
(66, 'Atsushi Kanamoto', '金本敦', '配角', 'Ryouta Oosaka', 'Johnny Black was a survivor of Sword Art Online, he''s a member of the infamous red guild Laughing Coffin and is partnered with Xaxa. He is well known for using poisons and such in battles.', '/uploads/images/c_70687.jpg'),
(66, 'Seijirou Kikuoka', '菊岡誠二郎', '配角', 'Toshiyuki Morikawa', 'Seijirou Kikuoka is a member of the Ministry of Internal Affairs and Communications, Technology, Second Separated Advanced Network Division, or «Virtual Division». He uses the nickname «Chrysheight» in «ALfheim Online»', '/uploads/images/c_72205.jpg'),
(66, 'Alicia Rue', 'アリシャ・ルー', '配角', 'Chiwa Saitou', 'Alicia Rue is the leader of the Cait Sith. She was elected by popular vote. She is also training her dark magic capable of using Moonlight Mirror. She forms an alliance with the Sylphs to finish the Conquer the World Tree Quest. ~!During the meeting with Sylph , the groups are attacked by Salamanders lead by General Eugene. Kirito dives in to save the day and fights off Eugene although Kirito has inferior equipment. Later, along with Sylph reinforcements, she aid Kirito''s ascension of the World Tree after using collected funds to purchase armor of at least Ancient grade for all of her warriors.!~ (Source: SAO Wiki)', '/uploads/images/c_72901.png'),
(66, 'Eugene', 'ユージン', '配角', 'Kenta Miyake', 'General Eugene is the head of the Salamander armed forces. ~!He was considered the strongest player in ALfheim Online until he was defeated by Kirito during the Conference of the Lords.!~ (Source: SAO Wiki)', '/uploads/images/c_72903.png'),
(66, 'Sigurd', 'シグルド', '配角', 'Takuya Kirimoto', 'Sigurd is a Sylph warrior in the VRMMORPG «ALfheim Online». He lost to Lyfa in the Sylph tournament yet he still retained high ambitions to hold power among the Sylph. He later tries to betray the Sylph to the Salamander. He is later caught and exiled by Sakuya, after the botched assassination attempt. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_72905.png'),
(66, 'Kyouji Shinkawa', '新川恭二', '配角', 'Natsuki Hanae', 'Kyouji is a player of the American produced VRMMORPG Gun Gale Online. He uses the AGI powered character Spiegel. He is Asada Shino''s friend and the one introduced her to GGO. ~!He is a son of the director of a hospital. He later develops a hatred towards Zekushido, as well as other STR-oriented players, for destroying Spiegel''s development by suggesting AGI as the way to power provoking him to boost AGI, but being unable to wield heavy guns due to his lack in STR. He also later develops a stalker attachment towards Shino, resulting in him attempting a homicide and suicide together with her, only to be foiled by Kirito, almost being killed in the process. He also played the role of Death Gun when Zenkushido and Usujiro Takaro were killed. In the end, he and his brother were arrested by the police.!~ (Source: SAO Wiki)', '/uploads/images/c_73151.jpg'),
(66, 'Sakuya', 'サクヤ', '配角', 'Sayuri Yahagi', 'Leader of the Sylph race and an exceptional swordswoman. She was elected as the leader of the Sylph race by popular vote (80% voice of the vote). Her statistics are not very high due to her status as a Lord not allowing her to do much training. Despite her low stats, she is a formidable opponent in the Sylph dueling tournaments. ~!During a meeting with the Cait Sith, she is attacked by Salamanders led by General Eugene. At the same moment, Kirito flies in to challenge the intruder to a duel. After Kirito wins the battle, she attempts to seduce him along with Alicia Rue. Lyfa smothers their attempt, saying that he is accompanying her to the World Tree. At the end of the arc, Lady Sakuya leads a combined force of Cait Sith and Sylph against the World Tree in an attempt to aid Kirito along his journey.!~ (Source: SAO Wiki)', '/uploads/images/c_73811.jpg'),
(66, 'Natsuki Aki', '安岐ナツキ', '配角', 'Ayako Kawasumi', 'is a nurse who works for the Japan Ground Self-Defense Force (JGSDF) and was assigned by Kikuoka Seijirou to oversee Kirigaya Kazuto''s medical condition at «Chiyoda Hospital» when he was hospitalized as well as during his rehabilitation. She is later assigned to watch over Kazuto during the «Death Gun» incident and after Kazuto is injected with succinylcholine.', '/uploads/images/c_136729.jpg'),
(66, 'Dyne', 'ダイン', '配角', 'Satoshi Tsuruoka', 'Dyne is a player in the VRMMO game, Gun Gale Online. He is the leader of a PvP (anti-personnel) squadron that primarily targets weaker low-risk opponents.', '/uploads/images/c_187242.jpg'),
(66, 'Pale Rider', 'ペイルライダー', '配角', '', 'Pale Rider was one of the participants of the third Bullet of Bullets(BoB) tournament in the Gun Gale Online. Pale Rider was a STR-type player, who had three dimensional mobility. Pale Rider was a tall, skinny male who wore blue and white camouflage clothing. Due to his black helmet, his face could not be seen. Pale Rider used an ArmaLite AR17 Shotgun.', '/uploads/images/c_187243.jpg'),
(66, 'Behemoth', 'ベヒモス', '配角', 'Kenichirou Matsuda', 'A high-ranked mercenary player in the VRMMO, Gun Gale Online, who is usually hired as a bodyguard for player groups with money but no perseverance. Behemoth uses a heavy GE M134 Minigun as his weapon of choice.', '/uploads/images/c_187244.jpg'),
(66, 'Nori', 'ノリ', '配角', 'Asami Tano', 'She is a medium-range, damage-dealer member of the Sleeping Knights, a guild of terminally ill patients who met in Serene Garden and played various virtual reality games as a form of palliative care. Nori had played a variety of virtual reality games, until the guild eventually arrived to ALfheim Online, where Nori chose to be a Spriggan.', '/uploads/images/c_212207.jpg'),
(66, 'Freyja', 'フレイヤ', '配角', 'Yuuko Minaguchi', 'An Npc that appears in the scalibur sword plot, being locked up and being Klein who falls in love with her and frees her', '/uploads/images/c_212614.jpg'),
(66, 'Thrym', 'スリュム', '配角', 'Shouzou Iizuka', 'is an NPC that appears in ALfheim Online. He is the king of the Frost Giants and the main antagonist of the Caliber Arc.', '/uploads/images/c_212616.png'),
(66, 'Siune', 'シウネ', '配角', 'Yuu Shimamura', 'She was the second sub-leader of the Sleeping Knights, a guild of terminally ill patients who met in Serene Garden and played various virtual reality games as a form of palliative care. An Si-eun had played a variety of virtual reality games, including Insect Site, until the guild eventually arrived to ALfheim Online, where An Si-eun chose to be an Undine.', '/uploads/images/c_212618.jpg'),
(66, 'Tecchi', 'テッチ', '配角', 'Nobuyuki Kobushi', 'He is a close-range, tank-build member of the Sleeping Knights, a guild of terminally ill patients who met in Serene Garden and played various virtual reality games as a form of palliative care. Tecchi had played a variety of virtual reality games, until the guild eventually arrived to ALfheim Online, where Tecchi chose to be a Gnome.', '/uploads/images/c_212619.jpg'),
(66, 'Talken', 'タルケン', '配角', 'Atsushi Tamaru', 'He is a medium-range, damage-dealer member of the Sleeping Knights, a guild of terminally ill patients who met in Serene Garden and played various virtual reality games as a form of palliative care. Talken had played a variety of virtual reality games, until the guild eventually arrived to ALfheim Online, where Talken chose to be a Leprechaun.', '/uploads/images/c_212620.jpg'),
(66, 'Jun', 'ジュン', '配角', 'Daiki Yamashita', 'He is a close-range tank-build swordsman member of the Sleeping Knights, a guild of terminally ill patients who met in Serene Garden and played various virtual reality games as a form of palliative care. Jun had played a variety of virtual reality games, until the guild eventually arrived to ALfheim Online, where Jun chose to be a Salamander.', '/uploads/images/c_212621.jpg'),
(66, 'Yamikaze', '闇風', '配角', 'Gou Shinomiya', 'Is an AGI-type player in Gun Gale Online and a participant in the 2nd and 3rd Bullet of Bullets.', '/uploads/images/c_212622.png'),
(66, 'Tamotsu Shigemura', '茂村保', '配角', 'Hiroshi Kamiya', 'He is a Gun Gale Online player who ranked first in the second Bullet of Bullets tournament.', '/uploads/images/c_212626.jpg'),
(66, 'Aiko Konno', '紺野藍子', '配角', '', 'She is the older sister of [Yuuki Konno](https://anilist.co/character/64523). She is the founder of the Sleeping Knights Guild, a group of terminally ill patients who play VRMMOs.', '/uploads/images/c_212627.png'),
(66, 'Verdandi', 'ベルザンディ', '配角', 'Mai Nakahara', 'NPC that are part of the Excalibur mission.', '/uploads/images/c_212646.png'),
(66, 'Skuld', 'スクルド', '配角', 'Saki Fujita', 'She is one of the NPCs that are part of the Excalibur mission.', '/uploads/images/c_212679.png'),
(66, 'Urd', 'ウルズ', '配角', 'Houko Kuwashima', 'It is an NPC that appears in one of the missions of ALfheim Online which consists of rescuing the Holy Sword Excalibur from Þrymheimr. She is friends with the Evil-type animal creatures that inhabit Jötunheimr.', '/uploads/images/c_212691.png'),
(66, 'Pina', 'ピナ', '配角', 'Shiori Izawa', 'is Silica''s Feathered Little Dragon and the first known monster to be tamed in Sword Art Online. It understands Silica''s commands and will protect her in any way it can, as it is her «Tamed Monster». It is also present in ALfheim Online as her Cait Sith familiar.', '/uploads/images/c_212810.png'),
(66, 'Kurahashi', '倉橋', '配角', 'Hidenobu Kiuchi', 'He is in charge of the long-term care department at the Yokohama Kōhoku General Hospital and was Konno Yuuki''s doctor since she was little. He had been helping her overcome her human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) and was the one who persuaded her to use the Medicuboid', '/uploads/images/c_212915.jpg'),
(66, 'Endou', '遠藤', '配角', 'Youko Hikasa', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_213209.jpg'),
(66, 'Ginrou', 'ギンロウ', '配角', 'Anri Katsu', 'He is a member of Dyne''s PvP (anti-personnel) squad that targets weaker, low-risk opponents. Ginrou''s evasion skills in face-to-face combat is known to be above average', '/uploads/images/c_213210.png'),
(66, 'Avatar Buyer', 'アバターバイヤー', '配角', 'Tsuguo Mogami', 'A GGO player dedicated to purchasing skins from new players', '/uploads/images/c_213211.png'),
(66, 'Juushi X', '銃士X', '配角', '', 'A player in the VRMMO game, Gun Gale Online, and a participant in the 3rd Bullet of Bullets. She is one of the four players in the finals of the tournament who had not participated in the finals of the previous two tournaments.', '/uploads/images/c_247629.png'),
(66, 'Akiyo Sada', '佐田明代', '配角', 'Sayaka Aida', 'Housekeeper working for the Yuuki family', '/uploads/images/c_247631.png'),
(66, 'Shishi Ou Richie', '獅子王リッチー', '配角', '', 'Richie participated in the 2nd Bullet of Bullets tournament, during which he occupied the highest point in the area and used his machine gun to keep other players away. However, Richie had to withdraw after running out of ammunition.', '/uploads/images/c_247633.png'),
(67, 'Ken Kaneki', '金木研', '主角', 'Natsuki Hanae', '__Height:__ 169 cm (5''6") Ken Kaneki was originally a human and a normal college student until he encountered a female ghoul named [Rize](https://anilist.co/character/88413/Rize-Kamishiro) who was posing as a human at the time. Rize, using Kaneki''s crush on her as leverage, managed to lure him into an alley and tried to eat him but ended up dying when construction beams fell on top of her. Kaneki, already in a half-dead state from Rize''s attempts at killing him, ends up in a hospital and has some of Rize''s organs transplanted into his body. This results in him absorbing some of Rize''s powers and characteristics, such as a ghoul eye, powers of regeneration, and the inability to stomach human food. Terrified and lost, Kaneki''s life takes a dramatic turn from then on as he tries to find a place for himself in the world, realizing he now belongs to neither the human nor ghoul world and refusing to eat humans to sustain himself. Meeting some of the ​other ghouls, as well as humans, makes him realize that things aren''t just black and white and that there are more to ghouls and humans than originally thought.', '/uploads/images/c_87275.png'),
(67, 'Touka Kirishima', '霧嶋董香', '主角', 'Sora Amamiya', '__Height:__ 156 cm (5''1") Touka is a ghoul successfully posing as a human and working as a waitress at a cafe which serves as a gathering place for other ghouls, as well as a food resource. She saves [Kaneki](https://anilist.co/character/87275/Kaneki-Ken)''s life at one point and acts as a reluctant guide to him and his adaptation to the ghoul society. She doesn''t like Kaneki much and has no qualms about expressing her dislike for him. She is very serious, tough and hard-working, trying to keep their district as safe for ghouls and humans as possible. Her powers and strength are also quite great and she makes for a formidable opponent.', '/uploads/images/c_87277.png'),
(67, 'Hinami Fueguchi', '笛口雛実', '配角', 'Sumire Morohoshi', '__Height:__ 148 cm - 152 cm (4''10" - 4''11") Hinami is a child ghoul whose parents were killed by ghoul investigators. Before, she and her mother seek help from the owner of the Antique Cafe to acquire food. Hinami is initially quite shy, but when she opens up, she is cheerful and earnest. [Ken](https://anilist.co/character/87275/Kaneki-Ken) helps her learn kanji, as she cannot attend school, and is very eager to learn. Currently, she is living together with [Touka Kirishima](https://anilist.co/character/87277/Kirishima-Touka).', '/uploads/images/c_88293.png'),
(67, 'Koutarou Amon', '亜門鋼太朗', '配角', 'Katsuyuki Konishi', '__Height:__ 191 cm (6''3") A first class police investigator who investigates Ghouls, also known as a Dove. He comes to the 20th ward with his mentor, [Mado Kureo](https://anilist.co/character/88423), to investigate Ghoul incidents in the area. He has a strong sense of justice, fervently believing it is the right and moral thing to do to exterminate the Ghouls. He hunts the Ghouls in order to prevent more human children from becoming orphaned like himself, and he often works after hours to achieve his goals. He wields a "Quinque" (a weapon made from the "Kagune" of a Ghoul) that has the appearance of a pole-arm with a large cylindrical bludgeon at the end.', '/uploads/images/c_88407.png'),
(67, 'Yukinori Shinohara', '篠原幸紀', '配角', 'Yutaka Nakano', 'A Special Class Ghoul Investigator. In the past, he acted as Koutarou Amon''s instructor at the Academy.', '/uploads/images/c_88408.png'),
(67, 'Nishiki Nishio', '西尾錦', '配角', 'Shintarou Asanuma', '__Height:__ 177 cm (5''9") Nishiki Nishio is a ghoul whose original feeding ground was taken from Rize. He is a sophomore in the Pharmaceutical Department of Kamii University and Kimi Nishino''s boyfriend.', '/uploads/images/c_88409.png'),
(67, 'Kimi Nishino', '西野貴未', '配角', 'Yurie Kobori', 'Kimi Nishino is a assistant for Akihiro Kanou who aids in his ghoulification experiments, the previous human lover of Nishiki Nishio and a medical student at Kamii University.~!Although she is aware of his ghoul nature, she remained loyal to him and kept his secret. After the Owl Suppression Operation, he left her in order to keep her safe.!~', '/uploads/images/c_88410.jpg'),
(67, 'Ayato Kirishima', '霧嶋絢都', '配角', 'Yuuki Kaji', '__Height:__ 159 cm (5''2") Ayato Kirishima is [Touka Kirishima](https://anilist.co/character/87277/Touka-Kirishima)''s younger brother. He grew up with his sister in the 20th ward but at some point of time, he disappeared. Currently, he is an executive of Aogiri Tree. An arrogant youth with a similar harsh attitude that resembles his sister. Other than physical looks, he shares many similarities with Touka such as his cold, hotblooded attitude and a habit for kicking people. However, he''s more harsh compared to her and surprisingly nicer than his Aogiri superiors.', '/uploads/images/c_88411.png'),
(67, 'Juuzou Suzuya', '鈴屋什造', '配角', 'Rie Kugimiya', '__Height:__ 160 cm (5''3") A Rank 3 Ghoul Investigator. In the past, he went by the name Rei Suzuya. He is the partner of [Yukinori Shinohara](https://anilist.co/character/88408). He is a young man with androgynous appearance. He has many stitches used as both first-aid and fashion. His hair is tied with a stitching string in a roman numeral 13 pattern, with large pupils that leaves an eerie and frightening impression.', '/uploads/images/c_88412.png'),
(67, 'Rize Kamishiro', '神代利世', '配角', 'Kana Hanazawa', '__Height:__ 164 cm Rize Kamishiro is a ghoul that was hanging out at Anteiku. She set her eyes on [Ken Kaneki](https://anilist.co/character/87275/Kaneki-Ken), but moments before eating him, she died in an accident and her organs were transplanted in Ken Kaneki, making him half-ghoul.', '/uploads/images/c_88413.jpg'),
(67, 'Uta', 'ウタ', '配角', 'Takahiro Sakurai', '__Height:__ 177 cm A ghoul that has his own art studio where he makes masks for other ghouls. He has a lot of piercings and tattoos on his body, making him look pretty intimidating, even as a normal-looking human. He''s the one who also made a mask for Kaneki.', '/uploads/images/c_88414.jpg'),
(67, 'Itori', 'イトリ', '配角', 'Ayahi Takagaki', 'Itori is an old friend of Yomo and Uta. She can be found in Helter Skelter bar, where she makes her share in the information web of the underworld. Itori is over friendly and talkative. She likes having fun and even doing pranks. Her bad point might be her using people like toys to get the information she wants.', '/uploads/images/c_88415.jpg'),
(67, 'Enji Koma', '古間円児', '配角', 'Anri Katsu', 'Enji Koma is a ghoul and a waiter at Anteiku. He is an expert coffee brewer. In his youth, he was known as the Devil Ape and led the Apes ghoul gang.', '/uploads/images/c_88416.jpg'),
(67, 'Taro-chan', 'タロちゃん', '配角', 'Taketora', 'Taro is a scrapper of the Ghoul Restaurant and owned by Madam A.', '/uploads/images/c_88417.jpg'),
(67, 'Tatara', 'タタラ', '配角', 'Kouji Yusa', 'A direct subordinate of the One-Eyed King and one of Aogiri Tree''s leaders. He was a former member of the Chinese ghoul organization Chi She Lian. As one of the Aogiri Tree leaders and a trusted subordinate working under the One-Eyed King, Tatara comes off as a rather loyal individual. He is portrayed as composed and stoic mostly. He often monitors the activities of the Aogiri executives, but kills in cold-blood when embarking on a mission. He is also proud of his immense stamina when fighting and the accuracy of his calculations as well. Tatara seems to have a taste for precision; as shown when he turns down Kaneki considering he''s an artificial one-eyed ghoul. He appears to hold a grudge against Houji, to the extent that even the Quinque associated with him, is enough to make him enraged and lose his near unflappable composure. As the second-in-command of Aogiri, it can be inferred that he is quite powerful.', '/uploads/images/c_88418.png'),
(67, 'Nico', 'ニコ', '配角', 'Kenjirou Tsuda', '__Species:__ Ghoul __Height:__ 175 cm __Affiliations:__ Clown Mask Ghoul Gang A gay ghoul (okama) in love. He was once acting together with Yamori and participating in Aogiri Tree.', '/uploads/images/c_88419.jpg'),
(67, 'Hideyoshi Nagachika', '永近英良', '配角', 'Toshiyuki Toyonaga', '__Race:__ Human Hideyoshi is a normal human and the best friend of [Ken Kaneki](https://anilist.co/character/87275/Kaneki-Ken). Hide is incredibly observant and can figure things out about people in a almost sherlock-like manner. He also becomes interested in things and works hard on them until he finds something else to interest him.', '/uploads/images/c_88421.png'),
(67, 'Ryouko Fueguchi', '笛口リョーコ', '配角', 'Fumiko Orikasa', '[Hinami](https://anilist.co/character/88293/Hinami-Fueguchi)''s mother.', '/uploads/images/c_88422.jpg'),
(67, 'Kureo Mado', '真戸呉緒', '配角', 'Tooru Ookawa', '__Height:__ 177 cm A senior first class investigator, or a "Dove," who hunts Ghouls. He is Amon''s mentor and partner. He hunts Ghouls with a maniacal glee, and believes that all Ghouls are lesser than humans, calling them "trash," and mocking them for trying to "imitate" human behavior. Mado is a fanatic about collecting Ghoul''s "Kagune" (their extra limbs) and making them into "Quinque," or weapons that Doves use to kill Ghouls.', '/uploads/images/c_88423.png'),
(67, 'Shuu Tsukiyama', '月山習', '配角', 'Mamoru Miyano', '__Height:__ 180 cm Shuu Tsukiyama was the infamous Gourmet ghoul of the 20th ward. He was a fourth-year student studying Social Welfare at the Department of Human Sciences at Seinan Gakuin University. He comes from the extremely wealthy and influential Tsukiyama family which his father, Mirumo Tsukiyama was the head of. Tsukiyama himself became the head of his family after the Tsukiyama Family Extermination Operation. He was also a member of the Ghoul Restaurant, known as MM until he betrayed them. He joined Kaneki''s group with the hidden intention of eating Ken Kaneki, obsessed with his scent and taste but eventually came to genuinely care for Kaneki. Two years later, his severe depression and anorexia after Kaneki''s apparent demise left him emaciated and required constant care from his family servants. After finding out Kaneki was alive and meeting him, he recovers, being able to walk and eat on his own as well as take measures to help Kaneki regain his memories.', '/uploads/images/c_88424.png'),
(67, 'Yakumo Oomori', '大守八雲', '配角', 'Rintarou Nishi', 'A white-haired brute with sharp lizard eyes. Yamori is ghoul who is as scary as he looks. Normally in a entirely white suit and black dress shirt, he resembles a typical gangster.', '/uploads/images/c_88428.jpg'),
(67, 'Akira Mado', '真戸暁', '配角', 'Asami Seto', '__Species:__ Human __Height:__ 164 cm __Affiliations:__ CCG __Quinque:__ Amatsu (Koukaku/Bikaku) __Likes:__ making quinques, solving puzzles and cats Akira Mado is a Rank 2 Ghoul Investigator and Kureo''s daughter. She is currently partnered with Koutarou Amon. She is an intelligent woman and seems to be always serious about work and her daily routine in general. Like her father, she has deep insight and intuition that helps her in investigation and determining what is going on around her while on the field. She shares her father''s "quinque-mania," but it is not as extreme as his was. Akira remains professional in most situations, no matter who she is faced with, and she isn''t one to admit her own feelings on a subject unless provoked to a certain degree. Seen through her interactions with others, it is most likely that she would prefer to make a quinque rather than to interact with someone else.', '/uploads/images/c_88838.png'),
(67, 'Kishou Arima', '有馬貴将', '配角', 'Daisuke Namikawa', '__Height:__ 180 cm __Quinque:__ IXA (Koukaku), Narukami (Ukaku), Yukimura 1/3 (Koukaku) Kishou Arima is a famed Special Class Ghoul Investigator known as the CCG''s Reaper. He is undefeated as a Ghoul Investigator and at some point was formerly partnered with Take Hirako. His investigative skills and prowess in combat has led many investigators such as [Koutarou Amon](https://anilist.co/character/88407/Koutarou-Amon) to admire him. __Tokyo Ghoul:Re__ ~!He later passes down his Yukimura 1/3 (Koukaku) quinque to [Sasaki Haise](https://anilist.co/character/87275/Ken-Kaneki), a rank 1 investigator and mentor of Quinx squad. Along with [Akira Mado](https://anilist.co/character/88838/Akira-Mado), he is the overseer of the Quinx squad and keeps a check on Sasaki Haise along with the Quinx members.!~', '/uploads/images/c_88946.jpg'),
(67, 'Noro', 'ノロ', '配角', 'Kenji Hamada', 'He is one of the direct subordinates of the King of an Eye and one of the leaders of the Aogiri Tree, next to Tatara. In the past he was called Noroi and was responsible for raising Eto, when Kuzen surrendered in District 24. He is a giant who intimidates with an overwhelming silence, seems to communicate only through actions, not words.', '/uploads/images/c_125567.jpg'),
(67, 'Seidou Takizawa', '滝澤政道', '配角', 'Shinnosuke Tachibana', '__Height:__ 171 cm Takizawa is a Rank 2 Ghoul Investigator. A classmate of [Akira Mado](https://anilist.co/character/88838/Akira-Mado) at the Academy, he is partnered with Kousuke Houji and assigned to the 20th ward to investigate the Gourmet. He greatly respects [Kishou Arima](https://anilist.co/character/88946/Kishou-Arima) and [Koutarou Amon](https://anilist.co/character/88407/Koutarou-Amon) and admires their achievements. ~!Though he was declared among the casualties of the raid in the 20th Ward, it is revealed that he had actually survived as artificial one-eyed ghoul. He is now a member of Aogiri Tree. As an artificial one-eyed ghoul, he is known as Owl. After betraying Aogiri and killing [Tatara](https://anilist.co/character/88418/Tatara), Takizawa reunited with Akira Mado, and became a member of Ken Kaneki''s organization, Goat. !~', '/uploads/images/c_125884.jpg'),
(67, 'Yoshimura', '芳村', '配角', 'Takayuki Sugou', 'Yoshimura is a ghoul and the manager of the Anteiku cafe. He tries to help every ghoul, especially those who can''t hunt themselves. He takes in Ken Kaneki and tries to help him survive being a ghoul. ~!He is Eto''s father.!~', '/uploads/images/c_136024.png'),
(67, 'Itsuki Marude', '丸手斎', '配角', 'Yuuji Ueda', 'Itsuki is a Special Class Ghoul Investigator. He is the commander of the 11th Ward Special Countermeasures Unit and Chief of Division II.', '/uploads/images/c_145219.jpg'),
(67, 'Kousuke Houji', '法寺項介', '配角', 'Shou Hayami', 'Kousuke is a Special Class Investigator and a former partner of Kureo Mado prior to a major assignment in China. He was previously assigned to the 20th Ward as the partner of Seidou Takizawa and worked on the Gourmet case. He''s devoted to the mastery of quinque and is said to have surpassed Kureo. Currently, he serves as a member of the illustrious S3 Squad. (Source: Tokyo Ghoul Wikia)', '/uploads/images/c_167631.jpg'),
(67, 'Renji Yomo', '四方蓮示', '配角', 'Yuuichi Nakamura', '__Height:__ 182 cm (5''11") Renji Yomo is a worker at Anteiku and the right hand of [Yoshimura](https://anilist.co/character/136024/Yoshimura). He is an old friend of [Uta](https://anilist.co/character/88414/Uta) and [Itori](https://anilist.co/character/88415/Itori). Because of his scavenging habits and long-beaked, avian mask, he has the nickname of "Raven."', '/uploads/images/c_172074.jpg'),
(67, 'Akihiro Kanou', '嘉納明博', '配角', 'Kenji Nomura', 'Akihiro Kanou, often referred to as Professor Kanou, is a physician at Kanou General Hospital.', '/uploads/images/c_189325.png'),
(67, 'Arata Kirishima', '霧嶋新', '配角', 'Yuuya Uchida', 'Father of Touka Kirishima and Ayato Kirishima. Virtuous and gentle, Arata is a pacifist ghoul who is content to live peacefully with humans and wants the same for his children. ~!Arata''s status is currently unknown. However, it is known that his kagune is currently being used as CCG''s new exoskeleton armor.!~', '/uploads/images/c_189326.png'),
(67, 'Yoriko Kosaka', '小坂依子', '配角', 'Chinatsu Akasaki', 'A university friend of Touka''s. In :re she is revealed to be working in a bakery, often frequented by Rank1 Ghoul Inspector Takeomi Kuroiwa, son of the Special Class Ghoul Investigator Iwao Kuroiwa. ~!Takeomi proposes to Yoriko in chapter 104 of :re!~', '/uploads/images/c_189327.png'),
(67, 'Kaneki no Haha', 'カネキの母', '配角', 'Rieko Takahashi', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_189328.png'),
(67, 'Kuramoto Itou', '伊東倉元', '配角', 'Shinya Takahashi', '__Height:__ 172 cm Kuramoto Itou is a First Class Ghoul Investigator and the deputy squad leader of the Hirako Squad.', '/uploads/images/c_206156.png'),
(67, 'Hetare', 'ヘタレ', '配角', 'Sora Amamiya', 'Hetare is a cockatiel parrot who lived in Anteiku prior to its destruction. Hetare is a plump bird with pale, yellow feathers and grey wings. As is common with cockatiels, he has orange circles on his cheeks, and a wispy crest protruding from the top of his head. His most notable feature is the star mark on his left wing, hence Renji Yomo''s alternate nickname for him.', '/uploads/images/c_206209.png'),
(67, 'Kazuichi Banjou', '万丈数壱', '配角', 'Kentarou Itou', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_241488.jpg'),
(67, 'Maiko Abe', '阿倍麻衣子', '配角', 'Mayumi Asano', '__Height:__ 160 cm Maiko is a member of the Ghoul Restaurant', '/uploads/images/c_241526.png'),
(67, 'Asaki Fueguchi', '笛口 アサキ', '配角', 'Kousuke Toriumi', 'Hinami''s father.', '/uploads/images/c_241528.png'),
(67, 'Kaya Irimi', '入見カヤ', '配角', 'Fuyuka Ooura', 'Kaya Irimi is a waitress working at Anteiku.', '/uploads/images/c_241529.png'),
(67, 'Ayumu Hogi', '穂木あゆむ', '配角', 'Rui Tanabe', 'Ayumu is a First Class Investigator from the CCG and Vice-Chief of Chuu Hachikawa''s squad. Ayumu was part of the Squad 3 in the Anteiku raid.', '/uploads/images/c_241530.png'),
(67, 'Misato Gori', '五里美郷', '配角', 'Reina Ueda', 'Misato Gori is a Rank 2 Ghoul Investigator. She is currently affiliated with the 13th ward.', '/uploads/images/c_241531.png'),
(67, 'Ippei Kusaba', '草場一平', '配角', 'Taishi Murata', 'Ippei Kusaba was a Rank 3 Bureau Investigator working at CCG''s branch in the 20th ward and the partner of Yasunori Nakajima.', '/uploads/images/c_241536.png'),
(67, 'Yasunori Nakajima', '中島康智', '配角', 'Kazuhiro Oguro', 'Yasunori Nakajima is a bureau investigator working at CCG''s branch in the 20th ward and was the partner of Ippei Kusaba.', '/uploads/images/c_241541.png'),
(67, 'Older Bin-Brother', '瓶兄弟', '配角', 'Yuuki Fujiwara', 'Masked ghoul brothers and executives of Aogiri Tree. Most of the ghouls in the 11th ward of Aogiri Tree are their subordinates. It is said they strongly believe in the one eyed king''s ideology. Their Kagune is of the Bikaku type.', '/uploads/images/c_241542.png'),
(67, 'Katsuya Mabuchi', '馬淵活也', '配角', 'Shinya Takahashi', 'Katsuya Mabuchi is a ghoul investigator. He is the subordinate of Itsuki Marude and is normally seen standing beside Marude.', '/uploads/images/c_241545.png'),
(67, 'Taguchi', '田口', '配角', 'Reina Ueda', 'Taguchi is a nurse at Kanou General Hospital.', '/uploads/images/c_241546.png'),
(67, 'Souta', '宗太', '配角', 'Ooki Sugiyama', 'Souta was a member of the Ghoul Restaurant, where he went by the alias PG. He hides his face with a clown mask.', '/uploads/images/c_241549.png'),
(67, 'Kazuo Yoshida', '吉田カズオ', '配角', 'Teruyuki Tanzawa', '__Species:__ Ghoul __Height:__ 179 cm Kazuo Yoshida is a ghoul who Ken met in a dark alley and moments later was killed by Nishiki Nishio since he was feeding on his turf. He also appeared in omake at the end of some volumes and worked as Chief Instructor in the Fitness Club "ZEN."', '/uploads/images/c_241550.png'),
(67, 'Hisashi Ogura', '小倉久志', '配角', 'Teruyuki Tanzawa', 'Hisashi Ogura is a ghoul researcher. He often goes on TV programs to speak about them.', '/uploads/images/c_241553.png'),
(68, 'Akame', 'アカメ', '主角', 'Sora Amamiya', '__Height:__ 164 cm (5''4") Akame is one of the members of the Assassin''s group, Night Raid. She is the first member to attack [Tatsumi](https://anilist.co/character/64749), and comes very close to killing him. She initially appears very serious and cold-hearted, but she is actually caring and worries about the safety of her comrades. She has a younger sister named [Kurome](https://anilist.co/character/65297), who is a member of the Jaegers, and loyal to the Empire. Her Teigu is the One-Cut Killer: Murasame, a katana known for being coated in an immensely deadly poison that could kill those cut by it within seconds, as the poison itself has no antidote. ~!When she was a child, her parents had sold both her and Kurome to the Empire. There, they were placed and raised as Assassins from childhood. Akame in particular became infamous enough to earned the top rank in the Imperial Assassin Division. At some point, many of her comrades had died and she become dissatisfied and resentful towards the government. It was not until she was sent to kill former General Najenda that Akame finally defected to the Rebels after being swayed by her.!~', '/uploads/images/c_63351.jpg'),
(68, 'Tatsumi', 'タツミ', '主角', 'Souma Saitou', 'Tatsumi is a swordsman from a small village. He set out to the capital with two of his companions in hope of raising money for the village. He got separated from his friends and reaches the capital. Tatsumi was not aware of the type of place the capital really was. After a series of events centered around his naivety of the true nature of the capital he found himself being saved be Night Raid (Assassination Group) and later join them to rid the capital of its corrupt inhabitants.', '/uploads/images/c_64749.jpg'),
(68, 'Leone', 'レオーネ', '主角', 'Yuu Asakawa', '__Height:__ 170 cm (5''7) Leone is one of the older members of the assassination group, Night Raid. She has a very relaxed and a cheerful personality, which tends to display a lack of ladylike manners, such as shoving [Tatsumi](https://anilist.co/character/64749/Tatsumi) into her breasts, putting her feet on the table, or consuming large amounts of Sake. She serves as a sort of big sister figure to Tatsumi and the younger members in Night Raid, often referring to herself as "Onee-San". Despite the morally dodgy nature, she can sometimes display, Leone is not one to tolerate injustice and can be especially vicious to those who commit the vilest acts. She excels at gathering information and exercising calm judgement when necessary. Her teigu is Lionel, a teigu is in the form of a belt, when activated, it enhanced her speed, reflexes, strength, and regeneration, as well as giving her animal-like characteristics.', '/uploads/images/c_65227.jpg'),
(68, 'Mine', 'マイン', '主角', 'Yukari Tamura', '__Height:__ 155 cm (5''1) Mine is a self-proclaimed "Genius Sniper", as well as being a sharp-tongued and quick-witted member of the assassin''s group, Night Raid. She is often quick to anger, and easily irritated with those she does not know well. Despite this cold exterior, she has shown to be warm and kind to those she has opened up to. Mine wields a powerful Teigu in the form of a rifle called the "Roman Artillery: Pumpkin" that fires highly concentrated piercing shots of spirit energy. Her proficiency in its use allows her to strike any target with extreme precision. When Pumpkin''s user is in a dangerous situation, the power of its shots is​ magnified. Manga spoilers: ~!Tatsumi and Mine retired from service and settled down away from civilization where they married and had a child.!~', '/uploads/images/c_65229.jpg'),
(68, 'Lubbock', 'ラバック', '主角', 'Yoshitsugu Matsuoka', 'Lubbock is a member of the assassin group, Night Raid. He is often shown being a pervert, including trying to peep on Leone while bathing, usually these attempts end in failure. In the city, his cover is an owner of a bookstore. Lubbock''s teigu is, Infinite Uses: Cross Tail, a wire based teigu able to be used offensively and defensively ~!Rabac was 4th son born into a wealth merchant family in a region in the Empire. During his childhood as a boy he met Najenda who just moved into the region for the first time. Falling in love at first sight he left the privileged life he no longer desired to follow her into the army. Using his talent, Rabac rose through the ranks to the point where he could serve and be by her side. He would also join Najenda in her deflection to the rebellion, even going as far risk his life to change the military records of both him and her to K.I.A. Because of this he shares a somewhat antagonistic relationship Susanoo who he views as a rival for Najenda''s affections.!~', '/uploads/images/c_65231.jpg'),
(68, 'Sheele', 'シェーレ', '配角', 'Mamiko Noto', '__Age:__ Mid 20''s __Height:__ 160cm (5''3) Sheele is one of the members of the Assassin''s group, Night Raid. While she seems to be clumsy and ditzy on the surface, she''s a very caring and sweet person. She bears the Teigu "Ecstasy", a huge pair of scissors that can cut through anything. ~!Growing up in the low districts of the Capital, her clumsy nature caused many people throughout her life often consider her useless, isolating her from nearly everyone. At one point in her past, she had a friend who didn''t mind her personality but was attacked by her ex-boyfriend. Sheele killed the boyfriend in order to protect her, revealing that she had a strange talent for killing. However, in the end, this broke their friendship. Soon after, a gang-related to the man she killed earlier sought revenge against her and had already murdered her parents. Sheele defeated the group and was later scouted by the Revolutionary Army who learned of her ability. By joining, she wanted to use her talent in a way that would make her useful to others by helping fix society. She is one of the first members to warm up to Tatsumi, comforting him while he mourned his deceased friends from his home village. Later, she is attacked by Seryuu, and killed while saving Mine from harm.!~ (Source: Akame ga Kill! Wiki)', '/uploads/images/c_65233.jpg'),
(68, 'Bulat', 'ブラート', '配角', 'Katsuyuki Konishi', 'Bulat was once a high-ranking Imperial Officer known as "100 Man-Slayer Bulat". He later decided to betray the Empire when his superior was framed for not giving in to the Prime Minister''s agenda. Bulat became disgusted with the Empire that cared more for bribes, than merit regardless of how hard he worked. After leaving the Empire, he joined the Revolutionaries, and eventually Night Raid. Bulat''s teigu is the Demon Armor: Incursio an Armor-type teigu that took on the form of a short sword with a chain link tassel in its sealed form. Once released, the user was enveloped in a full body armor. ~!He died in battle, before his death at the hands of his former boss he entrusted the Incursio to [Tatsumi](https://anilist.co/character/64749/).!~', '/uploads/images/c_65235.jpg'),
(68, 'Chelsea', 'チェルシー', '配角', 'Kaori Nazuka', 'A seasoned assassin working for the Revolutionary Army, having successfully carried out countless missions. While she is somewhat aloof and carefree when not on the job, she is also extremely objective and is often quite blunt when voicing her opinions. Her Teigu, ''Gaea Foundation'', is a cosmetics box that allows her to instantly change her appearance and build at will. Later in the series: ~!she develops a crush on Tatsumi.!~', '/uploads/images/c_65237.jpg'),
(68, 'Esdeath', 'エスデス', '配角', 'Satomi Akesaka', '__Height:__ 170 cm (5''7) Esdeath is a high-ranking general of the Empire, and leader of the Jaegers. She enjoys torturing her enemies slowly, seen when she used her Teigu to put large blocks of ice in a cauldron so that the people inside would die slower and suffer more. Despite her sadistic actions, she is actually shown to have a compassionate heart when it comes to the lives of her men and others close to her. Her Teigu is called Demons Extract, which allows her to manipulate ice and mold it from nothing. ~!She is looking for love and although her expectations were high when she saw [Tatsumi](https://anilist.co/character/64749)''s skill, she smiled and fell in love with him instantly !~', '/uploads/images/c_65239.jpg'),
(68, 'Kurome', 'クロメ', '配角', 'Ayaka Oohashi', 'Kurome is a member of the Jaegers, and the younger sister of [Akame](https://anilist.co/character/63351/Akame). Like her sister, she has a big appetite and is often seen eating, usually candy. She stubbornly refuses to share her candy with even her comrades. Kurome wields an offensive Teigu like her sister, in the form of a sword named "March of the Dead: Yatsuhusa", which allows her to enslave up to 8 enemies killed with the Teigu. Also like her sister, she is extremely skilled in the art of the sword and assassination. ~!When she was a child, her parents had sold both Akame and her to the Empire.!~', '/uploads/images/c_65297.jpg'),
(68, 'Wave', 'ウェイブ', '配角', 'Yoshimasa Hosoya', 'Wave is a member of the Jaegers who is very similar to Tatsumi. He is from a small town on the coast where he served in the Imperial Navy, and brought a massive bag full of seafood with him when he joined the Jaegers. Also similar to Tatsumi, he is often used for Comic Relief. When he first arrived at the meeting room for his new group, he first encountered Bors, who ignored him shyly until the rest of the crew showed up. Like Tatsumi, Wave uses a sword in combat and has formidable skills. He Wields the Armor type Teigu, " Grand Chariot ", which is a newer version of Incursio. (Source: Akame ga Kill! Wiki)', '/uploads/images/c_65555.jpg'),
(68, 'Susanoo', 'スサノオ', '配角', 'Shintarou Asanuma', '__Age:__ Approx. 1000 __Faction:__ Night Raid __User:__ Najenda Susanoo is one of the new members of Night Raid that [Najenda](https://anilist.co/character/72267/Najenda) brought back with her from the Revolutionary Army HQ. He is a tall man with distinctive bull horns coming out of the sides of his head. He saves the members of Night Raid (except Tatsumi), who were all under the effects of a powerful poison created by Dr. Stylish. He is then caught in an explosion created by Stylish''s exploding minions, and it is revealed that he is a Human Teigu, regenerating his lost limbs immediately.', '/uploads/images/c_65559.jpg'),
(68, 'Bors', 'ボルス', '配角', 'Eiji Takemoto', 'A member of Jaegars, he was formerly a member of the Incineration Squad. His Teigu is Rubicante, a flamethrower type Teigu. Despite his looks he is married to an attractive woman and has a child. He always wears a mask and tries to hide his face; yet Esdese forcefully removes his mask at one point and claims there is nothing wrong with his face. ~!He is killed by Chelsea while trying to retreat.!~', '/uploads/images/c_65793.png'),
(68, 'Najenda', 'ナジェンダ', '配角', 'Risa Mizuno', 'Najenda, also known as The Hunk of the Rebellion is the head of the assassin group Night Raid. Taciturn, sharp-minded and level-headed, she leads the group with a surprisingly gentle but firm air. Her years of experience serving in the Empire as a general have made her a highly capable leader. Najenda is sometimes mistaken as a man due to her boyish appearance, even sometimes being nicknamed ''The Hunk of the Rebellion" by her cohorts. She tends to have a habit of telling "cold jokes" and making bad puns. Her teigu is a biological type teigu named [Susanoo](https://anilist.co/character/65559/Susanoo)', '/uploads/images/c_72267.png'),
(68, 'Seryuu Ubiquitous', 'セリュー・ユビキタス', '配角', 'Kana Hanazawa', 'Seryuu is a member of the Jaegers, formerly of the Imperial Guard. She has a strong fixation upon "Justice", originating from her father''s service in the Emperial Army and subsequent death. She also highly respected Ogre the Demon, her superior and teacher, and was heavily anguished by his death as well. Her opinion of justice is blunt, she believes the Night Raid are evil for their actions as assassins, but believes killing in service to justice is always right, which ultimately makes her opinion of murder similar to theirs if not the complete same thing. However, Seryuu has a twisted sense of right and wrong, bordering on a completely black and white view of the world. All people who serve the empire, despite the deeds they do both publicly and not, are considered good by her, while those who oppose it, even those forced to against their will, are pure evil. Her twisted view of justice has caused a level of distrust towards her by her own teammates, as well as generally the entire emperial forces, on occasion, as she brutally murdered a group of prisoners long before they could interrogate the group. (Source: Akame ga Kill! Wiki)', '/uploads/images/c_83405.png'),
(68, 'Spear', 'スピア', '配角', 'Yurika Aizawa', 'Spear was the daughter of the former Prime Minister Chouri, and a disciple of the "Temple of the Imperial Fist". (Source: Akame ga Kill! Wiki)', '/uploads/images/c_124797.png'),
(68, 'Suzuka', 'スズカ', '配角', 'Eriko Matsui', 'Suzuka is a member of the Four Rakshasa Demons, who served as the Prime Minister''s squad of executioners. (Source: Akame ga Kill! Wiki)', '/uploads/images/c_126273.jpg'),
(68, 'Gozuki', 'ゴズキ', '配角', 'Rintarou Nishi', 'Gozuki is the leader of the newly formed assassination squad of the Empire, the Elite Seven. (Source: Akame ga Kill! Wiki)', '/uploads/images/c_126274.jpg'),
(68, 'Mez', 'メズ', '配角', 'Aina Suzuki', 'Mez is the daughter of Gozuki as well as a member of the Four Rakshasa Demons, who served as the Prime Minister''s squad of executioners. (Source: Akame ga Kill! Wiki)', '/uploads/images/c_126276.jpg'),
(68, 'Daidara', 'ダイダラ', '配角', 'Anri Katsu', 'Daidara is a member of Esdeath''s former bodyguards, known as "The Three Beasts". He''s a battle fanatic who will fight anyone who seems strong, and constantly takes every opportunity to improve himself when he can. He is first introduced attacking and assassinating the former Prime Minister, along with Liver and Nyau. Later, they are ordered by Esdeath to assassinate another political rival on a cruise ship. There they encountered Tatsumi and Bulat.', '/uploads/images/c_127424.jpg'),
(68, 'Dr. Stylish', 'Dr.スタイリッシュ', '配角', 'Ken Narita', 'Dr. Stylish was a member of the Jaegers, and formerly was a Doctor in the service of the Empire. He was obsessed with being Stylish and looking good. He is however at heart a classic mad scientist caring nothing for the lives of his subjects and more concerned for his own experiments than anything else. He was however very intelligent being able to see through Tatsumi''s cover even when Esdeath could not. He has also been heavily hinted to be homosexual.', '/uploads/images/c_163191.jpg'),
(68, 'Budou', 'ブドー', '配角', 'Hozumi Gouda', 'Described as a man who rarely leaves the battlefield, General Budou is a hardened man, with years of training and military hardship shaping him to his current state. As a general born from a celebrated lineage, Budou takes great pride in his honor, and that of the empire. Unlike most generals, he doesn''t affiliate himself with the Prime Minister, and the general downright detests the pig. He even went on to state that once the rebels would be crushed, those who caused chaos in the country would incur his wrath. His teigu is called "Adrammelech," but its abilities are unknown.', '/uploads/images/c_163193.jpg'),
(68, 'Air', 'エア', '配角', '', 'Air was one of three girls who were sold to Bach, due to their village being deeply in debt by the over taxation of the Empire.', '/uploads/images/c_163196.jpg'),
(68, 'Aria', 'アリア', '配角', 'Kanami Satou', 'Aria was a girl from the capital that offered Tatsumi a place to stay when she found him on the streets after being conned by Leone. She came from a wealthy family and had a habit of offering strays a place to stay in her mansion. ~!Apparently, she and her family had an interest of luring people from the country to their place and tortured them to death. Night Raid killed her family, and Aria was killed by Tatsumi after he witnessed the death of his two friends, Sayo and Ieyasu, at the hands of Aria''s family.!~', '/uploads/images/c_163197.jpg'),
(68, 'Aria no Chichi', 'アリアの父', '配角', 'Haruo Yamagishi', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_163200.jpg'),
(68, 'Dooya', 'ドーヤ', '配角', '', 'Dooya was an assassin sent from the Northern Tribes. She was killed by Kurome and her dead body was turned into a puppet under Kurome''s command. As mentioned by Kurome, she was a confident and cheerful person and she still exhibits her confidence even as a corpse puppet. She wields two hand guns. She is shown to be an expert marksman even was able to overwhelm Mine, a self-titled "genius marksman," for a while. Because of her state as a resurrected puppet, she does not feel pain or fatigue, enabling her to fight stronger opponents such as Teigu users without possessing a Teigu herself.', '/uploads/images/c_163203.png'),
(68, 'Gamal', 'ガマル', '配角', '', 'Gamal was a corrupt oil merchant who was eventually targeted by Night Raid under contract, and killed by Leone and Akame.', '/uploads/images/c_163205.jpg'),
(68, 'Ibara', 'イバラ', '配角', 'Satoshi Hino', 'Ibara is one of the Four Temple Rakshasa Demons, a group of executioners who serve the Prime Minister. He can freely control his body to stretch his body parts and manipulate them. Ibara seems to have a cocky and bloodthirsty personality, nearly attacking Seryu upon the first meeting of the Demons and the Jaegers. He admonishes Seryu for her skepticism of the Four Demon''s abilities, and tells her that she and the Jaegers should "Just sit back and drink wine in this mansion".', '/uploads/images/c_163206.jpg'),
(68, 'Fal', 'ファル', '配角', '', 'Fal was one of three girls who were sold to Bach, due to their village being deeply in debt by the over taxation of the Empire.', '/uploads/images/c_163207.jpg'),
(68, 'Aria no Haha', 'アリアの母', '配角', 'Natsuo Nakamura', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_163208.jpg'),
(68, 'Hana', '鼻', '配角', 'Yuuki Ishikari', 'Hana was a member of Team Stylish. Hana (鼻 ・はな) mean "nose" in japanese', '/uploads/images/c_163210.jpg'),
(68, 'Honest  Daijin', 'オネスト大臣', '配角', 'Kouji Ishii', 'A large man with a demonic appearance, including a crown of horns that give the idea that they are growing out of his head. He manipulates Emperor Makoto and runs the Empire behind the scenes this way. He is the primary antagonist of the series, and hates Night Raid and the Revolutionary Army strongly. He is often shown eating. He cares very little for anything and will do anything to maintain his own power. It is stated that Emperor Makoto only won the battle of succession due to the Prime Minister''s influence and planning. The Prime Minister before him was Chouri. A man that was a kindhearted but strong will. A strong adviser to the former emperor, who desired to return to the capital to stop the decline of the empire. When the Prime Minister became aware of this he had Esdeath''s force''s (The "Three Beasts") to kill him. He is known to have one son named Syura who is currently the leader of the secret police Wild Hunt, and he is also known to have one blood relative named Iwokaru, who was killed by Night Raid.', '/uploads/images/c_163214.jpg'),
(68, 'Luna', 'ルナ', '配角', '', 'Luna was one of three girls who were sold to Bach, due to their village being deeply in debt by the over taxation of the Empire.', '/uploads/images/c_163215.jpg'),
(68, 'Liver', 'リヴァ', '配角', 'Jouji Nakata', 'Liver was the leader of Esdeath''s personal bodyguards and the strongest group in her army, known as "The Three Beasts". He was a refined and battle-hardened man, who was deeply loyal to Esdeath. He once was an accomplished General in the Empire''s army and Bulat''s superior years ago. During the Empire''s war against the Southern Lands, he was dismissed from his post due to being framed on false charges when he did not give in to the Prime Minister''s bribes. At the military tribunal he attempted to valiantly defend himself using his records and merits, but it fell on deaf ears. After ultimately being left to rot prison for the rest of his life Esdeath appeared, and in a surprising move she freed him on the condition that he would join her army. She valued his abilities and achievements, thinking that it would be a waste to leave him imprisoned. Esdeath also offered him patronage against the Prime Minister and his other enemies. Grateful for being saved and granted a new life back in the military, he became indebted to Esdeath, leading some of her most loyal men. When he and Bulat met once again for the first time in years on the cruise ship "Ryussen" with their paths in life having diverged, they battled to the death with their loyalty and ideals on the line.', '/uploads/images/c_163218.jpg'),
(68, 'Horimaka', 'ホリマカ', '配角', 'Kouhei Sugesawa', 'Owner of the teigu: Adayasu, a scythe teigu whose abilities are a mystery. Because the empire is unaware of this teigu, Horimaka is Bolick''s trump card.', '/uploads/images/c_163219.jpg'),
(68, 'Kubikiri Zank', '首斬りザンク', '配角', 'Satoshi Tsuruoka', 'Zank was once an imperial executioner. Possess the Imperial Arm Spectator, that has the form of a headpiece with a large eye attached to it. He was known for severing the heads of his victims. Night Raid was contracted to track him down and kill him.', '/uploads/images/c_163223.jpg'),
(68, 'Me', '目', '配角', 'Eiji Takeuchi', 'Me was a member of Team Stylish. Me (目 ・め) means "eye" in japanese', '/uploads/images/c_163224.jpg'),
(68, 'Nyau', 'ニャウ', '配角', 'Hitomi Nabatame', 'Nyau is a member of Esdeath''s bodyguard "The Three Beasts". Despite his playful personality and innocent looks, he was by far the most sadistic member of the group with his hobby of collecting human faces. Like the other members he was charged by Esdeath to lure out Night Raid while getting rid of the Prime Minister''s political enemies in secret. He battled with Tatsumi and Bulat aboard the cruise ship "Ryuusen" where he caused all the passengers to fall asleep by using his Teigu, Scream. ~!He was the last of the Three Beasts to fall, killed by Tatsumi in one blow after activating Incursio.!~', '/uploads/images/c_163226.jpg'),
(68, 'Ogre ', 'オーガ', '配角', 'Tsuyoshi Koyama', 'Ogre was a captain from the Capital Guard, and the former superior of Seryuu. He was also the one that recommended Dr. Stylish to Seryuu, as she wanted to become stronger. He had been accepting bribes from an oil merchant named Gamal and other criminals, and often framed innocent people to take the fall for the criminals. ~!Ogre was killed by Tatsumi, after he threatened to annihilate the client and her family.!~', '/uploads/images/c_163227.jpg'),
(68, 'Rokugou', 'ロクゴウ', '配角', 'Kento Fujinuma', 'Rokugou was a general serving The Empire before his attempt of defection which failed. He was assassinated by Kurome and became one of her puppets.', '/uploads/images/c_163228.jpg'),
(68, 'Trooma', 'トローマ', '配角', 'Shinya Hamazoe', 'He is a member of Team Stylish. Trooma is one of Dr. Stylish''s stronger henchmen. It is unknown whether he had Dr. Stylish perform experiments on him or not.', '/uploads/images/c_163230.jpg'),
(68, 'Koutei ', '皇帝', '配角', 'You Taichi', 'Koutei is the young ruler of the empire. He is shown to be a naive young boy who wishes to lead his people to a bright future. Unfortunately, due to the Prime Minister''s influence, he is largely ignorant to the suffering of his people, and is actually contributing to the collapse of The Empire.', '/uploads/images/c_163232.jpg'),
(68, 'Shura ', '修羅', '配角', 'Ryouhei Kimura', 'Shura is a mysterious individual who has recently begun to make his move. He seems to share his father''s lust for power as well as his corruption but wishes to surpass him in terms of being rotten. He created and is leading the majorly corrupt and twisted Secret Police "Wild Hunt" to aid the Jägers and to compensate for their losses; however, he regards the empire as a toy. The incident in the theater implies he solely enjoys causing carnage. Also much like Cosmina, Champ, and Enshin, Shura took part in the mass rape during the Umatora Theater incident where the producer denies the accusation of it''s plays criticizing the Empire and tries to bribe Shura, but he declines the money in a heartbeat declaring the death sentence on them leading to the entire team being raped and killed by Wild Hunt in which Shura shows his twisted side by calling this action an investigation. He then mentions that this is all because Esdeath was not present in the Capital. After his devilish act, Shura joyfully tells his father how much of a kick he gets from leading Wild Hunt telling he made preparations to take out Night Raid. Along with his father, he watches the Great General Budo arrive. ~!In Chapter 52, he tortures what he thinks is an unarmed Lubbock; however, Lubbock manages to trick Shura into removing his shackles. He then pulls some string out of his mouth and immediately kills Shura. !~', '/uploads/images/c_163233.jpg'),
(68, 'Shoui', 'ショウイ', '配角', 'Kento Fujinuma', 'He is the baron of the Empire.', '/uploads/images/c_163235.jpg'),
(68, 'Natala', 'ナタラ', '配角', '', 'Natala was a member of the Empire''s assassination group Group of Terror appearing in the prequel series Akame Ga Kill!: Zero until his death. He is now serving as one of Kurome''s main corpse puppets. Natala is one of the members of Kurome''s group of assassins. He died some time before the main story and his deceased body was reanimated by Kurome using Yatsufusa. He is later use in a battle against Night Raid, defending Kurome from her enemies. After the battle, Natala became one of the last two puppets, the other being Dooya. Natala wielded Trisula. Mine mistakenly thought it was a Teigu, but it is in fact a Shingu. Because the weapon''s design allows it to expand and contract at will, its style of killing is to cut the opponent''s body in two. Natala bifurcated Chelsea with this weapon.', '/uploads/images/c_163236.jpg'),
(68, 'Mimi', '耳', '配角', 'Ayaka Imamura', 'Mimi was a member of Team Stylish. Mimi (耳・みみ) means "ear" in japanese', '/uploads/images/c_163238.jpg'),
(68, 'Chouri', 'チョウ', '配角', 'Takehiro Hasu', 'The former prime minister and the father of Spear.', '/uploads/images/c_163239.jpg'),
(68, 'Numa Seika', 'ヌマ・セイカ', '配角', 'Yuuki Ishikari', 'Numa Seika was the Prince of the Northern Tribes. Know for his in combat and tactics abilities.', '/uploads/images/c_163240.jpg'),
(68, 'Sten', 'シュテン', '配角', 'Kenji Nomura', 'Sten is one of the Four Rakshasa Temple Demons who serve as the Prime Minister''s squad of executioners. He seems to think of murdering as "releasing one''s soul." Sten is a large man with a heavily muscled build similar to Ibara. He has a long braided hairstyle with hair sticking far out at the sides and bald at the top of his head. He has long bushy beard and mustache, bushy eyebrows, and dark prominent circles around his eyes. Similar to his fellow Rakshasa Demons, he wears armor plating on his forearms. He also wears a large Iron pauldron on his left shoulder. ~!In Chapter 36, Lubbock hits him with a spear made of threads. Sten is able to withstand the attack, but Lubbock uses the threads that pierced Sten''s body to cut his heart into pieces.!~', '/uploads/images/c_163242.jpg'),
(68, 'Toby', 'トビー', '配角', 'Shinya Takahashi', 'Toby was a member of Team Stylish.', '/uploads/images/c_163243.jpg'),
(68, 'Ieyasu', 'イエヤス', '配角', 'Kouji Takahashi', 'Ieyasu was a childhood friend of Tatsumi and Sayo that set out on a journey to the capital to earn money for their village. He seemed to have a bad sense of direction and was a known troublemaker. During their journey, they were attacked by night bandits which separated them. He managed to stay with Sayo and got invited by Aria to her mansion. They were served with a meal that made them lose consciousness. He was put on drugs which made him suffer from the "Lubora disease." He survived until Tatsumi and Night Raid arrived at the place where he, Sayo, and other people that were lured by Aria and her family, were imprisoned. He seems to be glad when Tatsumi killed Aria. He then succumbed to the last stages of "Lubora disease." Ieyasu was shown to wield an axe. He presumably possessed combat abilities on par with Tatsumi, as they and Sayo trained together since they were little.', '/uploads/images/c_163244.jpg'),
(68, 'Sayo', 'サヨ', '配角', 'Mikako Komatsu', 'She set out with Tatsumi and Ieyasu to earn money for their village. On the way, they were attacked by night bandits and got separated. Sayo managed to stay with Ieyasu while Tatsumi was separated from them. She and Ieyasu were then invited by Aria to her mansion, and she provided them with a meal that was drugged, making them lose consciousness. Sayo was then tortured to death, although she didn''t submit to Aria and her family even until the moment of her death. Tatsumi personally slays Aria after he is told the truth about Aria and her sadistic family. There is a chance that Tatsumi was in love with her, as the illusion that Zank showed revealed her to be the most important person in the world to him. Sayo was seen carrying a bow and a stack of arrows. She seemed to have good combat abilities and presumably was a well-trained archer, as Tatsumi stated that both she and Ieyasu were strong.', '/uploads/images/c_163245.jpg'),
(68, 'Gebaze', 'ゲバゼ', '配角', 'Kanehira Yamamoto', '__Eye Color:__ Black __Hair Color:__ Black __Gebaze__ was the Head of Public Finance of The Empire. He was a large man with dark hair and a small mustache who wore clothing resembling those of a sultan. Additionally around his neck he wore a golden jeweled necklace.', '/uploads/images/c_166786.png'),
(68, 'Shihandai', '師範代', '配角', 'Keiichi Kuwabara', '__Eye Color:__ Dark Blue __Hair Color:__ Blond __Shihandai__ is a rather tall man with long, blond hair which he wore in a braid. His outfit consists of a lightly armored, long white shirt and grey pants. He also wears a belt around his wasit and around his chest to attach his shoulder pieces. He was one of the bodyguards in charge of Iokal''s protection, and a former instructor at the martial arts temple of The Empire.', '/uploads/images/c_166787.png'),
(68, 'Esdeath no Chichi', 'エスデスの父', '配角', 'Daichi Endou', 'Esdeath''s Father was a tribal leader of the Partas Clan. He taught Esdeath her primary survival skills and honed her hunting abilities. He is a tall middle-aged man with light blue hair worn in a mullet-like style, as well as a short beard, and blue eyes. He wears tribal clothing consisting of a black short-sleeved turtleneck shirt, a long white kimono, and a red vest on top of it, with a sash on his waist and a golden medallion around his neck. He also wears a black headband with his clan''s symbol on it.', '/uploads/images/c_166788.png'),
(68, 'Gin', '銀', '配角', '', '__Eye Color:__ Cyan (Manga), Grey (Anime) __Hair Color:__ Blonde (Manga), Silver (Anime) __Introduction:__ Gin was a member of the Empire''s assassination group Group of Terror. __Appearance:__ She is a young girl with silver hair worn in a long ponytail. She wears a sleeveless trench coat with a dark belt, black tights, boots and gloves.', '/uploads/images/c_166789.png'),
(68, 'The First Emperor', '始皇帝', '配角', 'Riki Kagami', '__Eye Color:__ Green __Hair Color:__ Green __Introduction:__ The First Emperor was the Empire''s founder over a thousand years prior to the massive rebellion and the one who the prompted for the creation of more advanced weaponry that would serve as a means to protect his country. __Appearance:__ He is a middle-aged man with green hair, green eyes, and a beard. He wears what is now a standard attire for an Emperor, which consists of a blue mantle, a large headdress, and a golden scepter.', '/uploads/images/c_166790.png'),
(68, 'Kaiser Frog', 'カイザーフロッグ', '配角', '', '__Abilities:__ Dissolving Acid, Enhanced Tongue __Introduction:__ Kaiser Frog is a giant, frog type Danger Beast species __Appearance:__ It has the appearance of a giant, frog creature. It is green with red spots and yellow eyes. It was considered the strongest of all frogs in the world and was known to have incredibly strong stomach acid that can dissolve anything they swallow. It also has a long tongue which can be used to grab prey. ~! Thie particular Kaiser Frog was revealed during Kurome and Bols'' battle against Night Raid to be one of Kurome''s newest puppets. !~', '/uploads/images/c_166791.png'),
(68, 'Cornelia', 'コーネリア', '配角', '', '__Height:__ 168 cm (5''6'''') __Eye Color:__ Blue __Hair Color:__ Blonde __Introduction:__ Cornelia was a member of the Empire''s Assassination group (former group of Akame). __Appearance:__ Cornelia is a young girl with long blonde hair and blue eyes. She wears a long white shirt with black pants and shoes. She also wears silver hoop earrings.', '/uploads/images/c_166792.png'),
(68, 'Henter', 'ヘンター', '配角', '', '__Henter__ was a survivor of the Ban Tribe. He was known to possess remarkable skill with knives, and for his tricky movement. He was killed by Kurome and was turned into one of her corpse puppets.', '/uploads/images/c_166793.png'),
(68, 'Kije', 'キジェ', '配角', '', '__Age:__ Mid 20s __Eye Color:__ Purple __Hair Color:__ Light Brown Kije is Bols'' wife. She is known to be cheerful, very loving and caring towards Bols.', '/uploads/images/c_166794.png'),
(68, 'Najasho', 'ナジャショ', '配角', '', '__Height:__ 162 cm (5''4'''') __Eye Color:__ Golden __Hair Color:__ Blond Najasho is a member of the Empire''s Assassination group (former group of Akame). He is the leader of the Elite Seven and is called "Chief" by the members.', '/uploads/images/c_166796.png'),
(68, 'Ritone', 'リトネ', '配角', '', 'Ritone is one of the spies for the Revolutionary Army. He is partnered up with [Pais.](https://anilist.co/character/166798)', '/uploads/images/c_166797.png'),
(68, 'Pais', 'パイス', '配角', '', 'Pais is one of the spies for the Revolutionary Army. She''s partnered with [Ritone](https://anilist.co/character/166797).', '/uploads/images/c_166798.png'),
(68, 'Bill', 'ビル', '配角', 'Youji Ueda', 'Bill (otherwise known as Uncle Bill) was the leader of The Empire''s assassination group, Group of Terror.', '/uploads/images/c_166799.png'),
(68, 'Death Tagool', 'デスタグール', '配角', '', '__Class:__ Super Class __Abilities:__ Energy Beams, Enhanced Physical Abilities Death Tagool is a giant dinosaur-like Danger Beast species.', '/uploads/images/c_166800.png'),
(68, 'Logue', 'ローグ', '配角', 'Konomi Tada', 'Bols'' daughter.', '/uploads/images/c_166801.png'),
(68, 'Guy', 'ガイ', '配角', '', 'Guy was a member of the Empire''s Assassination group (former group of Akame).', '/uploads/images/c_166802.png'),
(68, 'Jijo', '侍女', '配角', 'Rika
 Mayama', 'The Palace maid was one of the revolutionaries who was tasked with assisting Tatsumi and Lubbock with infiltrating the royal palace.', '/uploads/images/c_166803.png'),
(68, 'Green', 'グリーン', '配角', '', 'Green is a member of the Empire''s Assassination group (former group of Akame)', '/uploads/images/c_166804.png'),
(68, 'Tsukushi', 'ツクシ', '配角', '', 'Tsukushi was a member of the Empire''s Assassination group (former group of Akame).', '/uploads/images/c_166805.png'),
(68, 'Iokal', 'ロラク', '配角', '', 'Iokal was a blood relative of the Prime Minister Honest.', '/uploads/images/c_166806.png'),
(68, 'Bolic ', 'ボリック', '配角', 'Masami Iwasaki', 'Bolic was a spy working for the Prime Minister Honest posing as a high-ranking individual of the Path of Peace. His goal was to kill the leader of the Path of Peace without revealing his true identity and take his place, so that the Empire could manipulate the religious organization for its own purposes.', '/uploads/images/c_166807.png'),
(68, 'Apeman', 'エイプマン', '配角', '', 'Apeman is a large, gorilla-like Danger Beast species.', '/uploads/images/c_166808.png'),
(68, 'Wall', 'ウォール', '配角', '', 'Wall was a famous guardsmanwho used a riot shield as his main weapon.', '/uploads/images/c_166809.png'),
(68, 'Poney', 'ポニ', '配角', '', 'Poney is a member of The Empire''s assassination group Elite Seven (former group of Akame). She uses the Shingu Yocto-bottoms.', '/uploads/images/c_166810.png'),
(68, 'Hekatonkheires', '魔獣変化', '配角', '', 'Magical Beast Transformation: Hekatonkheires, also known by its nickname Koro, was a biological Teigu owned by Seryu Ubiquitous who was often seen with her.', '/uploads/images/c_198089.jpg'),
(68, 'Shoufu', '娼婦', '配角', 'Ayaka Fukuyama', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_244784.png'),
(69, 'Shinichi Izumi', '泉新一', '主角', 'Nobunaga Shimazaki', 'Shinichi is a thoughtful, compassionate high-school boy whose hand is infected with a Parasite. Shinichi is repeatedly put into difficult positions. He must find a way to peacefully coexist with [Migi](https://anilist.co/character/13773/Migi), the Parasite which has taken over his hand, and reconcile his desire to protect humanity from the Parasites with his desire to keep his own Parasite a secret in order to avoid being killed or used as a laboratory specimen. Like a superhero with a secret identity, he must also find a way to explain away his Parasite-fighting activities, as well as the stress and grief they cause him, to his friends and family. Shinichi''s retention of a human mind, emotion, and sensibilities causes other Parasites to see him as a threat. He and his Parasite must defend themselves from attacks by other Parasites, and their ability to think and act independently, and as a team, gives them a tactical edge over normal Parasites.', '/uploads/images/c_12323.jpg'),
(69, 'Migi', 'ミギー', '主角', 'Aya Hirano', 'Migi is the Parasite which lives in [Shinichi](https://anilist.co/character/12323)''s hand. Unlike "successful" Parasites, Migi has no desire to kill humans for sustenance, and is nourished by the food Shinichi eats. Migi is, like other Parasites, completely without emotion. His primary consideration is survival, and he has threatened (and in some cases attempted) to kill other humans who pose a threat to he and Shinichi''s secrecy. When he and Shinichi were first coming to terms, he even threatened to remove Shinichi''s other limbs in order to render him unable to place the two of them in danger. Migi can be reasoned with, however, and has just as much reason to be mistrustful of other Parasytes as does Shinichi. On the other hand, unlike Shinichi, Migi has no inclination to place himself at risk in order to protect other humans from Parasites. As the series goes along however, he becomes more human, whereas the reverse happens to Shinichi, up until an event involving a baby occurs.', '/uploads/images/c_13773.jpg'),
(69, 'Ryouko Tamiya', '田宮良子', '配角', 'Atsuko Tanaka', 'Shinichi''s substitute math teacher. She is infected with a parasite.', '/uploads/images/c_16586.jpg'),
(69, 'Kana Kimishima', '君嶋加奈', '配角', 'Miyuki Sawashiro', 'Kana is a disobedient "bad girl" who develops a crush on Shinichi. She is attracted to him because of his sensitive personality, and because she can sense something "different" about him. ~!In reality, Kana has an unexplained psychic ability to sense parasites. However, her senses are not as fine-tuned as those of the parasites themselves, and she cannot tell whether she is sensing the presence of Shinichi or of a normal parasite, putting her in considerable danger.!~ (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_19215.jpg'),
(69, 'Satomi Murano', '村野里美', '配角', 'Kana Hanazawa', 'Shinichi''s best friend and sometime companion. Shinichi and Satomi develop a romantic relationship over the course of the series, but their attraction to and fondness for one another is hampered by Shinichi''s fear of his own monstrous nature, and Satomi''s fear of Shinichi''s secretive behavior and the mood swings that result from the trials and tribulations in his life.', '/uploads/images/c_19436.jpg'),
(69, 'A', 'A', '配角', 'Makoto Yasumura', 'Mr. A is a Parasite who considers Shinichi a threat. Reiko calls him a fool while Migi describes him as "not one of our smart ones." Mr. A has no capacity for subtlety or deception, and no qualms about using his shapeshifting abilities in view of the public, reasoning that he can always get out of trouble by fighting, running away, and changing into a different face. Mr. A (or rather, his host body) is the father of Reiko''s child. Shinichi is forced to battle Mr. A when he attempts to hunt Shinichi down and kill him at school. Though Shinichi and Migi badly wound him, they are forced to flee before he can be completely destroyed. He is killed after their battle by Tamura Reiko for endangering her undercover lifestyle.', '/uploads/images/c_22141.jpg'),
(69, 'Nobuko Izumi', '泉信子', '配角', 'Chieko Sasai', 'Shinichi''s mother. 40 years old. Housewife. ~!She "dies" early on when she is taken over by a Parasite, and stabs Shinichi through the heart when he refuses to accept it; she is then killed later on by a tag team of Shinichi and Uda.!~ (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_22143.jpg'),
(69, 'Hideo Shimada', '島田秀雄', '配角', 'Akira Ishida', 'Hideo is a Parasite with a teenager''s body who decides to integrate with human society. Hideo enrolls in Shinichi''s high school and expresses a desire to become friends with Shinichi, who does not trust him. Although Hideo is a relatively peaceful Parasite, he has no qualms about brutalizing or even killing bullies who try to start fights with him, and he continues to hunt humans (although he claims that he is learning to eat normal food instead). He is killed by Shinichi and Migi after another student discovers his secret and confronts him about it, causing him to go on a killing spree. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_22144.jpg'),
(69, 'Gotou', '後藤', '配角', 'Kazuhiko Inoue', 'Gotou is an "experimental" Parasite created by Reiko. He is actually composed of several combined Parasites, whose shapeshifting ability has advanced to the point where they can switch positions, each forming a different limb as the situation requires. Gotō is the most intelligent and skilled, and is the de facto leader of the composite body. Because his head and all of his limbs are made of Parasite cells, Gotō is much faster, stronger, and more dangerous than standard Parasites, and nearly impossible to injure. Gotō is the last Parasite that Shinichi and Migi take down; Gotō actually ends up causing the temporary death of Migi, and absorbs Migi into his body for a small period of time. Shinichi is left with only one arm during this period, but manages to recover Migi and secures victory. The name "Gotō" is a pun on a word "五 Go" meaning number 5, implying he can control 5 Parasites, whereas the other Parasyte in the same body called Miki (三木 Miki lit. Three trees) can control only 3. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_22145.jpg'),
(69, 'Takeshi Hirokawa', '広川剛志', '配角', 'Yuu Mizushima', 'Hirokawa is the leader of a cabal of Parasites which counts Reiko and Goto among its members. The group attempts to accrue political power in order to set up safehouses where they can take their victims, killing and eating them in secret. Hirokawa gains election to the office of mayor in East Fukuyama City, a small town (by Japanese standards) of 500,000 people close to Shinichi''s hometown. Hirokawa wins by running on a campaign centered around locally-based environmentalism. ~!Secretly, Hirokawa is a radical environmentalist who believes that the Parasites'' purpose is to cull the human population, standing one step above them on the food chain. The police force kills Hirokawa and discovers that he was 100% human and a Parasite sympathizer.!~ (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_22147.jpg'),
(69, 'Kamijou', '上条', '配角', 'Yuuya Murakami', 'Student at the same school as Shinichi.', '/uploads/images/c_71953.png'),
(69, 'Mitsuo', 'ミツオ', '配角', 'KENN', 'Student of Kita High School. Likes Kana. Gets jealous and beats up Shinichi.', '/uploads/images/c_71955.png'),
(69, 'Mitsuyo', '美津代', '配角', 'Seiko Fujiki', 'Old Lady that helps Izumi Shinichi at the end of the story.', '/uploads/images/c_72223.png'),
