(97, 'Tenjouyaburi', '天井破り', '配角', 'Takashi Onozuka', 'He was a spirit who appeared early on in the series. He was the first ghost to appear and be exorcized.', '/uploads/images/c_133383.png'),
(97, 'Hiroshi Kumagawa', '隈川弘', '配角', 'Shunsuke Takeuchi', 'He is part of the Body Improvement Club and a student of Salt Middle School.', '/uploads/images/c_133384.png'),
(97, 'Hideki  Yamamura', '山村秀樹', '配角', 'Daiki Hamano', 'He is a student of Salt Middle School and a member of the Body Improvement Club.', '/uploads/images/c_133385.png'),
(97, 'Momozou  Takenaka', '竹中桃蔵', '配角', 'Ikuji Nose', 'Takenaka is originally introduced as an image-conscientious character pushed into the Telepathy Club similarly to Mob. However, once it is revealed that he is a Telepath, he is shown to be standoffish despite his humor and tendency to tease others. He feels lonely given his telepathy and is overwhelmed by the consciousness of society. ~!Takenaka had previously filled a gap in the Telepathy Club to maintain the minimum number of members needed for the club. He had no interest in the club or in telepathy. He worried about how people looked at him because of his club membership, so he decided to leave the club. As a result of him leaving the club, Tome Kurata had to find a new member to keep the club open. He is later revealed to have joined the tennis club. In chapter 98 he is revealed to be a telepath. He returned to their former club room investigate the telepathic ringing generated by Mob and Shiratori brothers. He is subsequently recruited to help contact extraterrestrial life, although he only joins out of obligation. Later, he is revealed to have actually memorized the summoning formation and incantation despite knowing it to be a hoax, as he didn''t want to ruin their memory. He proceeds to spend his New Years'' with the others after successfully coming into contact with alien lifeforms.!~', '/uploads/images/c_133388.jpg'),
(97, 'Jun Sagawa', '佐川純', '配角', 'Seiichirou Yamashita', 'He is a student of Salt Middle School and the president of the Body Improvement Club.', '/uploads/images/c_133389.jpg'),
(97, 'Hanako', '花子', '配角', 'Tomomi Watanabe', 'She is Reigen''s first client to appear in the series. ~!Hanako had engaged in a sort of test of courage before coming to see Reigen; consequently, a ghost has been haunting her in her dreams. She had asked many psychics to help her and get rid of the ghost and eventually, accompanied by her boyfriend Taro, she asks for help from Arataka Reigen. She guides Reigen and Taro to the building with the ghost in question, after much scepticism about Reigen coming from her boyfriend. She recounts a tale of a man who struck his head on the ceiling of the building after seeing a cockroach, frightening Reigen. The ghost, Ceiling Crasher, haunting her appears, leading Reigen to attempt to exorcise it (unsuccessfully). Reigen calls in Mob, who exorcizes​ the ghost in front of her.!~', '/uploads/images/c_133390.jpg'),
(97, 'Tarou', '太郎', '配角', 'Wataru Hatano', 'Tarou is Hanako''s lover and a character that appears early on in the series. He is an aggressive skeptic of the supernatural and of psychics. He seems protective or relatively concerned about his lover.', '/uploads/images/c_133391.png'),
(97, 'Nioikagi', '匂い嗅ぎ', '配角', 'Kouzou Douzaka', 'He was a spirit who appeared and made his home terrorizing the students at a private girls'' high school.', '/uploads/images/c_133392.png'),
(97, 'Haruto  Kijibayashi', '稚子林春人', '配角', 'Ryuunosuke Watanuki', 'He is a third-year middle school student and a member of the Telepathy Club.', '/uploads/images/c_133395.png'),
