(126, 'Kyohei  Morishige', '森重挙兵', '配角', '', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_137031.jpg'),
(126, 'Higashio', '東尾', '配角', 'Hiroki Matsukawa', 'He is an esper and one of Sho Suzuki''s subordinates.', '/uploads/images/c_137032.png'),
(126, 'Koga', '古賀', '配角', '', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_137033.jpg'),
(126, 'Otsuki', '大月', '配角', 'Ryouta Iwasaki', 'He is an esper and one of Sho Suzuki''s subordinates.', '/uploads/images/c_137035.png'),
(126, 'Yanagawa', '柳川', '配角', '', 'He is an esper and former leader of actually disbanded terrorist organization Claw''s 4th Division.', '/uploads/images/c_137036.png'),
(126, 'Joseph', 'ヨシフ', '配角', 'Tasuku Hatanaka', 'He is an esper mercenary and assassin hired by the government.', '/uploads/images/c_137037.png'),
(126, 'Hiroshi Yabe', '矢部博司', '配角', 'Masafumi Kimura', 'He is a Prime Minister abducted by Shimazaki.', '/uploads/images/c_137038.jpg'),
(126, 'Sugimoto', '杉本', '配角', '', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_137039.jpg'),
(126, 'Hiroshi Shibata', '柴田宏', '配角', 'Kenta Miyake', 'He is a (formerly powerful) esper and a former member of the terrorist organization​ Claw as a part of the Ultimate 5.', '/uploads/images/c_137040.jpg'),
(126, 'Ishihara', '石原', '配角', '', 'He is an esper and former member of actually disbanded terrorist organization Claw''s 4th Division', '/uploads/images/c_137041.png'),
(126, 'Suzuki no Tsuma', '鈴木の妻', '配角', 'Houko Kuwashima', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_138286.png'),
(127, 'Hyakkimaru', '百鬼丸', '主角', 'Hiroki Suzuki', 'Hyakkimaru is the central character of Tezuka''s best-known samurai story, Dororo. A powerful warrior, Hyakkimaru is traveling on a long quest to retrieve 48 parts of his body which were sold to demons by his father at his birth. This is a very dramatic adventure series, with a great variety of unusual mythological creatures and demons, as well as bandits and other fierce foes. Gradually the grim experiences of his travels make Hyakkimaru more and more distant and grim, so as he recovers more and more of his human body he becomes at the same time less and less human.', '/uploads/images/c_14864.png'),
(127, 'Dororo', 'どろろ', '主角', 'Rio Suzuki', '~!__Gender__: Female!~ After seeing his swordsmanship, Dororo decides to follow Hyakkimaru. Dororo was a thief before meeting Hyakkimaru. ~!Dororo''s bandit father Hibukuro was wounded by a samurai official and later died. Her mother froze to death while fleeing in the snow, but before she died she drew a map on Dororo''s back to locate money hidden by her father at Bone Cape. Hyakkimaru learns that Dororo is female with the latter continuously insisting she is a boy, though this is because her parents raised her as one.!~', '/uploads/images/c_18130.jpg'),
(127, 'Biwamaru', '琵琶丸', '配角', 'Mutsumi Sasaki', 'Biwamaru (sometimes Biwa Maru) is a blind, itinerant acupuncture doctor, who wanders around Japan curing all sorts of ailments with miraculous speed. He is extremely disheveled in appearance, dressed in rags and walking with a twisted stick as a cane, and a rough bundle on his back. Biwamaru is effective, like Black Jack, an unlicensed doctor, since his practices are considered to be quackery by the medical establishment, while Biwamaru considers it barbaric to cut open a patient to cure them. This, as with Dr. Kiriko, Biwamaru is another nemesis who is too similar to Black Jack for the two to forgive their differences. Biwamaru also features in Tezuka’s best-known samurai manga, Dororo. ~!When Biwamaru came to Black Jack''s town in issue #126 ''The Blind Doctor of Acupuncture,'' (6/7/1976) it was hatred at first sight, as each dismissed the other as a quack, though neither was able to deny the effectiveness of the other’s treatments. To make matters worse, Biwamaru charges nothing for his services, in contrast with Black Jack''s outrageous fees, leading to criticism of Black Jack by the local community. Their interaction here effectively degenerated into each attempting repeatedly to prove that the other was a quack, and generally failing, though teaching each other bitter lessons about the limitations of their methods. The two met again not long afterwards in issue #141, ''Death of Hyojisai'' (The Master Forger, Two People at the Thermal Bath) when they met at a hot spring and di', '/uploads/images/c_24843.jpg'),
(127, 'Kagemitsu Daigo', '醍醐景光', '配角', 'Naoya Uchida', 'Daigo was the lord of Ishikawa domain which was ravaged by floods and starvation due to poor harvest. He made a deal with a group of 48 devils (12 in 2019 version) in order to save his domain and to aggrandise his power. He promises each devil a body part from his unborn child in exchange for the power to take over the land. ~!Towards the end of episode 24, while dying from the side effects of having made a pact with the demons, he is seen regretting having sold his son to the demons and realises that it was the will of Hyakkimaru to live on that the demons craved for and that perhaps, if he had succeeded his reign, the prosperity that he desired would have been fulfilled.!~', '/uploads/images/c_33887.jpg'),
(127, 'Narrator', 'ナレーター', '配角', 'Mugihito', 'This character page is set to represent and list all narrators, which haven''t been given a visual representation of themselves in their respective work. Please add other narrator characters, which were given a visual representation of themselves, separately from this narrator page.', '/uploads/images/c_36309.jpg'),
(127, 'Nuinokata', '縫の方', '配角', 'Chie Nakamura', 'Daigo''s wife, mother of Hyakkimaru and Tahoumaru.', '/uploads/images/c_133066.jpg'),
(127, 'Jukai', '寿海', '配角', 'Akio Ootsuka', 'A skilled doctor and surgeon who used healing magic and alchemical methods to give the child who became Hyakkimaru prostheses crafted from the remains of children who had died in the war.', '/uploads/images/c_133745.jpg'),
(127, 'Denkichi', 'でん吉', '配角', 'Takamaru  Seko', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_133821.jpg'),
(127, 'Tahoumaru Daigo', '醍醐多宝丸', '配角', 'Shouya Chiba', 'Brother of Hyakkimaru and the second son (successor) of Kagemitsu Daigo. Born after Hyakkimaru was abandoned.', '/uploads/images/c_133823.jpg'),
(127, 'Bandai', 'バンダイ', '配角', 'Mami Koyama', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_133824.jpg'),
(127, 'Mio', '未央', '配角', 'Nana Mizuki', 'Mio is a young girl who lived in an abandoned temple with orphans who lost their parents in the war. She is kind and caring as she tends to put others in priority instead of herself.', '/uploads/images/c_133825.jpg'),
(127, 'Kaname', '要', '配角', 'Kouhei Amasaki', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_135268.jpg'),
(127, 'Kane-Kozou', '鐘小僧', '配角', 'Riki Kitazawa', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_135269.jpg'),
(127, 'Osushi Niki', 'ニキお寿司', '配角', 'Marina Inoue', 'She is Tanosuke''s younger sister and a girl who cares deeply for her brother. She begs Hyakkimaru to spare Tanosuke''s life, but after her brother dies, she directs her resentment toward Hyakkimaru and drives him out of the village. In contrast, she bids Dororo a kind farewell, telling him to take care of himself.', '/uploads/images/c_135270.jpg'),
(127, 'Takebo', '丈簿', '配角', 'Yuka Terasaki', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_135271.jpg'),
(127, 'Tanosuke Niki', 'ニキ田之助', '配角', 'Hiroki Takahashi', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_135272.png'),
(127, 'Ohagi', 'おはぎ', '配角', 'Yuuko Kaida', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_135646.png'),
(127, 'Yajiro', '弥次郎', '配角', 'Fuminori Komatsu', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_135956.jpg'),
(127, 'Itachi', 'イタチ', '配角', 'Setsuji Satou', 'A bandit who betrayed Dororo''s father Hibukuro and sided with the authorities.', '/uploads/images/c_136576.png'),
(127, 'Ojiya', 'お自夜', '配角', 'Ayumi Fujimura', 'She is a bandit along with her husband, Hibukuro. She is the mother of Dororo.', '/uploads/images/c_136989.png'),
(127, 'Mutsu', 'むつ', '配角', 'Mariko Munakata', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_136990.jpg'),
(127, 'Hibukuro', '火袋', '配角', 'Kenta Miyake', 'He is the leader of a bandit clan that is devoted into raiding samurai forts. He is the father of Dororo', '/uploads/images/c_136991.png'),
(127, 'Hyogo', '兵庫', '配角', 'Kenichirou Matsuda', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_136992.jpg'),
(127, 'Saru', 'さる', '配角', 'Aki Kanada', 'He is a young boy, whose parents died when he was little. He used to live in the mountains all alone​ before he met a kind woman named Oume who took him in.', '/uploads/images/c_136993.jpg'),
(127, 'Souryo', '僧侶', '配角', 'Yoshihito Sasaki', 'His real name is unknown. He is a monk/priest who was in the temple Hall of Hell​ before Kagemitsu Daigo came and killed him.', '/uploads/images/c_136994.png'),
(127, 'Oume', '青梅', '配角', 'Sanae Kobayashi', 'She is a kind woman who takes care of an orphan boy called Saru after she found him alone in the mountains.', '/uploads/images/c_137172.jpg'),
(127, 'Sukeroku', '助六', '配角', 'Junko Takeuchi', 'He is the orphan that separates​ from his mother during the land split by the Banmon.', '/uploads/images/c_137173.png'),
(127, 'Okaka', 'おかか', '配角', 'Ayumi Fujimura', 'She is a young lady who lived in a small cottage which Dororo and Hyakkimaru encountered along their journey. She initially appeared to be a kind, compassionate individual, allowing the two to stay in her cottage for shelter. However, she was, in truth, the spirit of a Buddha Statue carver who lived a very long time ago', '/uploads/images/c_138121.png'),
(127, 'Maimai-onba', 'ミマイオンブ', '配角', 'Ayano Hamaguchi', 'She is one of the twelve demons that made a contract with Daigo Kagemitsu. She hypnotized Sabame to become his lover and do her bidding by killing Hyakkimaru and Dororo, so her offspring can eat them. However, she was unable to succeed.', '/uploads/images/c_138198.jpg'),
(127, 'Sabame', '鯖目', '配角', 'Kouji Yusa', 'He is the landlord of a mountain village. He had been hypnotized by the Maimai-onba to become her lover and being manipulated to kill Hyakkimaru and Dororo so that her offspring can eat them.', '/uploads/images/c_138199.jpg'),
(127, 'Youkai Kozo', '妖怪コゾ', '配角', 'Ikue Ootani', 'is the spirit of a deceased child who once lived in an orphanage in the mountains. Some time ago He along with the nun, the other orphans and the orphanage, burned down in a fire.', '/uploads/images/c_138526.png'),
(127, 'Jisho Ama Yuurei', '地所尼幽霊', '配角', 'Harumi Ueda', 'is the spirit of a deceased nun who once ran an orphanage in the mountains. Some time ago, She, along with the orphans and the orphanage, burned down in a fire.', '/uploads/images/c_138527.png'),
(127, 'Shiranui', '不知火', '配角', 'Ryuuichi Kijima', 'He s a lonely fisherman who seems to be the owner of two huge shark demons, Jiromaru and Saburomaru. But in reality, he is more of a slave to them.', '/uploads/images/c_138647.png'),
(127, 'Munetsuna', 'ムネツナ', '配角', 'Kazuhiro Yamaji', 'He is the father of Okowa and is known as the best swordmaker in the region. Although he makes a living by making swords, he has expressed discontent with the products he has made and wishes that he would make a sword for peace and not bloodshed. He fix up and sharpen Hyakkimaru''s blades.', '/uploads/images/c_139479.png'),
(127, 'Okowa', 'オコワ', '配角', 'Yume Miyamoto', 'She is the daughter of Munetsuna. She is the second love interest of Hyakkimaru after Mio. Okowa is a cheerful girl, but with childish attitude.', '/uploads/images/c_139480.png'),
(127, 'Saburota', 'サブロータ', '配角', 'Yuuichi Nakamura', 'He claims to be a courageous man wanting to kill the demon. But in reality, he''s a coward that submitted himself to Nue after being frightened to death from seeing people being devoured by the demon. From that day onwards, he even helped the beasts to lure any travellers into its territory and devour them bit by bit.', '/uploads/images/c_139935.png'),
(127, 'Nyoubou', '女房', '配角', 'Ayano Hamaguchi', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_331875.jpg'),
(128, 'Thorfinn Karlsefni', 'トルフィン・カルルセヴニ', '主角', 'Yuuto Uemura', '__Birthyear:__ 996 __Height:__ 100 cm (6-7 years old), 153 cm (16-18 years old), 155 cm (19 years old) Thorfinn is a courageous young man armed with two twin blades he inherited from his deceased [father](https://anilist.co/character/13021). He''s traveling with [Askeladd](https://anilist.co/character/13020), who is the leader of a ruthless group of mercenaries who take jobs from whoever they think can offer them a reasonable reward. Besides, Askeladd is the man who killed Thorfinn''s father, Thors, and the only reason Thorfinn is traveling with Askeladd is so he can defeat him in a duel and win back his father''s pride. Thorfinn only wants to win his father''s pride with a fair duel. Askeladd only agrees to these duels when Thorfinn completes a certain task (like bringing him the head of the opposing armies general on the battlefield). He does not fight for the love of battle, but is still prone to losing his composure when in combat. This hotheadedness often costs him battles against more experienced opponents.', '/uploads/images/c_10138.png'),
(128, 'Askeladd', 'アシェラッド', '主角', 'Naoya Uchida', 'Askeladd is the commander of a small but powerful Viking band, which owed its success to Askeladd''s exceptional intelligence. Ten years before the main Vinland Saga storyline, Askeladd accepted a contract to assassinate [Thors](https://anilist.co/character/13021), father of [Thorfinn](https://anilist.co/character/10138). During the Viking invasion and war in England, he manipulated Thorfinn''s desire for revenge against him as a way of keeping the gifted young fighter in his service. Askeladd is one of the most skilled fighters in the series, and is particularly adept at predicting his opponents'' moves in combat. Askeladd shares the name of Askeladden, a Norwegian folk character known for his cleverness. ~!He is half-Danish and half-Welsh, being the son of a Welsh princess captured by a Viking raider. He believes in the legend of Avalon, which inspired him to support Prince [Canute](https://anilist.co/character/17438)''s bid for kingship of the Danes and ultimately sacrifices himself assassinating King [Sweyn](https://anilist.co/character/27957) in order to install Canute as the Danish King and to ensure the safety of Wales from Denmark.!~', '/uploads/images/c_13020.png'),
(128, 'Thors Snorresson', 'トールズ・スノーレソン', '配角', 'Kenichirou Matsuda', '__Height:__ 180 cm (5''11") Thors is the father of [Thorfinn](https://anilist.co/character/10138), a Jomsviking general whose phenomenal combat prowess earns him the epithet "The Troll of Jom". Thors grows weary of battle after the birth of his children, fakes his own death, and retires to become a pacifist farmer. Thors is largely considered the greatest fighter to appear in the series, having defeated the likes of Askeladd and [Thorkell](https://anilist.co/character/17440) in single combat. Such was his strength that Floki was unwilling to engage him directly, even with an entire squadron of Jomsviking warriors. Unlike his son, Thors has no explicit or implied historical basis.', '/uploads/images/c_13021.png'),
(128, 'Canute Svenson', 'クヌート', '主角', 'Kenshou Ono', '__Birthyear:__ 996 __Height:__ 170 cm Canute is the prince of the Danes. He is initially portrayed as timid and womanly, with a bishounen appearance and inability to function without his retainer [Ragnar](https://anilist.co/character/82533). These traits, along with his strong Christianity, earn him the mockery of the Vikings with whom he works. ~!After Ragnar''s death, however, he has a sharp reversal of personality, becomes strong and kingly, and develops an ambition to create utopia on earth before God''s return. Towards this end, he plots to overthrow his father [Sweyn Forkbeard](https://anilist.co/character/27957) and take the crown of the Danes. Canute is based on the historical King Canute the Great, the most prominent Danish ruler of England.!~', '/uploads/images/c_17438.png'),
(128, 'Thorkell', 'トルケル', '配角', 'Akio Ootsuka', '__Height:__ 230 cm (7''7") Thorkell is a Jomsviking general and brother of the Jomsviking Chief. A giant man who loves combat, Thorkell defected from the Danish army to become a mercenary for the English, believing that fighting his fellow Vikings will give him a better challenge. This same love of war leads him to support Prince [Canute](https://anilist.co/character/17438)''s bid for kingship of the Danes. Before [Thors](https://anilist.co/character/13021)'' defection he works with and highly respects the man, and bears a fondness for his son [Thorfinn](https://anilist.co/character/10138) in the main plot. He duels twice with Thorfinn and dominates each time, though he loses two fingers in the first duel and an eye in the second. In battle, Thorkell typically wields a pair of axes as his primary weapons, but his greatest asset is probably his vast physical strength. During a skirmish with [Askeladd](https://anilist.co/character/13020)''s band, he hurled a spear with such force that it skewered three men at once, despite having been thrown from several hundred feet away. Thorkell''s character is based on Thorkell the Tall, a historical Jomsviking lord who is a mentor to Canute in the Flateyjarbók. ~!Joined Canute as his servant after seeing him change in front of Askeladd and Thorfinn.!~', '/uploads/images/c_17440.png'),
(128, 'Bjorn', 'ビョルン', '配角', 'Hiroki Yasumoto', 'Bjorn is [Askeladd](https://anilist.co/character/13020)''s second in command, a burly man who fights for the love of combat. He is a berserker, able to enter powerful rages through the consumption of certain mushrooms.', '/uploads/images/c_19485.png'),
(128, 'Leif Erikson', 'レイフ', '配角', 'Youji Ueda', '__Birthyear:__ 965 __Height:__ 152 cm (4''11") ~!An explorer who joins [Thorfinn](https://anilist.co/character/10138) in his quest to find paradise.!~', '/uploads/images/c_19486.png'),
(128, 'Willibald', 'ヴィリバルド', '配角', 'Satoshi Hino', 'A 23-year-old Friar who travels with and mentors Prince [Canute](https://anilist.co/character/17438). He enjoys alcohol and is searching for true love.', '/uploads/images/c_20704.jpg'),
(128, 'Ylva', 'ユルヴァ', '配角', 'Hitomi Nabatame', 'She is [Thorfinn](https://anilist.co/character/10138)''s older sister. After Thorfinn has set on a journey to avenge his father, [Thors](https://anilist.co/character/13021), she takes care of household and [her mother](https://anilist.co/character/141589).', '/uploads/images/c_27876.jpg'),
(128, 'Sweyn', 'スヴェン', '配角', 'Takayuki Sugou', 'Danish king who managed to conquer almost the entirety of England and Wales, all the while keeping control of his more northern kingdoms. Father of [Canute](https://anilist.co/character/17438). ~!After being provoked by Sweyn, [Askeladd](https://anilist.co/character/13020) executes the king by cutting off his head with a sword.!~', '/uploads/images/c_27957.png'),
(128, 'Narrator', 'ナレーター', '配角', 'Kenichirou Matsuda', 'This character page is set to represent and list all narrators, which haven''t been given a visual representation of themselves in their respective work. Please add other narrator characters, which were given a visual representation of themselves, separately from this narrator page.', '/uploads/images/c_36309.jpg'),
(128, 'Ragnar', 'ラグナル', '配角', 'Jin Urayama', 'He is the main adviser for Prince [Canute](https://anilist.co/character/17438). Ragnar is bald apart from very long, black, curly hair on the sides of his head. He has very thick black eyebrows that lie close to his deepset eyes. His wrinkles are also very deep, especially in his cheeks, just above his thick beard. (Source: Vinland Saga Wiki)', '/uploads/images/c_82533.png'),
(128, 'Floki', 'フローキ', '配角', 'Atsushi Ono', 'A Jomsviking commander whom contracted [Askeladd](https://anilist.co/character/13020) to assassinate [Thors](https://anilist.co/character/13021), Floki''s former comrade.', '/uploads/images/c_82537.jpg'),
(128, 'Halfdan', 'ハーフダン', '配角', 'Yoshimitsu Shimoyama', 'Halfdan is a wealthy and powerful landowner and moneylender known for his ruthlessness, earning the nickname "Iron Chain" for his skilled use of one as a weapon and symbol of his philosophy of chaining others.', '/uploads/images/c_140356.png'),
(128, 'Ari', 'アーレ', '配角', 'Mitsuhiro Ichiki', '__Height:__ 170 cm Ari is from [Thorfinn](https://anilist.co/character/10138/Thorfinn-Karlsefni)’s village in Iceland.~!He is the husband of [Ylva](https://anilist.co/character/27876) and the father of their four children.!~', '/uploads/images/c_140357.png'),
(128, 'Helga', 'ヘルガ', '配角', 'Ao Takahashi', 'She is the mother of [Thorfinn](https://anilist.co/character/10138) and [Ylva](https://anilist.co/character/27876), and the wife of [Thors](https://anilist.co/character/13021). ~!She''s the daughter of the Jomsviking Chief.!~', '/uploads/images/c_141589.jpg'),
(128, 'Asgeir', 'アスゲード', '配角', 'Ryouta Takeuchi', '__Height:__ 170cm [Thorkell](https://anilist.co/character/17440)''s first mate. Asgeir is one of the few characters Thorkell outwardly respects, meeting him at eye-level in conversation, listening to his advice, and putting him in charge of strategies and planning. Asgeir is often shown yelling at Thorkell and becoming easily worried and even panicked when Thorkell is in danger.', '/uploads/images/c_141590.png'),
(128, 'Torgrim', 'トルグリム', '配角', 'Hiroki Gotou', 'He is [Atli](https://anilist.co/character/141592)''s older brother.', '/uploads/images/c_141591.png'),
(128, 'Atli', 'アトリ', '配角', 'Shinya Takahashi', 'He is [Torgrim](https://anilist.co/character/141591)''s younger brother.', '/uploads/images/c_141592.png'),
(128, 'Mimi', '耳', '配角', 'Makoto Furukawa', 'A member of [Askeladd](https://anilist.co/character/13020)''s band whose remarkable hearing allows him estimate distance and marching speed of enemy troops just by pressing his ear to the ground. He needs complete silence to work, and snow dampens sound enough to severely limit this ability.', '/uploads/images/c_141593.png'),
(128, 'Hordaland ', 'ホルザランド', '配角', 'Reina Kondou', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_147777.jpg'),
(128, 'Anne', 'アン', '配角', 'Yumi Hara', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_149584.png'),
(128, 'Lydia', 'リディア', '配角', 'Sayaka Oohara', 'a Welsh noblewoman who was captured and enslaved by the Norse warrior Olaf', '/uploads/images/c_156501.jpg'),
(128, 'Olaf', 'オラフ', '配角', 'Jirou Saitou', 'Norse warrior and the father of Askeladd.', '/uploads/images/c_156502.png'),
(128, 'Asser', 'アッサー', '配角', 'Tsuguo Mogami', 'is a Welsh envoy', '/uploads/images/c_156503.jpg'),
(128, 'Gorm', 'ゴルム', '配角', 'Tadashi Miyazawa', 'is a feudal lord in a village located on the Jutland Peninsula, Denmark. He really loves gold and it brightens his heart, just by looking at it.', '/uploads/images/c_156504.jpg'),
(128, 'Faxi', 'ファクシ', '配角', 'Hana Satou', 'is a young boy from Thorfinn''s village.', '/uploads/images/c_156505.jpg'),
(128, 'Mols', 'モルズ', '配角', '', '[Leif](https://anilist.co/character/19486)''s traveling partner.', '/uploads/images/c_156507.jpg'),
(128, 'Áki', 'アーク', '配角', 'Mitsuhiro Ichiki', 'A member of Askeladd''s band.', '/uploads/images/c_156508.jpg'),
(128, 'Jabbathe', 'ジャバザ', '配角', 'Kappei Yamaguchi', 'is a frank nobleman, who with the help of Askeladd was able to overtake a strong frank fortress.', '/uploads/images/c_156509.jpg'),
(128, 'Magni', 'マグニ', '配角', 'Tsuguo Mogami', 'is a young man from Thorfinn''s village.', '/uploads/images/c_156510.jpg'),
(128, 'Grim', 'グリム', '配角', 'Taito Ban', 'A young man from Thorfinn''s village.', '/uploads/images/c_156511.png'),
(128, 'Haldor', 'ハッルドール', '配角', 'Hiroki Matsukawa', 'Haldor is a warrior living in England.', '/uploads/images/c_156513.jpg'),
(128, 'Tore', 'トーレ', '配角', 'Tsuguo Mogami', 'is a member of Askeladd''s band.', '/uploads/images/c_156514.jpg'),
(128, 'Gratianus', 'グラティアヌス', '配角', 'Jirou Saitou', 'Gratianus is a Welsh warrior serving as a captain of Morgannwg''s military.', '/uploads/images/c_156515.jpg'),
(128, 'Gunnar', 'グンナル', '配角', 'Tsuguo Mogami', 'He is Ragnar''s Brother. ~!now he is a politician who currently serves as an adviser to King Canute.!~', '/uploads/images/c_156517.png'),
(128, 'Mord', 'モード', '配角', 'Masato Niwa', 'Mord is a young man from Thorfinn''s village.', '/uploads/images/c_232482.png'),
(128, 'Hakon', 'ハーコン', '配角', 'Yoshiaki Hasegawa', 'A young man from Thorfinn''s village.', '/uploads/images/c_232483.png'),
(129, 'Norman', 'ノーマン', '主角', 'Maaya Uchida', '__Height:__ 145 cm __Farm Identifier:__ 22194 Norman seems to be logical, well-meaning, and devoted, with a slightly naive side. He can easily plan his actions in advance and he anticipates on other''s actions. He is one of the top 3 ranking orphans, along with [Emma](https://anilist.co/character/121725/Emma) and [Ray](https://anilist.co/character/121724/Ray). Norman loves Emma and he is helpful and loyal towards her.', '/uploads/images/c_121700.jpg'),
(129, 'Isabella', 'イザベラ', '配角', 'Yuuko Kaida', '__Height:__ 170 cm __Farm Identifier:__ 73584 Isabella worked as a Mama at Grace Field House, taking care of the orphans that reside within.', '/uploads/images/c_121701.png'),
(129, 'Krone', 'クローネ', '配角', 'Nao Fujita', 'Sister Krone runs the Grace Field House orphanage with [Madam Isabella](https://anilist.co/character/121701/Isabella). She has the desire to usurp the position of "Mama" from Isabella.', '/uploads/images/c_121702.jpg'),
(129, 'Ray', 'レイ', '主角', 'Mariya Ise', '__Height:__ 150 cm __Farm Identifier:__ 81194 As one of the three perfect students at the orphanage, Ray is very logical, smart, cunning, extremely patient and is usually shown to read books by himself. Although he is extremely book smart he says that he never liked to study. According to data obtained by sister [Krone](https://anilist.co/character/121702/Krone), his weakness is that he gives up easily.', '/uploads/images/c_121724.jpg'),
(129, 'Emma', 'エマ', '主角', 'Sumire Morohoshi', '__Height:__ 145 cm __Farm Identifier:__ 63194 Emma acts as an older sister to the other children and loves her family very intensely. She is sweet, heroic, caring, and has a big heart. She can also be naive and reckless, and doesn''t hesitate to put herself at risk to ensure the safety of the group. The other kids describe her as having monster reflexes and an astounding ability to learn, which enables her to think fast in difficult situations and makes her a very good strategist. She could be considered a beacon of hope for the rest of the children.', '/uploads/images/c_121725.png'),
(129, 'Don', 'ドン', '配角', 'Shinei Ueki', '__Age (2045):__ 10 yo __Farm Identifier:__ 16194 __D.O.B:__ 2035/7/4 __Height (2045-2049):__ 155 - 174 cm Don has dark skin and a tall and slender appearance. He has short, messy black hair with an undercut and brown eyes. He wears the standard white uniform. Like [Emma](https://anilist.co/character/121725/Emma), Don cares deeply about his siblings. Don is portrayed as a cheerful and slightly careless boy, however, he too is fairly intelligent, coming around 5th place in the everyday test, after [Gilda](https://anilist.co/character/126455/Gilda). He also has talents in pick pocketing. His physical ability is also fairly strong.', '/uploads/images/c_126454.jpg'),
(129, 'Gilda', 'ギルダ', '配角', 'Lynn', '__Farm Identifier:__ 65194 __Height (2045-2049):__ 138 - 155 cm Gilda has short olive drab hair kept in a Chinese bob hairstyle and wears circular-lensed glasses. Gilda is an intuitive young girl. She also has a caring personality. She seems to be an introvert, however she also has her moments of bravery. She can also be quite threatening.', '/uploads/images/c_126455.png'),
(129, 'Phil', 'フィル', '配角', 'Hiyori Kouno', '__Height:__ 100 cm __Farm Identifier:__ 34394 (Grace Field House) __D.O.B:__ 2041 Phil is very active and can always be seen running around. ~!He is also shown to be very mature and intelligent for his age, even suspecting something was wrong when [Emma](https://anilist.co/character/121725/Emma) and the other older orphans were trying to find out ways to escape.!~', '/uploads/images/c_126475.jpg'),
(129, 'Anna', 'アンナ', '配角', 'Ai Kayano', '__Age (2045):__ 9 yo __Farm Identifier:__ 48194 (Grace Field House) __D.O.B:__ 2036/4/25 __Height (2045-2049):__ 135 - 162 cm Just like every other orphans of Grace Field, she wears the standard Grace Field Orphanage uniform. Anna grows to be a surprisingly big boned, tall girl. She has blonde hair tied into twin braids. ~!Later, she cuts her hair in order to help with the escape.!~~!During her time at the B06-32 shelter, she spends a lot of time studying medicine in order to help her family.!~', '/uploads/images/c_126504.png'),
(129, 'Lannion', 'ラニオン', '配角', 'Yuuko Mori', '__Age (2045):__ 7 yo __Farm Identifier:__ 54294 (Grace Field House) __D.O.B:__ 2038/4/28 __Height (2045-2049):__ 125 - 144 cm Lani is a mischievous and resourceful boy, who enjoys pulling pranks with his best friend, [Thoma](https://anilist.co/character/129784/Thoma). He is a bit cowardly, but also blunt and straightforward.', '/uploads/images/c_129783.jpg'),
(129, 'Thoma', 'トーマ', '配角', 'Mari Hino', '__Height:__ 123 cm __Farm Identifier:__ 55294 (Grace Field House) Thoma is a resourceful and mischievous boy, who enjoys pulling pranks alongside his best friend [Lani](https://anilist.co/character/129783). He is blunt, but can also be quite cowardly.', '/uploads/images/c_129784.jpg'),
(129, 'Conny', 'コニー', '配角', 'Ari Ozawa', '__Height:__ 115cm __Farm Identifier:__ 48294 Conny is nice and lovely towards Emma, Don and the other orphans. She always carried her stuffed rabbit Little Bernie around with her. Her intellect level seemed to be average for her age.', '/uploads/images/c_129785.jpg'),
(129, 'Nat', 'ナット', '配角', 'Shizuka Ishigami', '__Age (2045):__ 9 yo __Farm Identifier:__ 48194 (Grace Field House) __D.O.B:__ 2036/12/18 __Height (2045-2049):__ 133 - 156 cm Nat is a rather frail boy, with brown eyes and a tall nose line (which he takes great pride in). He wears the standard orphanage uniform. Even though he can be easily intimidated, he does have his moments of bravery.', '/uploads/images/c_129805.png'),
(129, 'Sobo', '祖母', '配角', 'Mami Koyama', 'Grandmother is a high-ranking human and once worked as [Isabella''s](https://anilist.co/character/121701/Isabella) Mama although she treated her more as a pawn than a human. ~!On January 27, 2046, it was revealed that all of Isabella''s mistakes and responsibilities, as in letting the children escape, were placed on Grandma Sarah. Although Isabella wasn''t able to manage her products, Sarah wasn''t able to manage Isabella. As a result, Sarah was shipped out to be served at the upcoming Tifari in order to make up for the escapees. Isabella took the role of Grandmother after that.!~', '/uploads/images/c_136463.jpg'),
(129, 'Leslie', 'レスリー', '配角', 'Sanae Kobayashi', '__Farm Identifier:__ 71584 Leslie was Isabella''s childhood friend and is shown to be very kind and loves music.', '/uploads/images/c_198999.jpg'),
(129, 'Jemima', 'ジェミマ', '配角', 'Kuon Erisa', '__Age (2045):__ 5 yo __Farm Identifier:__ 31394 (Grace Field House) __Height (2045-2049):__ 107 - 134 cm Jemima is cheerful and well-behaved. Though, she can display acts of mischievousness. She is seen to have a strong bond with [Alicia](https://anilist.co/character/199115).', '/uploads/images/c_199114.png'),
(130, 'Narrator', 'ナレーター', '配角', 'Yutaka Aoyama', 'This character page is set to represent and list all narrators, which haven''t been given a visual representation of themselves in their respective work. Please add other narrator characters, which were given a visual representation of themselves, separately from this narrator page.', '/uploads/images/c_36309.jpg'),
(130, 'Kaguya Shinomiya', '四宮かぐや', '主角', 'Aoi Koga', '__Height:__ 158 cm The vice president of the student council of Shuchiin Academy, member of the wealthy Shinomiya family, she is a multi-talented genius who can do anything if she sets her mind to it. Due to the way she was raised, she instinctively looks down on others and thinks of ways to use them for her own benefit. Kaguya rarely interacted with other people before she joined the student council, but that has begun to change. She is an incredibly sheltered girl, resulting in her lacking in several pieces of what might be considered common sense. She still doesn’t understand love very well, and her main objective is to make [Miyuki Shirogane](https://anilist.co/character/121101) fall in love and confess to her. Later in the series: ~!She confesses her love to Miyuki Shirogane and they start dating.!~ ~!In a Oshi no Ko special chapter, it was revealed that she married Miyuki and changed her surname to Kaguya Shirogane!~', '/uploads/images/c_120649.png'),
(130, 'Miyuki Shirogane', '白銀御行', '主角', 'Makoto Furukawa', '__Height:__ 175 cm He is a second year student at Shuchi''in Academy and the president of the student council. Miyuki is a handsome young man with blond hair and blue eyes. Due to his constant sleep deprivation and nearsightedness, his eyes appear to glare. He usually wears the regular Shuchi''in Academy black male uniform adorned with the Aiguilette, the golden chain-like accessory around his neck. The Aiguilette symbolizes his authority as student council president. Shirogane is a diligent student who, despite his underprivileged background, climbed his way to the top of his class through hard work and determination. Shirogane holds himself in high regard, consistently working to maintain his perfect image. He is textbook workaholic, enjoying his part-time job and often putting his own health at risk for the sake of his work. Due to his poor background, Shirogane values money greatly and goes to great lengths to not be wasteful, and generally dislikes expensive gifts. ~!Miyuki''s mother left his family when he was a child. Miyuki''s father''s factory was shut down and currently has no stable employment. They live in an apartment that costs ￥50,000 (Approx $450) a month. Due to this grisly past, he has been led to a lifestyle of part time jobs and hard work. He passed the Level 2 Kanji Kentei exam and has passed Grade Pre 1 on Eiken. He has also got second place on the National mock exam.!~ ~!Miyuki transferred into Shuchi''in Academy during his first year of high school on a scho', '/uploads/images/c_121101.png'),
(130, 'Yuu Ishigami', '石上優', '主角', 'Ryouta Suzuki', 'The treasurer of the student council of the Shuchiin Academy. He''s extremely valued by [Miyuki](https://anilist.co/character/121101), given that he single-handedly manages all the school''s funds. He''s also terrified of [Kaguya](https://anilist.co/character/120649), though no one else is sure why that is. Yuu keeps to himself and rarely speaks up, often getting into trouble when he does. He has a depressed outlook on life while having an inferiority complex. In contrast to his attitude, he is willing to help those in need and will sacrifice his pride if need be. Unlike his high school self, he had a much different outlook and demeanor during middle school. Later in the series: ~!Ishigami develops a crush on Tsubame that he inadvertently confesses his feelings for her at the school''s cultural festival. Ishigami does not realize that his actions were perceived as a confession by the rest of the student body and is therefore oblivious to the implications of having given Tsubame a heart-shaped gift (considered akin to a confession in Shuchiin tradition). After some convincing by Kaguya, Tsubame decides to seriously consider Ishigami''s confession, with her original intention being to let him down as gently as possible. It isn''t until Ishigami watches Tsubame''s performance of the traditional play that gave rise to the aforementioned tradition that he realizes his actions had unintended meaning. Even then, Ishigami''s thickheaded nature prevented him from recognizing the full meaning ', '/uploads/images/c_121102.png'),
(130, 'Chika Fujiwara', '藤原千花', '主角', 'Konomi Kohara', 'The secretary of the Shuchiin Academy student council. She could not be predicted, her thoughts could not be read. A natural disaster who unconsciously threw everything into chaos simply by being present, also known as __Subject F__. ~!In chapter 222 of the manga, Chika reveals that she played piano because she wanted to be perfect, and she becomes a prodigy at the piano. The expectations of her family and her fans rose, forcing her to practice more. She quit piano after Kaguya told her to just quit if she didn''t like the piano. Soon after Chika challenged Kaguya to a game battle and if she won, she would get to become Kaguya''s friend. In the end, she becomes Kaguya''s first friend.!~', '/uploads/images/c_121103.png'),
(130, 'Ai Hayasaka', '早坂愛', '配角', 'Yumiri Hanamori', 'Ai Hayasaka is a second-year student at Shuchiin Academy and a valet of the Shinomiya family. She is a member of the Hayasaka family, who have served the Shinomiya family for generations, gaining their trust. Having been personally assigned to enter Shuchiin Academy with her, Ai supports [Kaguya Shinomiya](https://anilist.co/character/120649) in her high school life and has been a part of Kaguya''s life for ten years. Because of their close relationship, Ai is one of the few people around to which Kaguya''s amiability is not an act. Even if she demonstrates maturity as a valet, Ai still has the concerns of a young girl, such as caring to be in fashion and going out with friends, even if she does not have much time for herself due to work. Ai helps Kaguya with the struggles about her feelings for [Shirogane](https://anilist.co/character/121101). ~!She later leaves her job as a maid to Kaguya but still continues her friendship.!~ ~!In the Doujin-ban universe, she starts dating and later gets engaged to Shirogane!~', '/uploads/images/c_121104.png'),
(130, 'Miko Iino', '伊井野ミコ', '配角', '', '__Height:__ 147 cm (4''7") She is a freshman at Shuchiin Private Academy and the Auditor of the Student Council. Miko has a strong sense of justice and will correct others on what''s right and wrong. Unfortunately, this led to her being bullied, though she still continues to uphold her idea of "right". She idolizes [Chika Fujiwara](https://anilist.co/character/121103), listening to anything she says, even if it''s for Chika''s enjoyment.', '/uploads/images/c_125886.png'),
(130, 'Kei Shirogane', '白銀圭', '配角', 'Sayumi Suzushiro', 'Kei Shirogane is [Miyuki Shirogane''s](https://anilist.co/character/121101) little sister. She attends Shuchiin middle school and is the treasurer for the middle school student council. She is a hard worker just like her brother and can be very prideful at times. She also inherited his sense of righteousness and hates it when someone doesn''t do the right thing in a given situation. Like her brother, she likes helping out those who are in trouble even if it means going out of her way to do it. Since she grew up in a family that places emphasis on saving money, she normally carries coupons and works hard for the things she wants to buy. She developed a prickly attitude towards her brother due to his over protectiveness. She''s also entered a rebellious phase and due to her pride and she cannot get herself to have a lighthearted conversation with Miyuki, leading into the similar mind games that Miyuki and [Kaguya](https://anilist.co/character/120649) play against each other, but her objective is to talk to Miyuki without making it look like she has a brother complex. She rarely speaks and most of the time it is only when she exchanges formalities at school or when she hurls abuses at her brother.', '/uploads/images/c_126144.png'),
(130, 'Erika Kose', '巨瀬工リカ', '配角', 'Ayaka Asai', 'She is a member of the mass media club at Shuchi''in Academy.', '/uploads/images/c_126986.png'),
(130, 'Karen Kino', '紀かれん', '配角', 'Madoka Asahina', 'She is a member of the mass media club at Shuchi''in Academy.', '/uploads/images/c_126987.png'),
(130, 'Tsubasa Tanuma ', '田沼翼', '配角', 'Taku Yashiro', 'He is a student in Shuchi''in highschool and always asks [Miyuki Shirogane](https://anilist.co/character/121101) for advice about love. [Kashiwagi](https://anilist.co/character/134330)''s boyfriend.', '/uploads/images/c_134327.png'),
(130, 'Maki Shijo', '四条眞妃', '配角', 'Kana Ichinose', 'Maki is a classmate and friend of [Nagisa](https://anilist.co/character/134330). She has short hair styled in short pigtails. She is friends with Nagisa and is secretly jealous of Nagisa''s relationship with her boyfriend, as she too liked Kashiwagi''s Boyfriend, but could not confess before. As a branch member of the Shinomiya clan, she is [Kaguya](https://anilist.co/character/120649)''s second cousin twice removed so she sometimes refers to Kaguya as "Auntie". [Miyuki](https://anilist.co/character/121101) and [Yuu](https://anilist.co/character/121102/Yuu-Ishigami) observe she acts very tsundere (cold on the outside but wanting to be affectionate), and similar to Kaguya in personality. She declares Yuu and Miyuki as her friends, due to their support in helping her process her failed romance, much to Kaguya''s horror', '/uploads/images/c_134328.png'),
(130, 'Moeha Fujiwara', '藤原萌葉', '配角', 'Ari Ozawa', 'Moeha is [Chika](https://anilist.co/character/121103)''s little sister who is in junior high. She is the student council vice-president at the junior high. She admires [Miyuki](https://anilist.co/character/121101) as well and hopes to confess someday. She has a habit of voicing dark ideas, which unnerve [Kaguya](https://anilist.co/character/120649) a great deal.', '/uploads/images/c_134329.png'),
(130, 'Nagisa Kashiwagi', '柏木渚', '配角', 'Momo Asakura', 'Nagisa is a classmate who occasionally asks [Kaguya](https://anilist.co/character/120649) about what to do in her relationships. [Tsubasa](https://anilist.co/character/134327)''s girlfriend.', '/uploads/images/c_134330.png'),
(130, 'Kobachi Osaragi', '大仏こばち', '配角', '', 'Kobachi is [Miko](https://anilist.co/character/125886)''s classmate with the glasses and a member of the disciplinary committee. She has been looking after Miko for over 10 years. ~!Though she doesn''t love him in a romantic way, she has liked Yu Ishigami since middle school. She believes that Tsubame Koyasu is a kind person and is therefore supportive of Ishigami''s feelings for Tsubame, despite her friend Miko being in love with Ishigami as well.!~', '/uploads/images/c_134331.png'),
(130, 'Betsy Beltoise', 'べルトクーズ・べツィー', '配角', 'Sally Amaki', 'The vice president of Shuchi''in Academy''s sister school in France.', '/uploads/images/c_134861.png'),
(130, 'Adolphe Pescarolo', 'アドルフ・ペスカローロ', '配角', 'Itaru Yamamoto', 'The Principal of Shuchi''in Academy He''s strict regarding school regulations, but knows how to garner the favor of students nonetheless. He helped Yu Ishigami get enrolled to Shuchi''in despite not finishing his task of making an apology letter. Despite being an authority figure within the school, he has shown comical disregard for school rules and discipline when it comes to his own actions, having been openly caught playing Pokemon Go on more than one occasion on school grounds while chastising nearby students for doing the same.', '/uploads/images/c_134892.jpg'),
(130, 'Shirogane no Chichi', '白銀の父', '配角', 'Takehito Koyasu', 'Father of [Miyuki](https://anilist.co/character/121101) and [Kei Shirogane](https://anilist.co/character/126144). ~!His wife left him and their factory shut down leaving him to not have any stable employment.!~ ~!He later becomes a youtuber.!~', '/uploads/images/c_134893.jpg'),
(130, 'Saburo Odajima', '小田島三郎', '配角', 'Haruo Satou', 'One of the Four Ramen Emperors of Tokyo. In the past, Saburo was in a relationship with [The Glutton Girl of Jinbocho](https://anilist.co/character/276380/Jinbouchou-no-Glutton-Girl), but he broke up with her over their polar opposite ramen styles, believing they''ll eventually end up at each other''s throats.', '/uploads/images/c_137169.png'),
(130, 'Toyomi Fujiwara', '藤原豊実', '配角', 'Mikako Komatsu', 'Toyomi Fujiwara is Chika Fujiwara and Moeha Fujiwara''s eldest sister. Toyomi is a girl that likes to wear revealing outfits, her hair is similar to Chika''s except that she tied hers with a flower shaped clip to go down on her left shoulder. She usually wears an aloof expression on her face. Toyomi is the laid back older sister type, who is very seductive and does whatever she likes, even against her own parents wishes.', '/uploads/images/c_158014.png'),
(130, 'Ienaga', '家永', '配角', 'Tomomi Mineuchi', 'An elementary school student', '/uploads/images/c_275596.jpg'),
(130, 'J Suzuki', '鈴木J', '配角', 'Takeshi Maruyama', 'A taxi driver and one of the Four Ramen Emperors of Tokyo.', '/uploads/images/c_275597.jpg'),
(130, 'Miki', 'みき', '配角', 'Hina Kino', 'An elementary school student', '/uploads/images/c_275598.jpg'),
(130, 'Pes', 'ペス', '配角', 'Yuuki Ishikari', 'Pes is the beloved pet dog of [Chika Fujiwara](https://anilist.co/character/121103/Chika-Fujiwara). He is quite a large dog, with golden fur and floppy ears. He has piercing eyes like [the president](https://anilist.co/character/121101/Miyuki-Shirogane)', '/uploads/images/c_275599.jpg'),
(130, 'Maki', 'マキ', '配角', 'Hikaru Akao', 'Hoped to hangout with Takkun, but he prioritized soccer instead. She does wanna cheer for him.', '/uploads/images/c_275600.jpg'),
(130, 'Tenchou', '店長', '配角', 'Kouichi Souma', 'A ramen chef', '/uploads/images/c_275601.jpg'),
(130, 'Shitsuji', '執事', '配角', 'Kayuki Matsumoto', 'One of the butler''s assigned to [Kaguya](https://anilist.co/character/120649/Kaguya-Shinomiya)', '/uploads/images/c_275602.jpg'),
(130, 'Subaru Suruga', '駿河すばる', '配角', 'Yuuka Morishima', 'One of [Ai Hayasaka](https://anilist.co/character/121104/)''s closest friends. She wears her Shuchi''in Academy school uniform modified to match up with kogal fashion. She is the daughter of the president of an IT company.', '/uploads/images/c_276146.jpg'),
(130, 'Mirin Hinokuchi', '火口三鈴', '配角', 'Yuka Nukui', 'One of [Ai Hayasaka](https://anilist.co/character/121104/)''s closest friends. She wears her Shuchi''in Academy school uniform modified to match up with kogal fashion. She is the daughter of an advertising executive.', '/uploads/images/c_276147.jpg'),
(131, 'Tanjirou Kamado', '竈門炭治郎', '主角', 'Natsuki Hanae', '__Height:__ 165 cm (5''5") __Combat Style:__ Water Breathing & ~!Sun Breathing!~ Tanjirou is kind by nature and has been described by others as having very gentle eyes. He has a great deal of determination and will not give up once he has a goal to achieve, an example being finding a cure for [Nezuko](https://anilist.co/character/127518). Even though he is relatively strong on his own, he isn''t opposed to asking others for help when he needs it. He is very protective of his friends and even more so of his younger sister. His biggest attribute is his ability to empathize with anyone, even demons. ~!Eventually, he discovers that he is a legendary Sun Breathing user.!~', '/uploads/images/c_126071.png'),
(131, 'Nezuko Kamado', '竈門禰豆子', '主角', 'Akari Kitou', '__Height:__ 153 cm (5''0") Transformed into a demon and left mute, Nezuko travels with her older brother [Tanjirou](https://anilist.co/character/126071/Kamado-Tanjirou) in a box on his back. She can change her size at will, and is a capable fighter when she needs to be, but has never killed or eaten any humans. Instead of gaining nourishment from humans, it seems that she recovers her energy by sleeping for long periods of time.', '/uploads/images/c_127518.png'),
(131, 'Inosuke Hashibira', '嘴平伊之助', '主角', 'Yoshitsugu Matsuoka', '**Height:** 164 cm (5''4") __Combat Style:__ Beast Breathing Inosuke is usually seen wearing a grey boar mask, with a shirtless version of the Demon hunter uniform. Without the mask he has messy shoulder length black hair and large green eyes with long eyelashes. He is described as having a girly looking face which greatly contrasts with his muscular body. Inosuke is extremely short-tempered and proud, and makes a big deal out of fighting opponents stronger than him claiming that''s his only hobby. He is a sore loser and is always trying to compete with Tanjiro and provoke him into fighting him, and usually failing. Due to growing up in the mountains by himself Inosuke has trouble interacting with others and only cares about himself most of the time. Though he''s often seen with 2 swords in hand, Inosuke is left-handed.', '/uploads/images/c_129130.jpg'),
(131, 'Zenitsu Agatsuma', '我妻善逸', '主角', 'Hiro Shimono', '__Height:__ 164 cm (5''4") __Combat Style:__ Thunder Breathing __Affiliation:__ Demon Slayer Corps __Occupation:__ Demon Slayer Zenitsu Agatsuma is one of the main protagonists of Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba and along with [Inosuke Hashibira](https://anilist.co/character/129130/Inosuke-Hashibira), a traveling companion of [Tanjiro Kamado](https://anilist.co/character/126071/Tanjirou-Kamado) and [Nezuko Kamado](https://anilist.co/character/127518/Nezuko-Kamado).', '/uploads/images/c_129131.png'),
(131, 'Muzan Kibutsuji', '鬼舞辻無惨', '配角', 'Toshihiko Seki', '__Height:__ 179 cm (5''10") He is the Demon King, the first of his kind, and the progenitor of all other demons in existence. Muzan is also the leader of the Twelve Kizuki, an organization of the twelve strongest demons in existence that serve directly under him. ~!A millennium ago, during the Heian Era, Muzan was turned into a demon during an experimental treatment trying to cure his terminal illness, and his goal since then was to live without the fear of death and become truly eternal. He believes that Sun Breathing users are his only threat. He has a grand total of seven hearts and five brains.!~', '/uploads/images/c_129132.jpg'),
(131, 'Kyoujurou Rengoku', '煉獄杏寿郎', '配角', 'Satoshi Hino', '__Height:__ 177 cm (5''10") __Combat Style:__ Flame Breathing He is greatly enthusiastic in regard to his duties as Flame Pillar and often cheerfully eccentric. He is amiable, kind and boasts extraordinary flame techniques and swordsmanship stemming from strict practice and discipline. He is an honourable warrior who adheres to his code of morals and principles that was instilled into him by his mother at a young age - the most significant being that those who were born strong have a duty to protect the weak.', '/uploads/images/c_129133.png'),
(131, 'Giyuu Tomioka', '冨岡義勇', '配角', 'Takahiro Sakurai', '__Height:__ 176 cm (5''9½") __Combat Style:__ Water Breathing Water pillar in the Demon Killing Corps. Giyuu is reserved and displays little emotion, instead giving off a calm feeling most of the time. As a water breath user, Giyuu has created his own style. The eleventh style, Lull, gives him the ability to nullify any oncoming attacks, though rapid attacks can pierce through it. Though Giyuu is reserved, he does have a few friends, such as Tanjirou and, in the past, [Sabito](https://anilist.co/character/137809/Sabito). Shinobu often pokes fun at Giyuu and is merciless when doing so, such as saying he has no friends and that others don''t like him. ~!He is one of the only Pillar, aside from [Sanemi](https://anilist.co/character/137774/Sanemi-Shinazugawa), who survived during the final fight against [Muzan](https://anilist.co/character/129132/Muzan-Kibutsuji).!~', '/uploads/images/c_130050.png'),
(131, 'Muichirou Tokitou', '時透無一郎', '配角', 'Kengo Kawanishi', '__Height:__ 160 cm (5''3") __Combat Style:__ Mist Breathing Muichiro is an air-headed individual who seems to constantly wander off in thought and never focus on one thing. Impassive and, at times, obtuse, he tends to think only for himself and operates on logic alone, never letting emotion guide him. Despite this, he has been shown to get serious when it is required and is devoted to his position as the Demon Slayer Corps'' Mist Hashira. Alternatively, he seems to display a cold and arrogant side as well. ~!He later died at Kokushibo''s hand.!~', '/uploads/images/c_136069.png'),
(131, 'Shinobu Kochou', '胡蝶しのぶ', '配角', 'Saori Hayami', '__Height:__ 151 cm (4''11") __Combat Style:__ Insect Breathing Shinobu is a demon slayer and the Insect Pillar of the Demon Killing Corps. She is 18 years old and one of two female pillars. Shinobu appears rather laid back, and always has a smile on her face regardless of the situation. Despite her relaxed exterior and her initial claim of wanting to get along with demons, she can be rather cruel and harbors a great deal of anger towards them. She is generally kind to other humans, but is rather sadistic in her treatment of demons. As a pillar, she is a top-class fighter despite her small stature. She is also well-versed in medical knowledge, and can concoct poisons and medicines alike. ~!During the Infinity Castle Arc, she encounters the Upper 2 demon [Douma](https://anilist.co/character/144591) and is slain by him in a fight. However, since she poisoned herself before the fight, Douma is severely incapacitated after eating her.!~', '/uploads/images/c_136070.png'),
(131, 'Tengen Uzui', '宇髄天元', '配角', 'Katsuyuki Konishi', '__Height:__ 198 cm (6''6") __Combat Style:__ Sound Breathing A Demon Slayer, and the Sound Pillar of the Demon Slayer Corps. Tengen is a very eccentric person, always wanting to complete actions as flashy as possible. Although he has displayed an uncaring and forceful attitude towards some people, he also has a caring side that is mainly only shown towards his most treasured ones, most notably his three wives, [Makio](https://anilist.co/character/250554), [Suma](https://anilist.co/character/250555), and [Hinatsuru](https://anilist.co/character/250556). He also shows a somewhat nicer side towards [Tanjiro](https://anilist.co/character/126071) after their mission and starts to accept him more as the series goes on.', '/uploads/images/c_136071.png'),
(131, 'Mitsuri Kanroji', '甘露寺蜜璃', '配角', 'Kana Hanazawa', '__Height:__ 167 cm (5''5") __Combat Style:__ Love Breathing Demon Hunter and the Love Pillar of the Demon Killing Corps. Mitsuri is a soft and kind person. She is very emotional and passionate, constantly complimenting people in her head, which probably contributes to her nickname of "the Hashira of Love". Although she is rather shy and is easily flustered, she is always kind to others, most notably towards [Obanai](https://anilist.co/character/137777), whom she appears to share a strong bond with. Besides her rather emotional personality, she can also come off as somewhat childish at times. ~!She was taught by Rengoku to use the flame breathing. However, although Mitsuri has learnt it, she was not as skillful with it and cannot fight to her fullest using it, leading her to solely develop the Love Breathing.!~', '/uploads/images/c_136072.png'),
(131, 'Sakonji Urokodaki', '鱗滝左近次 ', '配角', 'Houchuu Ootsuka', 'Retired member of the Demon Slayer Corps, previously holding the title of Water Hashira. He is the main cultivator of the Water Breathing style, having trained Makomo, Sabito, Giyu Tomioka, and Tanjiro Kamado.', '/uploads/images/c_137773.png'),
(131, 'Sanemi Shinazugawa', '不死川実弥', '配角', 'Tomokazu Seki', '__Height:__ 179cm (5''10½") Demon Hunter and the Wind Pillar of the Demon Killing Corps. He is the older brother of [Genya Shinazugawa](https://anilist.co/character/137776). Sanemi specializes in Wind Breathing, which has 9 forms. The technique consists of drawing the air from around the user to create whirlwind attacks that follow the user''s movements. Form names include Dust Whirlwind Cutter, Claws-Purifying Wind, Clean Storm Wind Tree, Rising Dust Storm, Cold Mountain Wind, Black Wind Mountain Mist, Gale - Sudden Gusts, Primary Gale Slash, and Idaten Typhoon.', '/uploads/images/c_137774.png'),
(131, 'Jigorou Kuwajima', '桑島慈悟郎', '配角', 'Shigeru Chiba', 'Retired member of the Demon Slayer Corps, having previously held the title of Thunder Hashira. He trained Zenitsu Agatsuma and Kaigaku.', '/uploads/images/c_137775.png'),
(131, 'Genya Shinazugawa', '不死川玄弥', '配角', 'Nobuhiko Okamoto', '__Height:__ 180 cm (5''11") Genya Is a Demon Hunter of the Demon Killing Corps. He is also the younger brother of the Wind Pillar [Sanemi Shinazugawa](https://anilist.co/character/137774). ~! Due to his lack of breath forms he is dependent on using his shotgun and demon form. His shotgun pelts are made from sun steel to be effective against demons. His demon form is active when he digests anything from a demon to gain demon like strength and abilities. He is the only demon hunter to have this ability given that it is drastically rare !~', '/uploads/images/c_137776.jpg'),
(131, 'Obanai Iguro', '伊黒小芭内', '配角', 'Kenichi Suzumura', '__Height:__ 162 cm (5''3") Obanai is a Demon Slayer and the Snake Pillar of the Demon Slayer Corps. A young man of short stature and a pale complexion. He has straight-edged black hair of varying lengths, the longest reaching down to his shoulders and the shortest stopping at his cheekbones, which he wears down with two shorter strands hanging between his eyes. He wears a navy blue version of the standard Demon Slayer uniform, along with a black and white pinstriped haori, the hem and cuffs of which are striped lengthways rather than vertically, which covers his hands. Obanai also sports bandages in place of the leg-wraps around his calves, as well as another set of bandages that cover his mouth, and blue-strapped zori on his feet. He is also always seen with his white snake, Kaburamaru, wrapped around his shoulders.', '/uploads/images/c_137777.jpg'),
(131, 'Gyoumei Himejima', '悲鳴嶼行冥', '配角', 'Tomokazu Sugita', '__Height:__ 220cm (7''2½") He is a Demon Slayer and the Stone Hashira of the Demon Slayer Corps. Gyomei also serves as the mentor of Genya Shinazugawa.', '/uploads/images/c_137778.jpg'),
(131, 'Makomo', '真菰', '配角', 'Ai Kakuma', 'A cute and mysterious girl who wears a floral pattern kimono. Her fox mask has two flowers on its right cheek. ~!She is a former apprentice of Urokodaki Sakonji.!~', '/uploads/images/c_137806.png'),
(131, 'Kagaya Ubuyashiki', '産屋敷耀哉', '配角', 'Toshiyuki Morikawa', 'He is the head of the Ubuyashiki Family and 97th leader of the Demon Slayer Corps known mainly as "Oyakata-sama" ("Master") by his subordinates and peers.', '/uploads/images/c_137808.png'),
(131, 'Sabito', '錆兎', '配角', 'Yuuki Kaji', 'He is a former apprentice of [Urokodaki Sakonji](https://anilist.co/character/137773/Urokodaki-Sakonji). ~!He dies saving the participators in the final selection, including [Giyuu](https://anilist.co/character/130050/Tomioka-Giyuu).!~', '/uploads/images/c_137809.png'),
(131, 'Matsuemon Tennouji', '天王寺松右衛門', '配角', 'Takumi Yamazaki', 'Kasugai Crow assigned to Tanjirou Kamado. Very intelligent and seems to have a large ego.', '/uploads/images/c_137810.png'),
(131, 'Susamaru', '朱紗丸', '配角', 'Mikako Komatsu', '~!Susamaru was a Demon that aspired to join Kibutsuji Muzan''s Twelve Demon Moons group.!~', '/uploads/images/c_138810.png'),
(131, 'Yahaba', '矢琶羽', '配角', 'Jun Fukuyama', '~!was a Demon that aspired to join Kibutsuji Muzan''s Twelve Demon Moons group.!~', '/uploads/images/c_138811.png'),
(131, 'Numa Oni', '沼鬼', '配角', 'Ryouhei Kimura', '~!was a Demon that went on a rash of kidnappings during Kamado Tanjirou''s first mission for the Demon Killing Corps.!~', '/uploads/images/c_138812.jpg'),
(131, 'Yushirou', '愈史郎', '配角', 'Daiki Yamashita', '__Height:__ 157 cm (5''2") Yushiro is a traveling companion of Tamayo and close ally of Kamado Tanjirou. He was turned into a Demon by Tamayo. Yushiro was a human who was under the care of Tamayo as she was practicing as a medical practitioner. He was in the frail state fighting disease when Tamayo gave him the choice of succumbing to his illness or to live longer as a Demon. He agreed to become a Demon and has since stayed by Tamayo''s side serving as an assistant as well as her guard. ~!Yushiro would become the last known survivor of the Demon race. In time he would dedicate himself to a life of art and become a world famous painter in the present day under the name of Yushiro Yamamoto, known for his paintings of Tamayo to wide critical acclaim!~', '/uploads/images/c_138846.jpg'),
(131, 'Tamayo', '珠世', '配角', 'Maaya Sakamoto', '__Height:__ 150 cm (4''11") Tamayo is a doctor and close ally of [Kamado Tanjirou](https://anilist.co/character/126071/Kamado-Tanjirou). She was turned into a Demon by [Kibutsuji Muzan](https://anilist.co/character/129132/Kibutsuji-Muzan).', '/uploads/images/c_138847.jpg'),
(131, 'Teoni', '手鬼', '配角', 'Takehito Koyasu', 'The Hand Demon was a notorious Demon that killed thirteen of Urokodaki Sakonji''s apprentices, including Sabito and Makomo.', '/uploads/images/c_138988.png'),
(131, 'Odou no Oni', 'お堂の鬼', '配角', 'Hikaru Midorikawa', 'The Head Demon is the first Demon encountered by Kamado Tanjirou.', '/uploads/images/c_138989.png'),
(131, 'Hotaru Haganezuka', '鋼鐵塚蛍', '配角', 'Daisuke Namikawa', 'Hotaru Haganezuka is a swordsmith affiliated with the Demon Killing Corps.', '/uploads/images/c_138990.jpg'),
(131, 'Kanao Tsuyuri', '栗花落カナヲ', '配角', 'Reina Ueda', '__Height:__ 156 cm (5''1½") Kanao Tsuyuri is a Demon Hunter and the Tsuguko, who is personally looked after by the Demon Killing Corps'' Pillars. She uses Flower Breathing. ~!When Kanao is first introduced, she is an indecisive and quiet girl due to the abuse she endured in her past before meeting the Kocho sisters. She became unable to make decisions by herself and repressed her emotions as a defense mechanism. In order to help rectify this, Kanae gave her a coin to flip to decide which path to follow when she didn''t know what to do. Later on, Tanjiro helps Kanao overcome her indecisiveness and Kanao soon becomes more confident in making decisions with or without her coin. Kanao and Tanjiro would eventually marry and start a family, having two great-great-grandchildren by the names of [Kanata Kamado](https://anilist.co/character/171144/Kanata-Kamado) and [Sumihiko Kamado](https://anilist.co/character/171145/Sumihiko-Kamado) between them.!~', '/uploads/images/c_139038.png'),
(131, 'Kanae Kochou', '胡蝶カナエ', '配角', 'Ai Kayano', 'Kanae Kocho was a Demon Slayer and the late Flower Hashira. She was slain several years prior to the present story. She is also the biological older sister of [Shinobu Kochou](https://anilist.co/character/136070/Shinobu-Kochou) and the adoptive older sister of [Kanao Tsuyuri](https://anilist.co/character/139038/Tsuyuri-Kanao).', '/uploads/images/c_139039.png'),
(131, 'Kiriya Ubuyashiki', '産屋敷輝利哉', '配角', 'Aoi Yuuki', '~!Kiriya Ubuyashiki is the son and middle child of Kagaya Ubuyashiki. He is the current head of the Ubuyashiki Household and leader of the Demon Slaying Corps!~', '/uploads/images/c_139460.png'),
(131, 'Nakime', '鳴女', '配角', '', 'Nakime is a mysterious Biwa Demon that dwells in the Dimensional Infinity Fortress. ~!Actually she is a member of the Twelve Demon Moons, replacing Hantengu and holding the position of Upper Moon Four.!~ (Source: Fandom)', '/uploads/images/c_139736.png'),
(131, 'Enmu', '魘夢', '配角', 'Daisuke Hirakawa', '__Race:__ Demon __Height:__ 168 cm (5''6") Enmu is a sadistic and cruel demon Who is only driven by his liking to making humans suffer. He is shown to be completely loyal to [Muzan](https://anilist.co/character/129132/Kibutsuji-Muzan). Caring about him probably more than what he cares about himself. He also hates the other lower moons, labeling them as "Fools". ~!Enmu was a member of the Twelve Demon Moons, having held the position of Lower Moon One.!~ ~!Enmu was aboard the infinity train, and starts eating humans in order to make himself more powerful. He knocks them unconscious, promising them that he will gift them with nice and peaceful dreams but in reality, after giving them a nice dream, he always likes to follow it up with a horrifying nightmare because he thinks it is so much fun.!~ ~!In the end, Tanjiro''s Hinokami Kagura cuts through Enmu''s train spine and kills him.!~', '/uploads/images/c_139737.png'),
(131, 'Kyougai', '響凱', '配角', 'Junichi Suwabe', '~!Kyougai was a member of the Twelve Demon Moons, having held the position of Lower Moon Six. He is also known as Drum Demon.!~ (Source: Kimetsu no Yaiba Fandom, edited)', '/uploads/images/c_139738.png'),
(131, 'Rui', '累', '配角', 'Kouki Uchiyama', '~!Rui was a member of the Twelve Demon Moons, having held the position of Lower Moon Five.!~ (Source: Kimetsu no Yaiba Fandom)', '/uploads/images/c_139739.png'),
(131, 'Kumo Oni Ani', '蜘蛛鬼「兄」', '配角', 'Shoutarou Morikubo', '~!The Older Brother Spider Demon was a member of the Spider Family.!~', '/uploads/images/c_139740.png'),
(131, 'Kumo Oni Ane', '蜘蛛鬼「姉」', '配角', 'Ryouko Shiraishi', 'She is a member of the spider family.', '/uploads/images/c_141690.png'),
(131, 'Kumo Oni Haha', '蜘蛛鬼「母」', '配角', 'Ami Koshimizu', 'Like most demons, she is cruel, unfeeling, and murderous towards humans. Though after much time with him, she developed fear for Rui and the Father Spider Demon who abused her for being weaker than expected. ~!She was a member of the Spider Family.!~', '/uploads/images/c_141692.png'),
(131, 'Kumo Oni Chichi', '蜘蛛鬼「父」', '配角', 'Tetsu Inada', '~!He was a member of the Spider Family.!~', '/uploads/images/c_141693.png'),
(131, 'Ukogi', 'うこぎ', '配角', 'Manaka Iwami', 'Ukogi is Zenitsu''s Kasugai Crow. He is the only sparrow to appear in the series and pass the Kasugai Crow Test and also the only Kasugai Crow without the ability to talk. His family was killed by Demons.', '/uploads/images/c_142420.jpg'),
(131, 'Naho Takada', '高田なほ', '配角', 'Yuuki Kuwahara', 'She is a servant of the Butterfly Estate.', '/uploads/images/c_145286.jpg'),
(131, 'Kiyo Terauchi', '寺内きよ', '配角', 'Nanami Yamashita', 'She is a servant of the Butterfly Estate.', '/uploads/images/c_145287.jpg'),
(131, 'Aoi Kanzaki', '神崎アオイ', '配角', 'Yuri Ehara', 'She is a Demon Slayer, though she works as a servant in the Butterfly Estate rather than taking to the front lines.', '/uploads/images/c_145288.jpg'),
(131, 'Sumi Nakahara', '中原すみ', '配角', 'Ayumi Mano', 'She is a servant of the Butterfly Estate.', '/uploads/images/c_145289.jpg'),
(131, 'Kanata Ubuyashiki', '産屋敷かなた', '配角', 'Shiori Izawa', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_153220.jpg'),
(131, 'Kotoha Hashibira', '嘴平琴葉', '配角', 'Mamiko Noto', '~!Kotoha was Inosuke''s mother!~', '/uploads/images/c_161211.png'),
(131, 'Kaigaku', '獪岳', '配角', 'Yoshimasa Hosoya', '__Height:__ 167 cm (5''6") A member of the Demon Slaying Corps, who was taught the Breath of Thunder by former Thunder Pillar, Jigoro, with fellow disciple Zenitsu.', '/uploads/images/c_165862.jpg'),
(131, 'Nichika Ubuyashiki', '産屋敷 にちか', '配角', 'Ari Ozawa', 'Nichika Ubuyashiki is one of the older daughters of Kagaya Ubuyashiki.', '/uploads/images/c_167548.png'),
(131, 'Hinaki Ubuyashiki', '産屋敷 ひなき', '配角', 'Yumiri Hanamori', 'Hinaki Ubuyashiki is one of the older daughters of Kagaya Ubuyashiki.', '/uploads/images/c_167549.png'),
(131, 'Murata', '村田', '配角', 'Kouki Miyata', 'Murata is a member of the Demon Slayer Corps.', '/uploads/images/c_171150.png'),
(131, 'Kie Kamado', '竈門葵枝', '配角', 'Houko Kuwashima', 'Kie is Tanjiro Kamado''s mother.', '/uploads/images/c_196849.png'),
(131, 'Hisa', 'ひさ', '配角', 'Ikuko Tani', 'Hisa is an old lady who welcomes Demon Slayers to rest in her house. Tanjiro Kamado and his group visit her after they fight Kyogai at the Drum House.', '/uploads/images/c_196850.png'),
(131, 'Shigeru Kamado', '竈門茂', '配角', 'Kaede Hondo', 'Shigeru was Tanjiro''s second youngest brother.', '/uploads/images/c_196851.png'),
(131, 'Takeo Kamado', '竈門竹雄', '配角', 'You Taichi', 'Takeo was Tanjiro Kamado''s first younger brother.', '/uploads/images/c_196852.png'),
(131, 'Hanako Kamado', '竈門花子', '配角', 'Konomi Kohara', 'Hanako was Tanjiro Kamado''s youngest sister.', '/uploads/images/c_196853.png'),
(131, 'Saburou', '三郎', '配角', 'Masaki Terasoma', 'Saburou is a villager from the village near Tanjiro''s home.', '/uploads/images/c_196854.png'),
(131, 'Rei Kibutsuji', 'きぶつじれい', '配角', 'Yuuko Minaguchi', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_206329.png'),
(131, 'Tanjurou Kamado', '竈門炭十郎', '配角', 'Shinichirou Miki', 'Tanjuro Kamadou was the husband of Kie Kamado and the late father of Tanjiro, Nezuko, Takeo, Hanako, Shigeru, and Rokuta. Tanjuro was a quiet, calculating, forgiving, charismatic and loving person. He had a peaceful relationship with his family and regularly lectured Tanjiro about life. While he appeared calm on the outside, he showed a decent, noble aura with a quiet perception to his surroundings. According to his son, he did not like standing out or displaying his true abilities to others. However, if his family is in danger, he would not hesitate to protect them and shows no mercy towards the enemy. ~!Despite not being a Demon Slayer and having a tragic disease that makes his body incredibly frail, Tanjuro was shown to be a phenomenally strong individual. He was born with a demon slayer mark on his forehead, had the ability to access the transparent world, and was constantly using the selfless state.!~', '/uploads/images/c_206330.png'),
(131, 'Kozo Kanamori', '鉄穴森鋼蔵', '配角', 'Eiji Takemoto', 'Kozo Kanamori is a swordsmith affiliated with the Demon Slayer Corps.', '/uploads/images/c_206331.png'),
(131, 'Rokuta Kamado', '竈門六太', '配角', 'Aoi Koga', 'Tanjiro''s youngest sibling.', '/uploads/images/c_207857.jpg'),
(131, 'Gotou', '後藤', '配角', 'Makoto Furukawa', 'Goto is a member of the Kakushi, the clean-up brigade of the Demon Slayers. He is the one who found a near-dead Tanjiro, Inosuke, and Zenitsu in the aftermath of the Entertainment District Arc. He possesses deep respect for the three because of their capability and bravery. At one point in his life, he was found worthy of being a Demon Slayer, but for unknown reasons, he decided to become one of the Kakushi.', '/uploads/images/c_207949.png'),
(131, 'Shoichi', '正一', '配角', 'Mitsuhiro Ichiki', 'Shoichi is a young boy saved by Tanjiro Kamado and Zenitsu Agatsuma when they approached him to help his older brother, Kiyoshi, escape from the Drum House. He also has a younger sister, Teruko.', '/uploads/images/c_207950.jpg'),
(131, 'Female Kakushi', '隠', '配角', '', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_207951.jpg'),
(131, 'Kibutsuji no Musume', '鬼舞辻の娘', '配角', 'Haruka Shiraishi', 'Muzan''s Daughter', '/uploads/images/c_207952.jpg'),
(131, 'Teruko', 'てる子', '配角', 'Miho Okasaki', 'Teruko is a young girl, accompanied by her brother Shoichi, who approaches Tanjiro Kamado and Zenitsu Agatsuma to help save her older brother from the Drum House.', '/uploads/images/c_207953.jpg'),
(131, 'Kiyoshi', '清', '配角', 'Shunichi Toki', 'Kiyoshi is the elder brother of Shoichi and Teruko, who gets kidnapped by the Drum House Demon, Kyogai.', '/uploads/images/c_207954.jpg'),
(131, 'Tokie', 'トキエ', '配角', 'Misako Tomioka', 'Tokie is a resident of the village the Swamp Demon attacked and his final target.', '/uploads/images/c_207955.jpg'),
(131, 'Toyo', '豊', '配角', 'Mitsuo Iwata', 'Toyo is an udon street vendor.', '/uploads/images/c_207956.jpg'),
(131, 'Tsunojou Oni', '角状鬼', '配角', 'Yoshihisa Kawahara', 'Tsunojou oni was a Demon that lived in the Drum House.', '/uploads/images/c_207957.png'),
(131, 'Kamanue', '釜鵺', '配角', 'KENN', 'Kamanue was a member of the Twelve Kizuki, having held the position of Lower Rank 6.', '/uploads/images/c_207958.png'),
(131, 'Mukago', '零余子', '配角', 'Kana Ueda', 'Mukago was a member of the Twelve Kizuki, having held the position of Lower Rank 4.', '/uploads/images/c_207959.jpg'),
(131, 'Shita Oni', '舌鬼', '配角', 'Tarusuke Shingaki', 'Shita Oni was a Demon that lived in the Drum House.', '/uploads/images/c_207960.png'),
(131, 'Rokuro', '轆轤', '配角', 'Taiten Kusunoki', 'Rokuro was a member of the Twelve Kizuki, having held the position of Lower Rank 2.', '/uploads/images/c_207961.jpg'),
(131, 'Chachamaru', '茶々丸', '配角', '', 'Chachamaru is a feline familiar that assists in Tamayo''s medical research with Demon blood. ~!Chachamaru is seen during the battle with Muzan, after the Infinity Castle collapses. The cat jumps above the remaining Hashira in order to administer an antidote to stave off the poisonous effects of Muzan''s attacks. As a result, it is sliced in half by the demon. However, it was later reassembled by Yushirou.!~', '/uploads/images/c_268212.jpg'),
(131, 'Ozaki', '尾崎', '配角', 'Hisako Toujou', 'Ozaki was a Demon Slayer and part of the Demon Slayer Corps.', '/uploads/images/c_306223.png'),
(131, 'Wakuraba', '病葉', '配角', 'Souichirou Hoshi', 'Wakuraba was a member of the Twelve Kizuki, having held the position of Lower Rank Three.', '/uploads/images/c_306224.png'),
(131, 'Satoko', '里子', '配角', '', 'Satoko was a villager betrothed to Kazumi. She was kidnapped and killed by the Swamp Demon.', '/uploads/images/c_310302.jpg'),
(131, 'Yatsu', 'やつ', '配角', 'Yoshiaki Hasegawa', 'Yatsu is a minor character of Kimetsu no Yaiba. He is a civilian that [Muzan Kibutsuji](https://anilist.co/character/129132/Muzan-Kibutsuji) bumped into at an alleyway in Asakusa.', '/uploads/images/c_310306.jpg'),
(131, 'Kazumi', '和巳', '配角', 'Koudai Sakai', 'Kazumi was a minor character in Kimetsu no Yaiba. He was a villager whose fiancée, Satoko, was kidnapped and eaten by the Swamp Demon.', '/uploads/images/c_310311.jpg'),
(132, 'Joutarou Kuujou', '空条承太郎', '配角', '', '__Height:__ 195 cm (6''5") __Occupation:__ Student, Marine Explorer, Oceanographer __Nationality:__ Japanese Joutarou is Holly Kujo''s son and [Joseph Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/6356)''s grandson. In Part 3, he has a recognizable attire of a blue trenchcoat-length school uniform jacket with yellow chains on the collar. He also wears a trademark hat which, while torn in the back, often seems to blend with his hair. When Joutarou first appears, he turned himself in to the police because he believes his Stand is an evil spirit possessing him. After he is released from jail, and learns what his Stand is, Joutarou gets used to Star Platinum -- a fierce, muscular, vaguely Aztec-looking spirit with "the precision of a machine" and the ability to destroy virtually anything with a sledgehammer barrage of fists. He has a very tough exterior, and is even rather rough and delinquent, but he also is very dedicated, intense, and loyal. He is very intelligent, but usually lets his (or Star Platinum''s) fists do the talking with the enemy, even though he often has to rely on his wits to deal with stand users'' attacks. He is also known for a quick and short temper. His catchphrase is "Yare yare daze." It generally relates of being bored or exasperation. In Part 3, he is the main target of [Dio](https://anilist.co/character/4004), who realizes that Joutarou is his greatest threat. One of the strongest stands in the JoJo universe; Star Platinum possesses super human senses, strength, sta', '/uploads/images/c_4003.png'),
(132, 'Dio Brando', 'ディオ・ブランドー', '主角', 'Takehito Koyasu', '__Height:__ 195 cm (6''5") __Race:__ Human (formerly), Vampire (onwards) __Nationality:__ British Dio is an immortal vampire and the arch rival of the Joestar clan. __Series 1: Phantom Blood__ ~!Dio is the son of [Dario Brando](https://anilist.co/character/74099/Brando-Dario), an alcoholic and abusive father. Back when Dio was just a boy, he was brought into the household of [George Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/21956/Joestar-I-George) after the mysterious death of his father, so as to repay the debt he owed Dio''s father for saving his life. But soon Dio''s personality caused trouble for George''s young son, [Jonathan Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/8087/Joestar-Jonathan). Even more of a sociopath than his father, Dio was resolute to shatter Jonathan''s spirit and take his place as the favored son, even going so far as to arrange for Jonathan''s dog [Danny](https://anilist.co/character/222601/Danny) to be burned to death. Initially, Dio is able earn the trust of the patriarch of the Joestar family through deceit (and at Jonathan''s expense). However, his plans of taking over the Joestar household were discovered by Jonathan when he discovered that not only had Dio poisoned his biological father to death, he was doing the same to his adoptive father, all to take the Joestar estate for his own. Determined not to be stopped, and understanding the potential to enjoy power over all things instead of just the Joestar estate, Dio wears and activates the Stone Mask, becoming ', '/uploads/images/c_4004.png'),
(132, 'Joseph Joestar', 'ジョセフ・ジョースター', '主角', 'Tomokazu Sugita', '__Height__: 195 cm (6''5") Joseph Joestar begins as a young Englishman in New York, with his grandmother [Erina](https://anilist.co/character/21937). However, an attack by [Straits](https://anilist.co/character/21961) and the disappearance of [Robert Edward O Speedwagon](https://anilist.co/character/21938) soon involve him in the greater chain of events.', '/uploads/images/c_6356.png'),
(132, 'Jonathan Joestar', 'ジョナサン・ジョースター', '主角', 'Kazuyuki Okitsu', '__Height:__ 195 cm __Nationality:__ British __Occupation:__ Archaeologist Born the unique son of the wealthy businessman [George Joestar I](https://anilist.co/character/21956), Jonathan is an honest, kind, and positive man whose life is fraught with tragedy after meeting his adopted older brother - and series antagonist - [Dio Brando](https://anilist.co/character/4004). In his battle against Dio, Jonathan becomes a Ripple user under the tutelage of the master [Will Anthonio Zeppeli](https://anilist.co/character/18062). **Part 5:**~!Jonathan is the biological father of [Giorno Giovanna](https://anilist.co/character/10529), the protagonist of Vento Aureo, as well as a handful of other illegitimate offspring.!~', '/uploads/images/c_8087.png'),
(132, 'Will A. Zeppeli', 'ウィル・A・ツェペリ', '配角', 'Yoku Shioya', 'Will A. Zeppeli was on a ship with a crew studying Aztec ruins when he was younger when his father put on the mask and killed everyone in the crew but his son. After this horrific event, Zeppeli travels the world in order to destroy the mask, and sees a man cure someone using the Ripple. Zeppeli is then directed to his master Tonpetty, who teaches him to use the Ripple. However, Tonpetty foresees Zeppeli''s death during his training, warning him that should he complete his training he will surely die. Zeppeli doesn''t share this fact until the fight with Tarkus, where he afterwards gives his power to Jonathan, whom he trained after the Joestar''s house burns down. His grandson is Caesar Anthonio Zeppeli.', '/uploads/images/c_18062.jpg'),
(132, 'Erina Pendleton', 'エリナ・ペンドルトン', '配角', 'Ayako Kawasumi', 'Erina is a young girl from [Jonathan Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/8087/)''s hometown. ~!She becomes his love interest then wife. She is the mother to [George Joestar II](https://anilist.co/character/130262/), and the grandmother and guardian to [Joseph Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/6356/).!~ (Source: JoJo Wikia)', '/uploads/images/c_21937.jpg'),
(132, 'Robert E. O. Speedwagon', 'ロバート・E・O・スピードワゴン', '配角', 'Youji Ueda', 'Robert E. O. Speedwagon is a major ally featured in the 1st part of JoJo''s Bizarre Adventure, Phantom Blood, and then the 2nd part, Battle Tendency. Formerly a Londoner thug residing in Ogre Street, Speedwagon befriends [Jonathan Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/8087/Joestar-Jonathan) and, despite remaining a powerless human, becomes a loyal ally to the Joestar Family during his whole life and beyond thanks to the company he''s founded: the Speedwagon Foundation. His company supports the Joestars in Stardust Crusaders, Diamond is Unbreakable, and Stone Ocean.', '/uploads/images/c_21938.jpg'),
(132, 'George Joestar I', 'ジョージ・ジョースターI世', '配角', 'Masashi Sugawara', 'George is [Jonathan Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/8087/Joestar-Jonathan)''s father and, after a tragic misunderstanding, adopts [Dio Brando](https://anilist.co/character/4004/Brando-Dio) in his family, kick-starting the events of the first six parts of the series.', '/uploads/images/c_21956.jpg'),
(132, 'Smokey Brown', 'スモーキー・ブラウン', '配角', 'Yuu Hayashi', 'A young boy living in New York. Joseph saves him from brutal, racist policemen, and he sticks around long enough to watch the battle against Straits. He also shows up at the end of Part 2 with Rudolf von Stroheim''s cavalry. Smokey is initially shown with a pigtail in Volume 5, which mysteriously disappears in the rest of the series. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_21957.jpg'),
(132, 'Rudol von Stroheim', 'ルドル・フォン・シュトロハイム', '配角', 'Atsushi Imaruoka', 'Stroheim is the commander of the Wehrmacht forces who discovered Santana in Mexico. ~!He is appropriately militaristic and menacing, but is also responsible for not only saving the life of Robert E. O. Speedwagon, but also for trying to help Joseph Joestar defeat Santana by blowing himself (and the enemy) up. He returns later as a cyborg to assist in the fight against Cars were he is sliced to pieces by Cars. He later returns again with a squad of soldiers to aid Joseph when an army of vampires tries to attack him. Later, when Joseph takes a plane to try and send Cars into a volcano, he saves him by jumping out the cockpit, breaking his legs as a direct result. He dies in 1943 in the front during the Battle of Stalingrad as a German soldier. He is the one who made Joseph''s prosthetic cyborg hand.!~ (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_21958.jpg'),
(132, 'Caesar Zeppeli', 'シーザー・アントニオ・ツェペリ', '主角', 'Takuya Satou', '__Height:__ 186 cm The grandson of [Will A. Zeppeli](https://anilist.co/character/18062/Zeppeli-Will-A). He is a blond, suave ladies'' man, as well as a skilled Ripple user. He was taught by [Lisa Lisa](https://anilist.co/character/21960/Lisa-Lisa), and currently lives in Italy. He is rather cool and collected, especially compared to [Joseph](https://anilist.co/character/6356/Joestar-Joseph), with whom he is grudgingly paired to fight the Pillar Men. But over time Joseph starts to grow on him so much he is able to understand his strange thought pattern. ~!When Caesar was young his father suddenly left with no explanation. Because of this Caesar grew up hating his father thinking he was out living a new life. One day when Caesar spots him walking he tails him with the intention of killing him. Caesar spots a jewel not knowing that it was the activation of [Wham](https://anilist.co/character/21965/Wamuu)''s trap and his father pushes him out of the way, sacrificing himself for Caesar. This leads to Caesar going ahead of the rest of the group to fight Wham, where he meets the ultimate fate, but not before doing his fair share of damage and ripping off Wham''s lip piercing, sending it in a Ripple bubble for Joseph before his body is crushed by a rock.!~', '/uploads/images/c_21959.jpg'),
(132, 'Lisa Lisa', 'リサリサ', '配角', 'Atsuko Tanaka', '__Birthday:__ ~!Dec, 1888!~ __Age:__ ~!50!~ __Height:__ 175 cm A mysterious Ripple user whom Joseph Joestar meets in Venice, Lisa Lisa reveals herself to be his friend Caesar Zeppeli''s mentor. She trains Joseph in the ways of the Ripple and joins in the fight against the Pillar Men, as a powerful Ripple user in her own right. ~!It is eventually revealed that she is Joseph''s long-lost mother, despite her youthful appearance. Her real name is Elisabeth Joestar and she is the infant Jonathan Joestar saved at the end of Phantom Blood and gave to his widow Erina to raise. She was subsequently adopted by the Ripple user Straits, and learned the art of the Ripple from him. As a young adult, Elisabeth eventually married George Joestar II, and they had one child. After George had been killed by a vampire, Elisabeth murdered her husband''s killer and burned him to ash, but he happened to be a high ranking military official. In order to avoid retaliation, the Speedwagon Foundation helped her to erase all evidence of her existence. She is gravely wounded in her one-on-one struggle with Kars, but manages to survive. She later tells Joseph her relation to him personally, at his own funeral. She eventually remarries.!~', '/uploads/images/c_21960.jpg'),
(132, 'Straits', 'ストレイツォ', '配角', 'Nobuo Tobita', 'Straits is another of Tonpetty''s followers. He aided Jonathan in the fight against Dio and his minions. He, along with Dire, were named after the band Dire Straits. ~!When Santana was discovered in the 1930s during Part 2, he betrayed Speedwagon and donned one of the newly discovered Stone Masks. He explained that he had always envied Dio''s strength and beauty and, as a result, desired to stop his aging process. He died after battling and losing to Joseph Joestar in New York City, overloading his own vampire body with Ripple energy. He is also the adoptive father of Lisa Lisa. !~ (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_21961.png'),
(132, 'Suzie Q', 'スージーＱ', '配角', 'Sachiko Kojima', '__Height:__ 168 cm The female assistant to Lisa Lisa. Suzie Q is a slightly ditzy girl who worries for her friends. Evidently this carefree personality has not diminished even in the events of Stardust Crusaders, when she is shown enthusiastically recording her sightings in Japan on a camcorder when on a trip to see her daughter. ~!She is introduced as the female assistant to Lisa Lisa. When she first appears, she is taken over by the remains of Esidisi and attacks her friends. Thanks to a combination attack by Caesar and Joseph, she is saved with only minor injury. She marries Joseph in 1939.!~', '/uploads/images/c_21962.png'),
(132, 'Santana', 'サンタナ', '配角', 'Kenji Nomura', 'He is discovered in a Mexican pyramid in 1938. He is then awakened and studied by a Nazi vampire study team in an underground base. The team, led by Major Stroheim, conducts live human experiments with the stone mask to try to strengthen the Nazi Army. The team awakens Santana in an advanced isolation room fortified with steel plates, and conduct behavioral experiments on him. They soon find that Santana feeds on vampires and is able to absorb food from the surface of his body. The team then is shocked by Santana''s escape from the isolation room. Santana breaks many of his own bones in order to squeeze himself into the 4-by-20 cm ventilation outlet of the room, and does all this at a speed faster than human eyes can perceive. The team shoots Santana with machine guns, only to find that Santana has learned their language and the mechanisms of their weapons from only minutes of contact. He then easily disposes of the Nazis who disturbed his sleep, and even manages to stay alive after being attacked, exposed to sunlight, and blown up. He is named after the long-lived rock group Santana. He is the only member of the Pillar Men to survive, and is theoretically still alive throughout all of the arcs. However, due to his vastly-improved Ripple power, it is possible that Joseph killed him after returning to America. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_21963.png'),
(132, 'ACDC', 'エシディシ', '配角', 'Keiji Fujiwara', 'ACDC is one of the Pillar Men that were discovered by Nazis in Rome. Like Wham and Cars, ACDC is very confident in his powers and abilities and see humans as inferior. However, he has a more violent temper than the others to the point that he has to cry and sob to calm himself down. He is named after Australian Hard rock band AC/DC. ~!ACDC uses "the skill of fire". He raises his body temperature in order to heat his blood to 500°C. He then extends his blood vessels out of his body and makes them into long, prehensile needles with which he injects his hot blood into enemies, dissolving them from within. Even if the blood isn''t injected directly, it can still eat through flesh and metal alike if sprayed on a target from the outside. AC/DC has been shown to have an extremely erratic temper, sobbing at the sight of his own severed arm, only to calm himself near-instantly and replace it with the arm of Loggins. He himself stated that he has a more explosive temper than either of his brethren, and claims to openly express any rage or sorrow he feels so he doesn''t lose his self-control. ACDC had traveled to ancient China and knew Sun Tzu''s theory that "all warfare is based on deception". In his battle with Joseph Joestar, he tries to intimidate him by disabling Joseph''s deceptive tactics. ACDC cuts the hidden rope through which Joseph plans to send Ripple energy to hurt him. Nevertheless, he falls for Joseph''s more sophisticated deception, for Joseph has predicted his action and emp', '/uploads/images/c_21964.png'),
(132, 'Wamuu', 'ワムウ', '配角', 'Akio Ootsuka', 'Wamuu is introduced as a servant to both Esidisi and Kars. He is a very strong and honorable warrior who possess the power of the wind, and also reflexively attacks anyone who steps on his shadow. If he goes blind, he can grow a horn on his forehead and sense sound waves with it. He can also draw air into his body and blast it through the tip of the horn, creating a highly-destructive "wind scalpel". He is also extremely honorable, stopping himself from defeating a defenseless Joseph Joestar when he said that with a month to train he could beat Wham. ~!Later on, he engaged in battle with Caesar Anthonio Zeppeli and killed him, but not before he managed to rip off Wham''s lip piercing containing the poison within Joseph. In another display of honor, Wham allowed the antidote to stay where Joseph could get it out of respect for Caesar''s valiant effort. Later challenging Wham to battle to avenge Caesar, they engaged in a deadly Roman chariot race, with Wham initially getting the upper hand. After Joseph managed to counter Wham''s wind scalpel, he was left as nothing more than a head with the Ripple energy slowly killing him. After Joseph gave Wham some of his own blood to ease his pain, he used the last of is strength to destroy a group of vampires that attempted to kill Joseph. Wham then vanished in a gust of wind, with Joseph giving an unconscious salute to him.!~ He is named after the 80s duo featuring George Michael, Wham!. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_21965.png'),
(132, 'Kars', 'カーズ', '配角', 'Kazuhiko Inoue', 'Cars is the leader of the Pillar Men. He is intelligent, ruthless, and single-minded in his dedication to obtaining the Red Stone of Aja. Strangely, despite his apathy towards humans and willingness to kill them, he has been shown to be more compassionate for other living beings. In Switzerland, he sliced a car that was about to hit a puppy in half, and later on maneuvered himself during a long fall to miss a patch of flowers near the bottom of the cliff. Cars'' power is that of light; he is able to produce bladed appendages from his arms and use these to reflect blinding light toward his enemies. He also has the same powers over his body that all the Pillar Men share. ~!When he gains the power of the stone mask, he becomes invulnerable to sunlight, and also gains some abilities on a genetic level; he can produce living creatures and control them, and can mutate his body into various forms. He outlasts his comrades and eventually does gain almost unlimited power as the ultimate "evolved" man through the Red Stone of Aja and a stone mask. In a final confrontation, he succeeds in severing Joseph''s hand but is eventually blown into space by a volcanic eruption as well as an ultimate Ripple attack from Joseph. Being immortal, he does not die; however he is unable to return to Earth after being thrown out of orbit. Trapped in the void of space for eternity, he eventually stops thinking and desires death.!~ He is named after the 80''s new wave group The Cars. (Source: Wikipedia)', '/uploads/images/c_21966.png'),
(132, 'Narrator', 'ナレーター', '配角', 'Tooru Ookawa', 'This character page is set to represent and list all narrators, which haven''t been given a visual representation of themselves in their respective work. Please add other narrator characters, which were given a visual representation of themselves, separately from this narrator page.', '/uploads/images/c_36309.jpg'),
(132, 'Dire', 'ダイアー', '配角', 'Taketora', 'Dire is a minor ally featured in Phantom Blood. Dire is a Ripple disciple under the Ripple Master Tonpetty and is a very close friend of Will Anthonio Zeppeli.', '/uploads/images/c_74057.png'),
(132, 'Tompetty', 'トンペティ', '配角', 'Tamio Ooki', 'Tonpetty is a minor ally featured in Part I: Phantom Blood. He is a Ripple master who trained Will Anthonio Zeppeli as well as Straizo and Dire.', '/uploads/images/c_74097.png'),
(132, 'Dario Brando', 'ダリオ・ブランドー', '配角', 'Tadashi Miyazawa', 'Dario is the father of [Dio Brando](https://anilist.co/character/4004/Brando-Dio). An alcoholic and abusive man, he is primarily responsible for contributing to Dio''s descent into evil. After a tragic misunderstanding, [George Joestar I](https://anilist.co/character/21956/Joestar-I-George) decides to give him a favor and adopts his son Dio into the Joestar Family.', '/uploads/images/c_74099.png'),
(132, 'Wang Chung', 'ワンチェン', '配角', 'Hiroshi Naka', 'Wang Chan is a minor antagonist featured in Part I: Phantom Blood personally as a human, Wang Chan has shown a greedy personality, selling a poison to Dio Brando without any regard for its use and heading back to the Joestar mansion to salvage for treasures and antiques. Upon becoming a vampire, however, he becomes entirely devoted to Dio''s wishes. Synopsis Originally only known as the "Oriental Man", he owned a curiosity shop on Ogre Street. Wang Chang sold Dio the poison which Dio used in his murder of Dario Brando and his attempted murder of George Joestar, although Wang was not concerned with what the poison was to be used for. He told Dio, without much, if any, intent to provoke him, of a man in his own land who had a similar birthmark to Dio''s who had had a harsh life, but in the end lived to be over 183. Sometime after, he was was captured by Jonathan Joestar and taken to the the Joestar Manor. When he is used in an attempt to force Dio to go with the police, he again mentions his fortune telling, saying that Dio is far too lucky to fully have to give up this early. Dio uses George''s blood to become a vampire, taking Wang Chan as his subordinate when the latter goes to search the Joestar manor for valuables. Dio trusts him enough to be responsible for his head and implanting it onto Jonathan''s body. This did not go according to plan, however as Jonathan use the last of his strength to crush Wang Chan''s head and sent a ripple to take control of his body, and made him si', '/uploads/images/c_74101.png'),
(132, 'Jack', '切り裂きジャック', '配角', 'Naomi Kusumi', 'Jack is a serial killer who meets Dio Brando and is transformed into a Zombie sent to fight the Joestar Group. He was inspired by the historical figure of the same name. (Source: JoJo Wikia)', '/uploads/images/c_74105.png'),
(132, 'Tarkus', 'タルカス', '配角', 'Tetsu Inada', 'Tarkus the "Dark Knight" was a knight from 16th Century Great Britain who was executed after losing a war. Resurrected as a Zombie by Dio Brando, he is wholeheartedly loyal to his new master and fights the Joestar Group. (Source: JoJo Wikia)', '/uploads/images/c_74109.png'),
(132, 'Bruford', 'ブラフォード', '配角', 'Kenjirou Tsuda', 'Bruford is an antagonist featured in Part I: Phantom Blood. He is a vampire made from the centuries-old corpse of a brave and powerful warrior of ancient Britain. Along with Tarkus, Bruford was one of "The Dark Knights". He also had unusual battle prowess and powers associated with his dark hair. ~!Bruford and Tarkus were successful in the Challenge of the 77 in 1563, two of only five challengers to succeed in history. Prior to their corruption, Bruford and Tarkus were members of the Tudor Dynasty and retainers of Mary Stuart. Eventually they were beheaded for supporting Mary against her political rival, Elizabeth. However, Elizabeth''s deception to force them to surrender led to a strong sense of betrayal that made them susceptible to manipulation by Dio.!~ ~!The pair were eventually resurrected as vampires by Dio Brando to oppose Jonathan Joestar, Will A. Zeppeli, and Robert Speedwagon. Bruford''s manipulation of his hair poses much challenge to Jonathan, eventually leading to them fighting underwater, until Jonathan swims downward to find air bubbles beneath the rocks, enabling him to draw breath and hit Bruford with a ripple overdrive. Moments before he disintegrates from the ripple, Bruford gives Jonathan his sword, Luck and Pluck. However, his corpse is kicked aside by a wrathful Tarkus, who attempts to finish off Jonathan and party on his own.!~', '/uploads/images/c_74113.png'),
(132, 'Holly Kuujou', '空条ホリィ       ', '配角', '', 'Holly Kuujou née Joestar is the daughter of [Joseph Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/6356/) and mother of [Joutarou Kuujou](https://anilist.co/character/4003/).', '/uploads/images/c_129824.png'),
(132, 'Mary Joestar', 'メアリー・ジョースタ', '配角', '', 'Mary Joestar is the late mother of Jonathan Joestar and wife of George Joestar. Never shown in person in the series, the only thing known about her story is that she accompanied her husband during a trip to London and died protecting her baby when her carriage had an accident and fell into a ravine. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130250.png'),
(132, 'Tattoo', '刺青', '配角', 'Hiroaki Tajiri', 'Tattoo is a rugged looking grown man with a medium sized beard and unkempt hair. His wardrobe consists mainly of a fringed leather jacket, pants, and belt. His most noticeable feature, and the obvious source of his name, is a large tattoo stretching from cheek to cheek and from forehead to nose dorsum - the tattoo appears to be either a butterfly or a design similar to a Rorschach test image. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130251.png'),
(132, 'Doobie', 'ドゥービー', '配角', 'Yuuichi Ishigami', 'Doobie is a minor antagonist featured in Phantom Blood. He is a musclebound masked zombie that Dio Brando sics on Poco''s Sister after she refuses to serve him. Doobie grabs the girl and rips her dress in an attempt to assault her, but his plan is quickly ruined by an anvil thrown by Jonathan Joestar. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130252.png'),
(132, 'Poco', 'ポコ', '配角', 'Yumiko Kobayashi', 'Poco was a cowardly boy who got bullied by other kids, but was protected by his sister. When confronted by her about when he was going to fight back and live on his own, Poco answered that he would do this "tomorrow", which causes her to slap him. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130253.png'),
(132, 'Donovan', 'ドノヴァン', '配角', 'Kenichirou Matsuda', 'Donovan is a mature athletic man whose dark hair is slicked back. His skin is colored differently around his eyes, starting from a wide area on his hairline and converging to the side of the root of his nose. Donovan wears a sleeveless officer outfit. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130259.png'),
(132, 'Mario Zeppeli', 'マリオ ・ ツェペリ', '配角', 'Jin Yamanoi', 'Mario Zeppeli is characterized as hard-working, trustworthy, and a wholesome family man. Although he loved his family, Mario had to abandon them in order to investigate the Pillar Men. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130260.png'),
(132, 'Loggins', 'ロギンズ', '配角', 'Yutaka Nakano', 'Loggins is a tall, muscular man with chiseled features and somewhat glazed eyes. He wears a tunic, an over-sized fez, and armbands. Loggins displays a very demanding demeanor when instructing Joseph and Caesar, often forcing them to do tough trials during their Ripple training. Despite this, he seems to have, along with Messina, a sense of humor as the two would often tease their disciples. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130261.png'),
(132, 'George II Joestar', 'ジョージ・ジョースター 2世', '配角', '', 'George resembles his father Jonathan and his son Joseph. He is only seen wearing a military dress uniform. Assumed to be a capable fighter pilot, George was one of the first to fly an aircraft during World War I. It''s hinted that he may have had a talent for the Ripple much like his father and son, though he was never given any training to properly use it. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130262.png'),
(132, 'Messina', 'メッシーナ', '配角', 'Hidetoshi Nakamura', 'Messina is a tall muscular man with short hair tied into a ponytail and a Fu Manchu mustache. He wears a long hat, a sleeveless tunic, and armbands. Though much of Messina''s personality isn''t focused upon, he displays the characteristics of a stern, yet effective instructor to Joseph and Caesar. Despite this, Messina seems to have a sense of humor as he, along with Loggins, would often tease his disciples during their training. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia)', '/uploads/images/c_130263.png'),
(132, 'Poco no Ane', 'ポコの姉', '配角', 'Aya Endou', 'She''s the older sister of Poco and was held captive in the castle by Dio', '/uploads/images/c_154086.png'),
(132, 'Styx', 'スティクス', '配角', 'Masayuki Katou', 'An alcoholic priest who discovers Dio''s coffin in the boat Jonathan and Erina board.', '/uploads/images/c_222600.png'),
(132, 'Danny', 'ダニー', '配角', '', 'Minor character appearing in Phantom Blood. He is [Jonathan Joestar](https://anilist.co/character/8087/Joestar-Jonathan)''s dog and childhood best friend. [George Joestar I](https://anilist.co/character/21956/Joestar-I-George) bought Danny when he was a puppy when Jonathan was five years old. Danny was very afraid of unfamiliar places and strange people causing him to bite Jonathan when the young boy first approached him. For a while, Jonathan also antagonized Danny by throwing stones at him. One day, while swimming in a river, Jonathan started drowning and was saved by Danny, which made them the best of friends. ~!Danny''s death at the hands of [Dio Brando](https://anilist.co/character/4004/Brando-Dio) serves as one of the primary catalysts in the lifelong rivalry between Jonathan and Dio.!~', '/uploads/images/c_222601.png'),
(132, 'Mark', 'マルク', '配角', 'Ryouta Oosaka', 'Mark is a German soldier and a friend of Caesar Zeppeli who participated in the effort for stopping the Pillar Men''s awakening.', '/uploads/images/c_232362.png'),
(132, 'Kisha', '記者', '配角', 'Seiko Yoshida', 'She arrives at the cafe where Joseph and Straizo are fighting and begins to take photos, saying it would reach the front page of the newspaper. Straizo catches her off guard and uses her as a hostage to approach Joseph, vowing to kill her if the Joestar runs off. Though Joseph attempts to bluff his way out by calling her a "floozie" he won''t risk his life to save, Straizo forces Joseph to fight him when he rips the reporter''s tooth out. After being saved, the reporter punches Joseph for insulting her and then kicks him in the knee. The adrenaline from the ordeal then wears off and she screams from the delayed pain of losing her tooth. This content comes from JoJo''s Bizarre Encyclopedia (https://jojowiki.com), and must be attributed to its authors, as specified in the license. JoJo''s Bizarre Wiki (the FANDOM wiki) is prohibited from using it, for repeatedly copying without giving attribution.', '/uploads/images/c_232365.png'),
(132, 'Chuugoku Kenpouka', '中国拳法家', '配角', 'Itaru Yamamoto', 'He originally tries to rob Jonathan Joestar in Ogre Street alongside Robert E. O. Speedwagon and Tattoo', '/uploads/images/c_233084.png'),
(132, 'Elizabeth I', 'エリザベスⅠ世', '配角', 'Yuka Keichou', 'Elizabeth I is a queen of England and a monarch from the Tudor dynasty. In 1565, she battles her first cousin once removed, Mary Stuart, over the throne. Her betrayal of Bruford and Tarkus, two retainers of Mary, led to the two knights cursing humanity; Dio Brando uses this resentment to his advantage over three hundred years later when he revives them as zombies. (Source: JoJo''s Bizarre Adventure Wiki)', '/uploads/images/c_243876.png'),
(132, 'Shitsuji', '執事', '配角', 'Shinobu Matsumoto', 'A butler of the Joestar Family.', '/uploads/images/c_243880.png'),
(132, 'Wired Beck', '鋼線のベック', '配角', 'Satoshi Tsuruoka', 'He is a Vampire created by Kars tasked with guarding the hotel Kars is hiding in and briefly battles Lisa Lisa.', '/uploads/images/c_243882.png'),
(132, 'Adams', 'アダムス', '配角', 'Hidenori Takahashi', 'Adams is a former human and villager from Windknight''s Lot who becomes a Zombie created by Dio Brando.', '/uploads/images/c_243884.png'),
(132, 'Shikai', '司会', '配角', 'Eiji Takeuchi', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389583.jpg'),
(132, 'Shounen B', '少年B', '配角', 'Ryouta Asari', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389584.jpg'),
(132, 'Yaji B', 'ヤジB', '配角', 'Takahiro Miwa', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389585.jpg'),
(132, 'Otoko', '男', '配角', 'Taira Kikumoto', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389586.jpg'),
(132, 'Kankyaku', '観客', '配角', 'Shinobu Matsumoto', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389587.jpg'),
(132, 'Onna', '女', '配角', 'Keiko Watanabe', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389588.jpg'),
(132, 'Yaji A', 'ヤジA', '配角', 'Yuusuke Kuwahata', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389589.jpg'),
(132, 'Shounen A', '少年A', '配角', 'Yoshitsugu Matsuoka', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_389590.jpg'),
(133, 'Ichika Nakano', '中野一花', '主角', 'Kana Hanazawa', '__Height__: 159 cm (5''2") First sister of the Nakano Quintuplets. Despite the negligible age difference among them, she took the role of the eldest sister properly. She is also trusted enough to act as their confidant and leader. Ichika aspires to become an actress. She likes to tease [Fuutarou](https://anilist.co/character/128063).', '/uploads/images/c_126371.jpg'),
(133, 'Nino Nakano', '中野二乃', '主角', 'Ayana Taketatsu', '**Height:** 159 cm (5''2") Second sister of the Nakano quintuplets. She usually acts as the mother of the family, she cooks for them and takes care of their medical needs. Among the five sisters, she is the one who has the highest hostility towards [Fuutarou](https://anilist.co/character/128063/Uesugi-Fuutarou) and often rebels against him. Nino has a sharp tongue and talks bluntly when confronting the others, even if the other party is her sister. She has an outgoing attitude and is socially aware, resulting in her having many friends. She is a scheming person and doesn''t hesitate to use underhanded methods to achieve her goals.', '/uploads/images/c_126372.jpg'),
(133, 'Miku Nakano', '中野三玖', '主角', 'Miku Itou', '__Height:__ 159 cm (5''2") Third sister of the Nakano Quintuplets. She is a silent and reserved girl. Miku tends to have a pessimistic attitude and little confidence regarding herself. Due to [Fuutarou](https://anilist.co/character/128063/Uesugi-Fuutarou)''s influence, she''s the first among the sisters who open up to him. Miku likes Japanese History (especially Generals from Sengoku Period) and greatly influenced by their philosophies, to the point of affecting her real-life behavior.', '/uploads/images/c_126373.jpg'),
(133, 'Yotsuba Nakano', '中野四葉', '主角', 'Ayane Sakura', '**Height:** 159 cm (5''2") She is the fourth sister of the Nakano Quintuplets, and one of the main characters of the Quintessential Quintuplets series. Having a cheerful and energetic personality, she has a strong tendency of helping people out. Yotsuba is an active and easygoing girl. She is a type of person who can''t say no to people who need help. She is also very physically fit, and is capable of tasks that her sisters can not do. She has excellent endurance and is great at sports. She''s the only sister with excellent eyesight. She has a good sense of smell and a green thumb. Though she''s great at physical activities, she has the lowest score out of all of her sisters. Yotsuba is the only sister who accepts [Fuutarou](https://anilist.co/character/128063) since the beginning and wholeheartedly supports him in everything.', '/uploads/images/c_126374.jpg'),
(133, 'Itsuki Nakano', '中野五月', '主角', 'Inori Minase', '**Height:** 159 cm (5''2") Fifth sister of the Nakano Quintuplets. Itsuki is a serious and earnest girl. Her speech is formal and polite. She is also someone who can''t be honest with herself and having difficulty to be more straightforward. Among the sisters, Itsuki is the most familiar with [Uesugi](https://anilist.co/character/128063)''s family members and circumstances. Note: Based on the character file in volume 14, Itsuki’s actual birthday is on May 6th as she was born at midnight. She celebrates her birthday on May 5th and prevents others from looking into it too deeply.', '/uploads/images/c_126375.jpg'),
(133, 'Fuutarou Uesugi', '上杉風太郎', '主角', 'Yoshitsugu Matsuoka', '__Height:__ 178 cm (5''10'''') Fuutarou is the main protagonist of the 5-toubun no Hanayome series. He is a student of the Asahiyama High School. He lives with his father, Isanari Uesugi, and younger sister, Raiha Uesugi, in a small apartment. He is a serious and hardworking high school student and a prodigy at the top of his grade. Because of his family''s perpetual poverty, he takes up the offer to tutor the Nakano quintuplets. Fuutarou is noted to have a big ego and high confidence. He is straightforward, tactless, and rude; but is actually capable of holding back his emotions. Despite that, Fuutarou could momentarily lose his composure when agitated and faced with unfavorable circumstances. He also initially did not like getting involved with other people''s problems, finding them to be troublesome. Despite his tactlessness and crudeness, he is knowledgeable enough in knowing what to say in specific situations when thrown at him; rarely giving up when trying to achieve a specific objective. Despite his egotistical nature, Fuutarou is very hardworking and has a very high amount of patience; especially when getting the attention of the quintuplets and tutoring them despite various amounts of failures and setbacks. He later on shows a sense of duty strong enough to help the quintuplets in their studies despite them not paying him immediately, even though the money that came with tutoring was the initial reason he accepted the job. He also begins valuing their relationship to the ', '/uploads/images/c_128063.jpg'),
(133, 'Isanari Uesugi', '上杉勇也', '配角', 'Satoshi Hino', 'Father of [Fuutarou](https://anilist.co/character/128063/Fuutarou-Uesugi) and [Raiha](https://anilist.co/character/130111/Raiha-Uesugi).', '/uploads/images/c_130110.jpg'),
(133, 'Raiha Uesugi', '上杉らいは', '配角', 'Natsumi Takamori', 'Fuutarou''s cheerful younger sister. Being the only female and the most family-conscious she is effectively the head of the small household. Her cute facial expressions will often sway others'' hearts. Appreciating the hard work Fuutarou does for their family, she sometimes delays the supper until his late return home so she can prepare his favourite meal.', '/uploads/images/c_130111.jpg'),
(133, 'Maruo Nakano', '中野マルオ', '配角', 'Takaya Kuroda', 'Stepfather of the Nakano Quintuplets after their mother remarried, several years before the series begins. He runs a large hospital and is also a doctor.', '/uploads/images/c_135383.jpg'),
(133, 'Maeda', '前田', '配角', 'Hayato Itou', 'Student of the Asahiyama High School. Before the school camping trip, Maeda asked Ichika Nakano to see him in a class where he would ask her to dance with him at the bonfire dance. ~!This came out as a failure. Later he went with another girl at the bonfire dance. Five years later, the pair showed up at Fuutarou''s wedding, already married and she is pregnant.!~', '/uploads/images/c_157144.jpg'),
(133, 'Hongo', 'ホンゴー', '配角', 'Aina Suzuki', 'She is the captain of the Basketball Club. Yotsuba would constantly assist the the Club, Due to her inability to say no. Hongo would even ask her if she wanted to join the club, to which Yotsuba refuses.', '/uploads/images/c_157158.jpg'),
(133, 'Oda', '織田', '配角', 'Ryouta Akazawa', 'Oda is a film producer of the Oda Talent Productions and Ichika Nakano''s manager. He is the single father of Kiku.', '/uploads/images/c_157161.jpg'),
(133, 'Tosho Iin', '図書委員', '配角', 'Rika Kinugawa', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_181588.png'),
(133, 'Matsui', '松井', '配角', 'Aya Uchida', 'A student at the Asahiyama High School. She danced with [Maeda](https://anilist.co/character/157144/Maeda) at the bonfire during the school field trip.', '/uploads/images/c_231825.png'),
(133, 'Yamada', '山田', '配角', 'Hisako Toujou', 'She is a student of the Asahiyama High School and friend of [Nino Nakano](https://anilist.co/character/126372/).', '/uploads/images/c_242709.jpg'),
(133, 'Yamauchi', '山内', '配角', 'Yuuta Aoki', 'He is a male student at the Asahiyama High School and a classmate of [Nino Nakano](https://anilist.co/character/126372/) during her second year.', '/uploads/images/c_242710.png'),
(133, 'Yotsuba no Tannin', '四葉の担任', '配角', 'Shinya Takahashi', 'He teaches History. He was also the homeroom teacher of [Yotsuba Nakano](https://anilist.co/character/126374/)''s sophomore class, class 2-2.', '/uploads/images/c_242711.jpg'),
(133, 'Gakushoku no Oba-chan', '学食のおばちゃん', '配角', 'Matsuri Mizuguchi', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_256741.jpg'),
(133, 'Tannin Kyoushi', '担任教師', '配角', 'Kouji Seki', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_256742.jpg'),
(133, 'Tenshu', '店主', '配角', 'Naoto Kobayashi', 'A shopkeeper from the firework festival.', '/uploads/images/c_256743.jpg'),
(133, 'Sensei', '先生', '配角', 'Kouji Seki', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_256744.jpg'),
(133, 'Taiiku Kyoushi', '体育教師', '配角', 'Ryou Sugisaki', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_256745.jpg'),
(133, 'Danshi Seito', '男子生徒', '配角', 'Shunichi Toki', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_256746.jpg'),
(133, 'Shachou', '社長', '配角', 'Ryouta Akazawa', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_256747.jpg'),
(133, 'Basket-bu Buchou', 'バスケ部部長', '配角', 'Aina Suzuki', 'Basketball club captain of the basketball club at Asahi High School.', '/uploads/images/c_256748.jpg'),
(133, 'Shinsain', '審査員', '配角', 'Takaaki Torashima', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_256749.jpg'),
(133, 'Joshi', '女子', '配角', 'Mao Ichimichi', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_256750.jpg'),
(133, 'Ootori', '大鳥', '配角', 'Kaoru Sakura', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_256755.png'),
(133, 'Kyoushi', '教師', '配角', 'Hiromichi Tezuka', NULL, '/uploads/images/c_256756.jpg'),
